{"level":30,"time":1776368674656,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gf5DBHpMaaNGKy5g3gf4cG","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: notes — Notes related to tree preservation calculations.\n     4→\n     5→NOTES:\n     6→1. CHINABERRY AND BRADFORD PEAR ARE INVASIVE TREES AND REQUIRE NO MITIGATION.\n     7→2. ASH TREES REQUIRE NO MITIGATION DUE TO EMERALD ASH BORER.\n     8→\n     9→## Block 3: notes — Notes on special construction techniques.\n    10→\n    11→SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\n    12→ECM 3.5.4 (D)\n    13→1. PRIOR TO EXCAVATION WITHIN TREE DRIP LINES OR THE REMOVAL OF\n    14→TREES ADJACENT TO OTHER TREES THAT ARE TO REMAIN, MAKE A\n    15→CLEAN CUT BETWEEN THE DISTURBED AND UNDISTURBED ROOT ZONES\n    16→WITH A ROCK SAW OR SIMILAR EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    17→2. IN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS THAT CANNOT BE PROTECTED DURING\n    18→CONSTRUCTION WITH FENCING AND WHERE HEAVY VEHICULAR TRAFFIC\n    19→IS ANTICIPATED, COVER THOSE AREAS WITH A MINIMUM OF 12 INCHES OF\n    20→ORGANIC MULCH TO MINIMIZE SOIL COMPACTION. IN AREAS WITH HIGH\n    21→SOIL PLASTICITY GEOTEXTILE FABRIC, PER STANDARD SPECIFICATION\n    22→620S, SHOULD BE PLACED UNDER THE MULCH TO PREVENT EXCESSIVE\n    23→MIXING OF THE SOIL AND MULCH. ADDITIONALLY, MATERIAL SUCH AS\n    24→PLYWOOD AND METAL SHEETS, COULD BE REQUIRED BY THE CITY\n    25→ARBORIST TO MINIMIZE ROOT IMPACTS FROM HEAVY EQUIPMENT.\n    26→3. ONCE THE PROJECT IS COMPLETED, ALL MATERIALS SHOULD BE\n    27→REMOVED, AND THE MULCH SHOULD BE REDUCED TO A DEPTH OF 3\n    28→INCHES. PERFORM ALL GRADING WITHIN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS BY\n    29→HAND OR WITH SMALL EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    30→4. WATER ALL TREES MOST HEAVILY IMPACTED BY CONSTRUCTION\n    31→ACTIVITIES DEEPLY ONCE A WEEK DURING ACCUMULATION OF THE\n    32→LEAVES.\n    33→5. WHEN INSTALLING CONCRETE ADJACENT TO THE ROOT ZONE OF A TREE,\n    34→USE A PLASTIC VAPOR BARRIER BEHIND THE CONCRETE TO PROHIBIT\n    35→LEACHING OF LIME INTO THE SOIL.\n    36→\n    37→## Block 5: notes — Plant list section heading.\n    38→\n    39→PLANT LIST\n    40→\n    41→## Block 6: notes — Notes related to the plant list.\n    42→\n    43→NOTES:\n    44→1. THE CONTRACTORS (GENERAL AND SUBCONTRACTORS) SHALL PROVIDE UNIT COSTS FOR ALL\n    45→SOFTSCAPE AND HARDSCAPE MATERIAL SPECIFIED ON THE DRAWINGS AND SPECIFICATIONS. UNIT\n    46→COSTS SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR MATERIALS AND INSTALLATION SEPARATELY. UNIT COSTS SHALL\n    47→BE: 'EACH' FOR PLANT MATERIAL, 'SQUARE FOOT' OR 'SQUARE YARD' FOR PAVEMENTS, LINEAR FOOT\n    48→FOR WALL AND FENCE, 'EACH' FOR SITE FURNISHINGS AND SITE AMENITIES, 'CUBIC YARD' OR 'CUBIC\n    49→FOOT' FOR SOIL, MULCH AND OTHER BULK PRODUCTS AND 'EACH' OR 'LUMP SUM' FOR\n    50→MISCELLANEOUS ITEMS. THE UNIT COST SHALL BE FORMATTED TO HAVE COLUMNS FOR; ITEMS, UNIT,\n    51→UNIT COST, TOTAL ITEM COST.\n    52→2. PLANT QUANTITIES ARE PROVIDED FOR OWNER CONVENIENCE ONLY. CONTRACTOR IS\n    53→RESPONSIBLE FOR VERIFYING AND PROVIDING PLANT QUANTITIES SHOWN ON THE LANDSCAPE PLAN.\n    54→3. CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR LOCATING AND SECURING TREE AND PLANT MATERIAL IN\n    55→ADVANCE. BECAUSE OF THE LONG LEAD TIME ON THIS INSTALLATION AND THE RECENT SHORTAGE\n    56→ON TREE CROP, CONTRACTOR SHALL RESERVE OR CONTRACT GROW TREES WITH A GROWER.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 11: table — Header for City of Austin Tree Preservation Calculations.\n    59→\n    60→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    61→TREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS:\n    62→\n    63→## Block 12: table — Calculations related to tree preservation.\n    64→\n    65→EXISTING TREES:\n    66→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 212 INCHES\n    67→(HERITAGE)\n    68→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n    69→(NON HERITAGE)\n    70→19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES 99 INCHES\n    71→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES 295 INCHES\n    72→19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES 0 INCHES\n    73→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES 66 INCHES\n    74→\n    75→TREES REMOVED\n    76→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 27 INCHES\n    77→(HERITAGE):\n    78→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n    79→(NON HERITAGE):\n    80→19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 79 INCHES\n    81→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 134 INCHES\n    82→19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES: 0 INCHES\n    83→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES: 66 INCHES\n    84→TOTAL: 288 INCHES\n    85→\n    86→REPLACEMENT INCHES REQUIRED\n    87→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 40.5 INCHES\n    88→(HERITAGE): 300%\n    89→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n    90→(NON HERITAGE): 100%\n    91→19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 100% 79 INCHES\n    92→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 50% 82 INCHES\n    93→19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES: 50% 0 INCHES\n    94→8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES: 25% 15.5 INCHES\n    95→TOTAL: 217 INCHES\n    96→\n    97→URBAN FORESTRY INFORMATION\n    98→TOTAL APP F TREE INCHES SURVEYED 606 INCHES\n    99→TOTAL APP F TREE INCHES REMOVED 240 INCHES\n   100→TOTAL INVASIVE TREE INCHES REMOVED 137 INCHES\n   101→\n   102→TOTAL MITIGATION INCHES PLANTED ON SITE 55 INCHES\n   103→REMAINING MITIGATION INCHES REQUIRED 162 INCHES\n   104→\n   105→MITIGATION DEFICIT (REPLACE REMAINING AT $32,400\n   106→STANDARD $200 PER INCH)\n   107→HB7 MITIGATION CREDIT (55x50%x$200) $5,500\n   108→AMOUNT TO BE PAID INTO FUND $26,900\n   109→\n   110→## Block 13: table — Table listing shade trees.\n   111→\n   112→SHADE TREES\n   113→\n   114→| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n   115→|---|---|---|---|\n   116→| [circle with dot] | | EXISTING TREE, TO BE PERSERVED | |\n   117→| [circle with cross] | 2 | LIVE OAK, QUERCUS VIRGINIANA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n   118→| [circle with hash] | 10 | CEDAR ELM, ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n   119→\n   120→## Block 14: table — Chart detailing required trees.\n   121→\n   122→COA REQUIRED TREES CHART\n   123→| | NUMBER OF TREES | INCHES OF TREES |\n   124→|---|---|---|\n   125→| STREETYARD | 5 TREES @ 1.5\" | 7.5 |\n   126→| BUFFER | 0 LARGE TREES @ 4\" | 0 |\n   127→| | 1 SMALL TREES @ 2.5\" | 2.5 |\n   128→| PARKING LOT | 2 TREES @ 1.5\" | 3 |\n   129→| | Total tree inches required | A = 13 |\n   130→\n   131→PROPOSED\n   132→| PER PLANT LIST | 12 @ 4\" | B = 68 |\n   133→| | 8 @ 2.5\" | |\n   134→\n   135→PROPOSED TREE INCHES THAT MAY BE COUNTED FOR MITIGATION\n   136→| | B-A = C | C = 55 |\n   137→\n   138→* Every required tree must be at least 1.5 caliper inches.\n   139→\n   140→## Block 15: table — Calculations related to landscaping.\n   141→\n   142→CITY OF AUSTIN\n   143→LANDSCAPE CALCULATIONS:\n   144→\n   145→STREET YARD AREA:\n   146→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   147→|---|---|---|\n   148→| TOTAL SITE AREA | N/A | 94,203 SF |\n   149→| TOTAL STREET-YARD AREA | N/A | 6,314 SF |\n   150→| STREET-YARD / LANDSCAPE (20%) | 1,263 SF | 5,206 SF |\n   151→\n   152→STREET YARD TREES:\n   153→EXISTING TREES CREDIT\n   154→| | | |\n   155→|---|---|---|\n   156→| 2\" DIAMETER TO 6\" DIAMETER | 0 | |\n   157→| 6\" DIAMETER OR GREATER | 4 | |\n   158→\n   159→EXISTING TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n   160→|---|---|\n   161→| | 8 CREDITS |\n   162→\n   163→PROPOSED TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n   164→|---|---|\n   165→| | 0 CREDITS |\n   166→\n   167→TOTAL STREET YARD TREES, EXISTING TREES CREDIT PLUS PROPOSED TREES CREDIT:\n   168→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   169→|---|---|---|\n   170→| | 5 | 8 |\n   171→\n   172→LANDSCAPE IN PARKING LOTS:\n   173→90SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN SY\n   174→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   175→|---|---|---|\n   176→| | 0 | 0 |\n   177→\n   178→60SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN NON SY\n   179→| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n   180→|---|---|---|\n   181→| | 60 | 816 |\n   182→\n   183→LANDSCAPE ISLAND MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE, 8' MIN. INSIDE WIDTH\n   184→1 TREE MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE\n   185→\n   186→BUFFERING POINTS FOR DRIVE AISLE:\n   187→| | SIZE | QTY | PREFERRED | OTHER | PROVIDED |\n   188→|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   189→| LARGE TREE | 4\" | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n   190→| SMALL TREE | 2.5\" | 1 | YES | | 9 |\n   191→| MEDIUM SHRUB | 5 GAL. | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n   192→| LARGE SHRUB | 7 GAL. | 16 | YES | | 48 |\n   193→\n   194→BUFFER POINTS REQUIRED: 40\n   195→BUFFER POINTS PROVIDED: 57\n   196→\n   197→PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE & PEDESTRIAN AMENITIES: SUB CHAPTER E\n   198→REQUIRED (5% OF SITE AREA) (5% X 94,293) 4,715 SF\n   199→PROVIDED 5,855 SF\n   200→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df64853a-4f90-499d-b38e-749986aed001","uuid":"cec441fb-1deb-4555-9e62-3f9c0993af71","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-35/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 35 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: notes — Notes related to tree preservation calculations.\n\nNOTES:\n1. CHINABERRY AND BRADFORD PEAR ARE INVASIVE TREES AND REQUIRE NO MITIGATION.\n2. ASH TREES REQUIRE NO MITIGATION DUE TO EMERALD ASH BORER.\n\n## Block 3: notes — Notes on special construction techniques.\n\nSPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\nECM 3.5.4 (D)\n1. PRIOR TO EXCAVATION WITHIN TREE DRIP LINES OR THE REMOVAL OF\nTREES ADJACENT TO OTHER TREES THAT ARE TO REMAIN, MAKE A\nCLEAN CUT BETWEEN THE DISTURBED AND UNDISTURBED ROOT ZONES\nWITH A ROCK SAW OR SIMILAR EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n2. IN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS THAT CANNOT BE PROTECTED DURING\nCONSTRUCTION WITH FENCING AND WHERE HEAVY VEHICULAR TRAFFIC\nIS ANTICIPATED, COVER THOSE AREAS WITH A MINIMUM OF 12 INCHES OF\nORGANIC MULCH TO MINIMIZE SOIL COMPACTION. IN AREAS WITH HIGH\nSOIL PLASTICITY GEOTEXTILE FABRIC, PER STANDARD SPECIFICATION\n620S, SHOULD BE PLACED UNDER THE MULCH TO PREVENT EXCESSIVE\nMIXING OF THE SOIL AND MULCH. ADDITIONALLY, MATERIAL SUCH AS\nPLYWOOD AND METAL SHEETS, COULD BE REQUIRED BY THE CITY\nARBORIST TO MINIMIZE ROOT IMPACTS FROM HEAVY EQUIPMENT.\n3. ONCE THE PROJECT IS COMPLETED, ALL MATERIALS SHOULD BE\nREMOVED, AND THE MULCH SHOULD BE REDUCED TO A DEPTH OF 3\nINCHES. PERFORM ALL GRADING WITHIN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS BY\nHAND OR WITH SMALL EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n4. WATER ALL TREES MOST HEAVILY IMPACTED BY CONSTRUCTION\nACTIVITIES DEEPLY ONCE A WEEK DURING ACCUMULATION OF THE\nLEAVES.\n5. WHEN INSTALLING CONCRETE ADJACENT TO THE ROOT ZONE OF A TREE,\nUSE A PLASTIC VAPOR BARRIER BEHIND THE CONCRETE TO PROHIBIT\nLEACHING OF LIME INTO THE SOIL.\n\n## Block 5: notes — Plant list section heading.\n\nPLANT LIST\n\n## Block 6: notes — Notes related to the plant list.\n\nNOTES:\n1. THE CONTRACTORS (GENERAL AND SUBCONTRACTORS) SHALL PROVIDE UNIT COSTS FOR ALL\nSOFTSCAPE AND HARDSCAPE MATERIAL SPECIFIED ON THE DRAWINGS AND SPECIFICATIONS. UNIT\nCOSTS SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR MATERIALS AND INSTALLATION SEPARATELY. UNIT COSTS SHALL\nBE: 'EACH' FOR PLANT MATERIAL, 'SQUARE FOOT' OR 'SQUARE YARD' FOR PAVEMENTS, LINEAR FOOT\nFOR WALL AND FENCE, 'EACH' FOR SITE FURNISHINGS AND SITE AMENITIES, 'CUBIC YARD' OR 'CUBIC\nFOOT' FOR SOIL, MULCH AND OTHER BULK PRODUCTS AND 'EACH' OR 'LUMP SUM' FOR\nMISCELLANEOUS ITEMS. THE UNIT COST SHALL BE FORMATTED TO HAVE COLUMNS FOR; ITEMS, UNIT,\nUNIT COST, TOTAL ITEM COST.\n2. PLANT QUANTITIES ARE PROVIDED FOR OWNER CONVENIENCE ONLY. CONTRACTOR IS\nRESPONSIBLE FOR VERIFYING AND PROVIDING PLANT QUANTITIES SHOWN ON THE LANDSCAPE PLAN.\n3. CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR LOCATING AND SECURING TREE AND PLANT MATERIAL IN\nADVANCE. BECAUSE OF THE LONG LEAD TIME ON THIS INSTALLATION AND THE RECENT SHORTAGE\nON TREE CROP, CONTRACTOR SHALL RESERVE OR CONTRACT GROW TREES WITH A GROWER.\n\n## Block 11: table — Header for City of Austin Tree Preservation Calculations.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nTREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS:\n\n## Block 12: table — Calculations related to tree preservation.\n\nEXISTING TREES:\n24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 212 INCHES\n(HERITAGE)\n24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n(NON HERITAGE)\n19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES 99 INCHES\n8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES 295 INCHES\n19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES 0 INCHES\n8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES 66 INCHES\n\nTREES REMOVED\n24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 27 INCHES\n(HERITAGE):\n24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n(NON HERITAGE):\n19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 79 INCHES\n8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 134 INCHES\n19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES: 0 INCHES\n8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES: 66 INCHES\nTOTAL: 288 INCHES\n\nREPLACEMENT INCHES REQUIRED\n24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 40.5 INCHES\n(HERITAGE): 300%\n24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n(NON HERITAGE): 100%\n19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 100% 79 INCHES\n8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES: 50% 82 INCHES\n19 INCHES AND GREATER, ALL OTHER TREES: 50% 0 INCHES\n8 TO 18.9 INCHES, ALL OTHER TREES: 25% 15.5 INCHES\nTOTAL: 217 INCHES\n\nURBAN FORESTRY INFORMATION\nTOTAL APP F TREE INCHES SURVEYED 606 INCHES\nTOTAL APP F TREE INCHES REMOVED 240 INCHES\nTOTAL INVASIVE TREE INCHES REMOVED 137 INCHES\n\nTOTAL MITIGATION INCHES PLANTED ON SITE 55 INCHES\nREMAINING MITIGATION INCHES REQUIRED 162 INCHES\n\nMITIGATION DEFICIT (REPLACE REMAINING AT $32,400\nSTANDARD $200 PER INCH)\nHB7 MITIGATION CREDIT (55x50%x$200) $5,500\nAMOUNT TO BE PAID INTO FUND $26,900\n\n## Block 13: table — Table listing shade trees.\n\nSHADE TREES\n\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [circle with dot] | | EXISTING TREE, TO BE PERSERVED | |\n| [circle with cross] | 2 | LIVE OAK, QUERCUS VIRGINIANA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n| [circle with hash] | 10 | CEDAR ELM, ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN |\n\n## Block 14: table — Chart detailing required trees.\n\nCOA REQUIRED TREES CHART\n| | NUMBER OF TREES | INCHES OF TREES |\n|---|---|---|\n| STREETYARD | 5 TREES @ 1.5\" | 7.5 |\n| BUFFER | 0 LARGE TREES @ 4\" | 0 |\n| | 1 SMALL TREES @ 2.5\" | 2.5 |\n| PARKING LOT | 2 TREES @ 1.5\" | 3 |\n| | Total tree inches required | A = 13 |\n\nPROPOSED\n| PER PLANT LIST | 12 @ 4\" | B = 68 |\n| | 8 @ 2.5\" | |\n\nPROPOSED TREE INCHES THAT MAY BE COUNTED FOR MITIGATION\n| | B-A = C | C = 55 |\n\n* Every required tree must be at least 1.5 caliper inches.\n\n## Block 15: table — Calculations related to landscaping.\n\nCITY OF AUSTIN\nLANDSCAPE CALCULATIONS:\n\nSTREET YARD AREA:\n| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n|---|---|---|\n| TOTAL SITE AREA | N/A | 94,203 SF |\n| TOTAL STREET-YARD AREA | N/A | 6,314 SF |\n| STREET-YARD / LANDSCAPE (20%) | 1,263 SF | 5,206 SF |\n\nSTREET YARD TREES:\nEXISTING TREES CREDIT\n| | | |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2\" DIAMETER TO 6\" DIAMETER | 0 | |\n| 6\" DIAMETER OR GREATER | 4 | |\n\nEXISTING TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n|---|---|\n| | 8 CREDITS |\n\nPROPOSED TREES CREDIT | PROVIDED |\n|---|---|\n| | 0 CREDITS |\n\nTOTAL STREET YARD TREES, EXISTING TREES CREDIT PLUS PROPOSED TREES CREDIT:\n| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n|---|---|---|\n| | 5 | 8 |\n\nLANDSCAPE IN PARKING LOTS:\n90SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN SY\n| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n|---|---|---|\n| | 0 | 0 |\n\n60SF / 12 PARKING SPACES LOCATED IN NON SY\n| | REQUIRED | PROVIDED |\n|---|---|---|\n| | 60 | 816 |\n\nLANDSCAPE ISLAND MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE, 8' MIN. INSIDE WIDTH\n1 TREE MUST BE WITHIN 50' OF EACH SPACE\n\nBUFFERING POINTS FOR DRIVE AISLE:\n| | SIZE | QTY | PREFERRED | OTHER | PROVIDED |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| LARGE TREE | 4\" | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n| SMALL TREE | 2.5\" | 1 | YES | | 9 |\n| MEDIUM SHRUB | 5 GAL. | 0 | YES | | 0 |\n| LARGE SHRUB | 7 GAL. | 16 | YES | | 48 |\n\nBUFFER POINTS REQUIRED: 40\nBUFFER POINTS PROVIDED: 57\n\nPRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE & PEDESTRIAN AMENITIES: SUB CHAPTER E\nREQUIRED (5% OF SITE AREA) (5% X 94,293) 4,715 SF\nPROVIDED 5,855 SF\n","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":259}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776368674701,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NauB2pDq2grktRZcbkwNpN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n     2→\n     3→Provides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n    11→*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n    12→*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n    13→*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n    14→*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n    15→*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n    16→*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n    21→*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n    22→*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n    23→*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n    24→*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n    25→\n    26→**Plant List Schedules**\n    27→*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n    28→*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n    29→*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n    30→*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n    31→*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n    32→\n    33→**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n    34→*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n    35→*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n    36→*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n    37→*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n    38→*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n    39→\n    40→**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n    42→\n    43→---\n    44→\n    45→- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n    46→- `block-4.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n    47→- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n    48→- `block-8.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n    49→\n    50→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    51→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f35260c3-5e1a-4786-b2cb-3f3a59e76a22","uuid":"144d62ac-c596-4bfe-8204-ef5ad8eb1d27","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-35/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 35 — Landscape Calculations\n\nProvides landscape calculations, plant lists, and tree preservation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains landscape and tree preservation calculations, plant schedules, and standard municipal notes for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to demonstrate compliance with City of Austin landscape, buffering, and tree mitigation requirements, detailing exact plant species, quantities, and associated fees for tree removal.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site & Landscape Areas:** Total Site Area: 94,203 SF; Total Street-Yard Area: 6,314 SF; Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 5,206 SF (Required: 1,263 SF)\n*   **Open Space & Buffering:** Private Common Open Space Provided: 5,855 SF (Required: 4,715 SF); Buffer Points Provided: 57 (Required: 40)\n*   **Parking Lot Landscape:** Non-Street-Yard Landscape Provided: 816 SF (Required: 60 SF)\n*   **Tree Preservation & Mitigation:** Total App F Tree Inches Surveyed: 606 inches; Total App F Tree Inches Removed: 240 inches; Total Invasive Tree Inches Removed: 137 inches\n*   **Mitigation Requirements:** Total Mitigation Inches Planted on Site: 55 inches; Remaining Mitigation Inches Required: 162 inches; Amount to be Paid into Fund: $26,900\n*   **Key Plant Quantities (Minimum specs):** 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.)\n*   **Groundcover Quantities:** 92 Obedient Plant (4\" flat), 72 Frogfruit (4\" flat)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n**Calculations & Mitigation Data**\n*   **Block 14:** City of Austin Landscape Calculations. READ for required versus provided area metrics for street yards, parking lots, buffering points, and private common open space.\n*   **Blocks 11 & 17:** Tree Preservation Calculations (Heading and Table). READ for an exact breakdown of existing trees, trees removed by size/category, replacement inches required (including 300% multipliers for heritage trees), and final fee-in-lieu calculations. \n*   **Block 15:** COA Required Trees Chart. READ for street yard, buffer, and parking lot tree inch requirements (Total required: 13 inches) versus proposed inches. \n*   **Block 3:** Tree preservation notes. READ for exemptions (Chinaberry, Bradford Pear, and Ash trees require no mitigation).\n\n**Plant List Schedules**\n*   **Blocks 6 & 16:** Plant List heading and Shade Trees schedule. READ for exact shade tree species, quantities (10 Cedar Elm, 2 Live Oak), and minimum planting specifications (100 Gal., 4\" Cal.). Use VISION to see the associated plan symbols.\n*   **Block 12:** Ornamental Trees schedule. READ for species, quantities, and container specs. Use VISION to map symbols to the landscape plan.\n*   **Block 18:** Shrubs schedule. READ for shrub species, quantities, container sizes, and maximum spacing requirements. \n*   **Block 13:** Groundcovers schedule. READ for groundcover species, quantities, and spacing specifications.\n*   **Block 5:** Plant list notes. READ for contractor instructions regarding unit cost formatting, substitutions, and plant sourcing responsibilities.\n\n**Municipal Notes & Specifications**\n*   **Block 1:** Remedial Tree Care Notes. READ for aeration and supplemental nutrient requirements for trees within construction areas.\n*   **Block 2:** Special Construction Techniques (ECM 3.5.4 D). READ for specifications on rock sawing, mulch applications, and grading near critical root zones.\n*   **Block 4:** Modified & Natural Area Protection Notes. READ for fencing, wrapping, and pruning rules before, during, and after construction.\n*   **Block 7:** Site Development Permit Landscape notes. READ for requirements on protective barriers, vegetation buffering, and temporary seeding during specific dates.\n*   **Block 8:** Site Development Permit Irrigation notes. READ for TCEQ Chapter 344 compliance, water conservation rules, and final inspection deliverable requirements.\n\n**Boilerplate & Administrative**\n*   **Blocks 9, 10, 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24:** Project and sheet administrative data. READ for project name (Valley View Townhomes), owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), location (3759 Valley View Road), engineering firm (Blu Fish Collaborative), landscape architect seal, and sheet number (32 of 35).\n\n---\n\n- `block-2.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit irrigation.\n- `block-4.md` — notes: Notes related to site development permit landscape.\n- `block-7.md` — notes: Notes on remedial tree care, aeration, and supplemental nutrient requirements.\n- `block-8.md` — notes: Notes on modified and natural area protection.\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
