{"level":30,"time":1776368708277,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan and identify all transformer pads shown on the site. For each transformer pad, provide:\n1. Location (e.g., \"northeast of Building 1\", \"between Buildings 2 and 3\")\n2. Dimensions (if labeled)\n3. Proximity to buildings, parking areas, streets, or other site features\n4. Any access door orientation indicated\n5. Whether the transformers are oil-filled or dry-type (if indicated)\n6. Any callouts or notes about the transformer pads\n7. Clearances or barriers shown around the transformer pads\n8. Whether any transformers are in enclosed or niche configurations\n\nBe specific about spatial relationships and measurement references visible on the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" there are five electrical transformer pads identified on the site. \n\nHere are the details for each, addressing your specific criteria:\n\n**1. Transformer Pad West of Building 1**\n*   **Location:** West of Building 1, adjacent to Unit 101.\n*   **Dimensions:** Not labeled.\n*   **Proximity:** Located in the grassy/landscaped area between the westernmost curved entrance drive and the west facade of Building 1. It is situated just north of an \"Electrical Pull Box\" and near \"Electrical Meters\".\n*   **Access door orientation:** Not indicated.\n*   **Type (Oil-filled/Dry):** Not indicated.\n*   **Callouts/Notes:** Labeled exactly \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\" with a leader line pointing to a blue square representing the pad.\n*   **Clearances/Barriers:** No explicit clearances (e.g., dashed lines indicating safe zones) or barriers (e.g., bollards) are shown around the pad.\n*   **Enclosed/Niche:** Appears to be