{"level":30,"time":1776368715202,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a9417b2844efa3f48","tool_use_id":"toolu_015NsDFTMFyqMDpfKEpSkiAS","description":"Analyze landscape plan for electric utilities","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"I need you to retrieve and analyze the landscape plan (Sheet 31) for the Valley View Townhomes project. The site plan document ID is: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777\n\nUsing any available tools, examine Sheet 31 and determine:\n1. Are there overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this landscape plan? If yes, describe their exact location(s) on the site\n2. What is the relationship between proposed trees and any overhead electric lines? Specifically:\n   - Where are trees proposed relative to OHE lines?\n   - What are the tree species and their mature heights?\n   - Can you estimate distances from trees to OHE lines?\n3. Are utility poles shown? If so, where are they located?\n4. What utility symbol legend is shown (symbols for OHE, poles, transformers, etc.)?\n\nThe landscape plan is expected to show a site layout with buildings, parking, landscaping, and utility lines. Look for any text labels, legend items, or visual indicators of overhead electric infrastructure.\n\nThis information is critical for evaluating Austin Energy tree clearance compliance (UCM § 1.10.10.4), which prohibits trees within specified distances of overhead lines:\n- Distribution lines (< 60kV): 15 feet minimum for non-utility-compatible trees, 25 feet for large (40+ ft) trees\n- Transmission lines (60kV+): 50 feet minimum\n- Within 10 feet of any utility pole: no trees permitted\n- Within 20 feet of underground equipment: trees allowed only with root barriers","uuid":"dec4cc08-e1db-4c2d-a0f7-b60a587dd484","session_id":"df64853a-4f90-499d-b38e-749986aed001"}
