{"level":30,"time":1776368719938,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SpnULsx5wMVkCG5AQ5VXad","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n     2→\n     3→Landscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n    11→*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n    12→*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n    13→*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n    14→*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n    15→*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n    16→*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    21→    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    25→    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    26→    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n    27→\n    28→*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    29→    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    30→    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n    31→\n    32→*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    33→    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    34→    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    37→    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    38→    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n    39→\n    40→*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    41→    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    42→    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n    43→\n    44→---\n    45→\n    46→- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n    47→\n    48→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    49→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"533d2716-803a-462f-887c-92de310aeb2f","uuid":"57c562b7-096b-42db-8333-7e97dbe74f7b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-31/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 31 — Landscape Plan\n\nLandscape design plan featuring planting details and irrigation notes.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Landscape Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout of plantings, open spaces, hardscape features, and site contours. It serves as the primary reference for landscape grading, planting mitigation requirements, and automatic irrigation system specifications.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Drawing Scale:** 1\" = 20'-0\"\n*   **Topsoil Placement Depth:** Finished elevation for parking lot islands and similar areas must be at least 6 inches below the finished parking lot/curb elevation.\n*   **Irrigation Spray Limits:** No spray irrigation is permitted on areas less than 10 feet wide (e.g., medians, buffer strips).\n*   **Irrigation Setbacks:** Above-ground irrigation emission devices must be set back at least 6 inches from impervious surfaces.\n*   **Rain Shut-off Threshold:** Automatic rain shut-off devices must trigger after more than 1/2 inch (0.5\") of rainfall.\n*   **Tree Mitigation Size:** Street yard and parking lot trees exceeding 1.5 caliper inches count towards mitigation.\n*   **Site Elevations:** Topographic contour lines indicate site elevations ranging generally from approximately 660 to 690 feet.\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Landscape and Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive site plan illustrating building footprints, parking layouts, sidewalks, utility lines (Water, Storm Drain, Overhead Electric), topographical contours, and the distribution of landscape elements.\n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of the site, locate specific landscape zones (using H-series key notes), trace contour grading, and identify the placement of mitigation trees.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Key Notes & Legend**\n    Defines the hatch patterns and symbols used in the main drawing, including paving (H.1), street yards (H.2, H.3), parking lot landscaping (H.4), common open space (H.5), wooden privacy fences (H.6), and sod (H.7). It also defines abbreviations for tree types (SY, PL, P, M).\n    *READ the block content for* exact definitions of hatch patterns, symbols, and mitigation tree sizing requirements (>1.5 cal. inch) to accurately interpret the main drawing.\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Irrigation Notes**\n    Technical specifications ensuring the automatic irrigation system complies with TCEQ Chapter 344. It covers hardware requirements (master valves, rain shut-offs), spatial constraints, and deliverables required from the installer (as-built plans, water budgets).\n    *READ the block content for* specific compliance metrics, installation constraints, and administrative requirements for final plumbing inspection.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — General Landscape Notes**\n    Specific grading and soil requirements for landscaped areas adjacent to paving, detailing the necessary finished elevation offsets to accommodate topsoil placement. Also provides guidance on drought variance procedures.\n    *READ the block content for* exact grading dimensions (6 inches below finished elevation) and supplemental irrigation requirements.\n\n*   **Block 1: diagram — Scale and Orientation**\n    Provides the graphical scale and North arrow for the main drawing.\n    *READ the block content for* the exact scale (1\" = 20'-0\") and *Use VISION to* orient the site layout.\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7, 8, 9: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains the title block information, including the project name (Valley View Townhomes), location (3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX), property owner (WM 41 Austin RE, LLC), and the licensed landscape architect's professional seal (dated 02/13/2026).\n    *READ the block content for* general project context, property address, and professional certification details.\n\n---\n\n- `block-3.md` — notes: Irrigation notes detailing requirements for automatic irrigation systems to comply with TCEQ Chapter\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":49,"startLine":1,"totalLines":49}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776368720144,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01PJmSGtytENYXEX8JpE8Jai","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Daj2izML6STscZKkMhx19v","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/guide.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7260,"cache_read_input_tokens":43357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7260},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"533d2716-803a-462f-887c-92de310aeb2f","uuid":"422313b2-f50b-4182-a768-d9ef00d7cb4e"}
{"level":30,"time":1776368720186,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Daj2izML6STscZKkMhx19v","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 19 — Utility Tap Plan\n     2→\n     3→Utility tap plan showing proposed water and wastewater connections.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Utility Tap Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout and connection points for proposed water, wastewater, and storm drain lines across eight multi-family buildings. Its primary purpose is to define utility routing, drainage fixture unit (DFU) loads, pipe material specifications, and regulatory compliance notes for the site's wet utilities.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Private domestic water branches: 2\" HDPE service tubing\n    11→*   Private wastewater branches: 6\" PVC at a minimum 2.0% slope\n    12→*   Pressure reducing valve (PRV) set pressure threshold: 65 psi\n    13→*   Number of private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    14→*   Trench depth requiring geologist inspection: Greater than 5 feet\n    15→*   Drainage Fixture Units (DFUs): 4Plex = 136 DFUs, 5Plex = 170 DFUs, 6Plex = 204 DFUs\n    16→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' (NAVD 88)\n    17→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 2**: The main site plan diagram showing buildings (Bldg. 1-8), utility routing (water, wastewater, storm drain), lift stations, cleanouts, and site topography. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, pipe routing, line lengths, and specific component locations.\n    22→*   **Block 1**: Legend defining the symbols and line types used for existing and proposed utilities (W, WW, RW, E, SD) in the main diagram. Use VISION to cross-reference symbols while reviewing Block 2.\n    23→*   **Block 13**: Utility notes specifying pipe materials and slopes for private domestic water and wastewater branches. READ for exact material sizes and installation standards.\n    24→*   **Block 7**: Drainage Fixture Unit Table breaking down the total DFU loads by building number and type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex). READ for specific sanitary load calculations.\n    25→*   **Block 17**: Benchmark data providing precise elevations and descriptions of vertical control points. READ for exact elevation values used for site grading and utility slopes.\n    26→*   **Block 10**: Water tap note outlining requirements for replacing existing Asbestos Cement (AC) pipe with Ductile Iron (DI) pipe and required hazardous disposal protocols. READ for regulatory compliance regarding existing AC lines.\n    27→*   **Block 11**: Special Services Division note mandating compliance with the Austin Fire Code for the site's private fire hydrant. READ for maintenance obligations and the exact private hydrant count.\n    28→*   **Block 5**: Technical note dictating the use of factory restrained joint pipes or mechanical joint restraint devices for all water line bends, tees, and valves. READ for specific structural requirements on water mains.\n    29→*   **Block 9**: PRV Note stipulating that any structure with water pressure at or above 65 psi must install a pressure reducing valve. READ for pressure management requirements.\n    30→*   **Block 19**: Geologist inspection requirement note triggered by the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule for deep trenching. READ for the specific trench depth threshold (5 feet).\n    31→*   **Blocks 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the project title block, engineering firm details, Texas 811 logo, legal description, disclaimers regarding utility locations, and a cross-reference to the landscape plan for trees. READ for general project administration and liability disclaimers if required.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"533d2716-803a-462f-887c-92de310aeb2f","uuid":"b4a13e93-ef69-4dc7-8960-a3afdc58576c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 19 — Utility Tap Plan\n\nUtility tap plan showing proposed water and wastewater connections.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Utility Tap Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout and connection points for proposed water, wastewater, and storm drain lines across eight multi-family buildings. Its primary purpose is to define utility routing, drainage fixture unit (DFU) loads, pipe material specifications, and regulatory compliance notes for the site's wet utilities.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Private domestic water branches: 2\" HDPE service tubing\n*   Private wastewater branches: 6\" PVC at a minimum 2.0% slope\n*   Pressure reducing valve (PRV) set pressure threshold: 65 psi\n*   Number of private fire hydrants on site: 1\n*   Trench depth requiring geologist inspection: Greater than 5 feet\n*   Drainage Fixture Units (DFUs): 4Plex = 136 DFUs, 5Plex = 170 DFUs, 6Plex = 204 DFUs\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' (NAVD 88)\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2**: The main site plan diagram showing buildings (Bldg. 1-8), utility routing (water, wastewater, storm drain), lift stations, cleanouts, and site topography. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, pipe routing, line lengths, and specific component locations.\n*   **Block 1**: Legend defining the symbols and line types used for existing and proposed utilities (W, WW, RW, E, SD) in the main diagram. Use VISION to cross-reference symbols while reviewing Block 2.\n*   **Block 13**: Utility notes specifying pipe materials and slopes for private domestic water and wastewater branches. READ for exact material sizes and installation standards.\n*   **Block 7**: Drainage Fixture Unit Table breaking down the total DFU loads by building number and type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex). READ for specific sanitary load calculations.\n*   **Block 17**: Benchmark data providing precise elevations and descriptions of vertical control points. READ for exact elevation values used for site grading and utility slopes.\n*   **Block 10**: Water tap note outlining requirements for replacing existing Asbestos Cement (AC) pipe with Ductile Iron (DI) pipe and required hazardous disposal protocols. READ for regulatory compliance regarding existing AC lines.\n*   **Block 11**: Special Services Division note mandating compliance with the Austin Fire Code for the site's private fire hydrant. READ for maintenance obligations and the exact private hydrant count.\n*   **Block 5**: Technical note dictating the use of factory restrained joint pipes or mechanical joint restraint devices for all water line bends, tees, and valves. READ for specific structural requirements on water mains.\n*   **Block 9**: PRV Note stipulating that any structure with water pressure at or above 65 psi must install a pressure reducing valve. READ for pressure management requirements.\n*   **Block 19**: Geologist inspection requirement note triggered by the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule for deep trenching. READ for the specific trench depth threshold (5 feet).\n*   **Blocks 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the project title block, engineering firm details, Texas 811 logo, legal description, disclaimers regarding utility locations, and a cross-reference to the landscape plan for trees. READ for general project administration and liability disclaimers if required.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
