{"level":30,"time":1776368741766,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please analyze Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and identify:\n1. The location and path of overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the plan\n2. The locations of all proposed trees (showing the symbols for shade trees, ornamental trees, groundcovers)\n3. Any labeled utility poles or electrical equipment\n4. The proximity/clearances between proposed trees and overhead electric lines\n\nDescribe the spatial arrangement and identify which trees appear to be within restricted zones near the overhead electric facilities. Include coordinates, zone descriptions (north, south, east, west sections), and approximate distances if visible on the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided document, which is labeled as **Sheet 28 of 35 (\"LANDSCAPE PLAN\")** for the \"VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\" project, here are the detailed findings regarding your requested items. \n\n*(Note: The prompt requested analysis of Sheet 31, but the provided image is marked as Sheet 28. The analysis below reflects the contents of the provided Sheet 28).*\n\n### 1. Location and Path of Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines\n*   **Path:** A single overhead electric line is explicitly labeled on this plan. It is denoted by a dashed line with the text **\"---OHE---\"** interspersed along its length.\n*   **Location:** This line runs horizontally across the entire **southern boundary** of the site plan (bottom edge of the drawing), oriented generally from west to east. \n\n### 2. Locations of Proposed Trees (and associated symbols)\nThe plan uses standard landscape architectural symbols (various circular outlines with internal crosshairs or branching patterns) to indicate trees, though the legend does not explicitly separate them into \"shade,\" \"ornamental,\" or \"groundcover\" categories by symbol shape. Instead, they are categorized by zoning function in the \"KEY NOTES\" and text below it:\n*   **SY - STREET YARD TREE:** Located primarily along the western boundary (left side of the page) near the street. These are placed within a shaded area labeled \"H.2\" (STREET YARD).\n*   **M - MITIGATION TREE:** Several trees are labeled with an \"M\". Notable locations include the far north property line (top edge) and the southeast corner.\n*   **PL - PARKING LOT TREE:** Found primarily in the northern section of the lot near parking spaces.\n*   **P - PARKING BUFFER PLANT TREE:** Located along the northern boundary acting as a buffer.\n*   **Spatial Arrangement:**\n    *   **North Zone:** A dense row of trees (labeled with M, PL, P) acts as a buffer along the northern property line.\n    *   **West Zone (Street Frontage):** Several large \"SY\" (Street Yard) trees are clustered near the western property line and entrance.\n    *   **South Zone:** A row of approximately five large trees is aligned along the southern property line.\n    *   **Groundcovers:** The legend designates **\"H.7\"** as **\"SOD\"**. Areas marked with H.7 are scattered throughout, including the southeast corner and eastern boundary. No other specific groundcover symbols are explicitly detailed in the legend.\n\n### 3. Labeled Utility Poles or Electrical Equipment\n*   **Utility Poles:** There are no prominently labeled utility poles (e.g., symbols explicitly tagged with \"UP\" or standard pole markers) visible along the \"---OHE---\" line or elsewhere on this specific landscape plan sheet.\n*   **Electrical Equipment:** No ground-mounted electrical equipment, such as transformers or switchgears (typically labeled XFMR or TR), are identifiable or labeled on this drawing. Landscape plans often omit these unless specific screening is being detailed.\n\n### 4. Proximity/Clearances Between Trees and OHE Lines\n*   **Restricted Zones / Clearances:** There are **no specific clearance zones** (e.g., dashed boxes indicating a 15-foot or 10-foot required clearance from the OHE) drawn or dimensioned on this plan.\n*   **Proximity/Conflicts:** There is a direct spatial overlap shown on the southern boundary. \n    *   There are approximately **five large tree symbols** drawn directly along the southern property line.\n    *   The center points (trunks) of these trees are placed extremely close to the property line.\n    *   The **canopies** of these five trees (indicated by the outer circles of the tree symbols) **directly overlap and intersect the path of the \"---OHE---\" line**. \n    *   Specifically, starting from the southwest corner and moving east along the southern boundary, every major tree shown in that row has a canopy spread that engulfs the dashed \"---OHE---\" line. One of these trees in the southeast corner is accompanied by an \"M\" (Mitigation Tree) label nearby.\n\n**Summary of Spatial Arrangement regarding OHE:**\nThe primary area of concern regarding overhead electric lines is the entire **southern boundary** of the site. The landscape plan depicts a row of large trees whose intended canopy spreads are placed directly underneath and overlapping the path of the designated \"---OHE---\" utility line, with no visible clearance easements or restricted planting zones indicated on this specific sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1436,"outputTokens":970,"totalTokens":4434,"reasoningTokens":2028},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-ch