{"level":30,"time":1776368742903,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan on Sheet 21 and identify:\n\n1. How many transformer pads are shown on the site plan?\n2. Where is each transformer pad located relative to the buildings (which building is it nearest to, or what area of the site)?\n3. What is the approximate distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building?\n4. Are there any dimension callouts or clearance annotations shown on the sheet for the transformer pads?\n5. Are any overhead distribution lines shown on the site plan?\n6. What other utility features are shown (pull boxes, meters, underground lines)?\n7. Are there any notes on the sheet that reference Austin Energy Design requirements or transformer specifications?\n8. What is the property boundary relative to the transformer pad locations?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about the transformer pad placement and any visible clearances or constraints.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here are the answers to your specific questions:\n\n**1. How many transformer pads are shown on the site plan?**\nThere are exactly four (4) transformer pads shown on the site plan. They are represented by square/rectangular boxes outlined in blue with lines pointing to them.\n\n**2. Where is each transformer pad located relative to the buildings?**\nEach of the four pads is explicitly labeled as **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. Their specific locations are:\n*   **Pad 1:** Located on the west side of the site, near the southwest corner of **Bldg. 1**. It sits between the building and the western drive aisle/property boundary.\n*   **Pad 2:** Located on the east side of the site, positioned in the gap just east of **Bldg. 4** and **Bldg. 5**, near the eastern property boundary.\n*   **Pad 3:** Located in the southwest quadrant of the site, near the southwest corner of **Bldg. 8**. It appears to be situated in a landscape or sidewalk island near a parking/drive area.\n*   **Pad 4:** Located in the southeast quadrant of the site, positioned just south of **Bldg. 7** and west of **Bldg. 6**, near the southern turnaround drive aisle.\n\n**3. What is the approximate distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building?**\nThere are **no explicit dimension lines or numerical distance callouts** provided on this sheet to indicate the exact distance from the transformer pads to the buildings. Visually, based on the site layout, all four pads appear to be placed in close proximity to their respective buildings (adjacent to surrounding sidewalks or drive aisles), but an exact measurement cannot be stated without dimension markers.\n\n**4. Are there any dimension callouts or clearance annotations shown on the sheet for the transformer pads?**\n**No.** There are no dimension callouts indicating the size of the transformer pads, nor are there any dashed lines, blast wall indicators, or text annotations showing required safety clearances (such as 10-foot or 5-foot clearance zones) around any of the four \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations.\n\n**5. Are any overhead distribution lines shown on the site plan?**\n**Yes.** Existing overhead electric lines are indicated by gray lines with the text pattern **\"--- OHE ---\"**. These are visible in two primary locations:\n*   Running longitudinally along the far western edge of the drawing (outside the main solid property boundary line, along the street right-of-way).\n*   Running horizontally along the southern edge of the drawing (just outside the main southern property boundary line).\n\n**6. What other utility features are shown (pull boxes, meters, underground lines)?**\nThe plan shows several other electrical features, all marked in blue, including:\n*   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: There are multiple pull boxes distributed throughout the site, acting as junction points along the main electrical routes.\n*   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: These are shown attached to or immediately adjacent to the various buildings (e.g., noted at Bldg. 1, Bldg. 2, Bldg. 4, Bldg. 6, Bldg. 8).\n*   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Solid blue lines represent the routing of underground power. This is explicitly labeled in at least two places: once where power enters the site on the west side, and again in the center of the site between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 1.\n*   **\"Electrical Vault Easement\"**: This is labeled near the southwest corner of Bldg. 8, encompassing an \"Electrical Pull Box\".\n\n**7. Are there any notes on the sheet that reference Austin Energy Design requirements or transformer specifications?**\n**No.** A review of the text in the \"Note\", \"Utility Notes\", and other text blocks at the bottom of the sheet yields no specific reference to \"Austin Energy\", its design criteria manual, or any specific transformer specifications (such as kVA ratings, pad dimensions, or grounding requirements). \n*(Note: There is a reference to \"COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S\" in the bottom left \"Note\", but this specifies rules for trenching and geologist inspection, not transformer/electrical design.)*\n\n**8. What is the property boundary relative to the transformer pad locations?**\nThe property boundary is delineated by the thickest, continuous black polygon outline on the plan. **All four transformer pads are located completely within the main property boundary.**\n*   The pads near Bldg. 1 (west) and Bldg. 4/5 (east) are located relatively close to the perimeter boundary lines.\n*   The pads near Bldg. 8 (southwest) and Bldg. 6/7 (southeast) are located further interior to the site.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1490,"outputTokens":1046,"totalTokens":5223,"reasoningTokens":2687},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan on Sheet 21 and identify:\n\n1. How many transformer pads are shown on the site plan?\n2. Where is each transformer pad located relative to the buildings (which building is it nearest to, or what area of the site)?\n3. What is the approximate distance from each transformer pad to the nearest building?\n4. Are there any dimension callouts or clearance annotations shown on the sheet for the transformer pads?\n5. Are any overhead distribution lines shown on the site plan?\n6. What other utility features are shown (pull boxes, meters, underground lines)?\n7. Are there any notes on the sheet that reference Austin Energy Design requirements or transformer specifications?\n8. What is the property boundary relative to the transformer pad locations?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about the transformer pad placement and any visible clearances or constraints."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-0M6EtsXQejBsGFYRNWwrfKwj","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:45:42 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::sk286-1776368660835-5f495dc17581"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here are the answers to your specific questions:\n\n**1. How many transformer pads are shown on the site plan?**\nThere are exactly four (4) transformer pads shown on the site plan. They are represented by square/rectangular boxes outlined in blue with lines pointing to them.\n\n**2. Where is each transformer pad located relative to the buildings?**\nEach of the 