{"level":30,"time":1776368772885,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"This is Sheet 31, a landscape plan for Valley View Townhomes. Please examine this sheet and identify:\n\n1. Are there overhead electric (OHE) lines shown? If yes, describe their exact locations on the site (north, south, east, west areas, along which roads/property lines).\n\n2. What utility symbols are shown on this sheet? Look for legend items or symbols indicating overhead electric lines, utility poles, transformers, or other electrical infrastructure.\n\n3. Where are trees shown on this plan? What tree species and approximate mature heights are labeled?\n\n4. Identify the relationship between proposed trees and any overhead electric lines - specifically note which trees are near OHE lines and estimate their proximity.\n\n5. Are utility poles visible? If so, what are their locations on the site?\n\nPlease provide a detailed spatial description of the utility infrastructure and landscaping layout shown on this sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (which is labeled as Sheet 28 of 35, though your prompt mentions Sheet 31), here are the findings for your specific questions:\n\n**1. Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines**\n*   **Yes**, overhead electric lines are shown on this plan.\n*   **Location**: A line labeled **\"-OHE-\"** runs horizontally along the entire southern boundary (bottom edge) of the site plan, parallel to the property line. \n\n**2. Utility Symbols**\n*   There is no dedicated utility legend on this specific landscape sheet; the \"KEY NOTES\" only cover paving and landscaping (H-1 through H-7).\n*   However, identifiable utility/infrastructure symbols within the plan include:\n    *   **\"-OHE-\"**: Overhead Electric line (running along the south).\n    *   **\"-SD-\"**: Likely Storm Drain (running east-west through the center of the site).\n    *   **\"-LOC-\"**: Limits of Construction (running around the perimeter of the work area).\n    *   **Pole Symbols**: Small circles with an \"x\" inside them are located at intervals along the \"-OHE-\" line, which typically represent utility poles.\n\n**3. Tree Locations, Species, and Heights**\n*   **Locations**: Trees are primarily shown clustered along the western boundary (left side, street yard), scattered along the northern boundary (top edge), and along the southern boundary (bottom edge). A few trees are also shown internally near parking areas.\n*   **Species and Mature Heights**: **None are labeled on this sheet.** The plan does not list specific tree species (e.g., \"Live Oak\") or approximate mature heights. \n*   Instead of species, trees are labeled with codes denoting their functional or mitigation status. The legend at the bottom right under \"KEY NOTES\" defines these as:\n    *   **\"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**\n    *   **\"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"**\n    *   **\"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"**\n    *   **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**\n    *(For example, trees on the west side are labeled with \"SY-M\", while trees on the north and south are frequently labeled \"M\" or \"PL\".)*\n\n**4. Relationship Between Trees and OHE Lines**\n*   Several proposed or existing tree canopies are located directly adjacent to or underneath the overhead electric lines along the southern boundary.\n*   Specifically, in the southeast (bottom right) and southwest (bottom left) corners, the large circular symbols representing tree canopies completely intersect and overlap the **\"-OHE-\"** line. Some of these trees are labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree). The trunks (center points of the tree circles) appear to be planted just north of the OHE line, but the expected canopies are directly in the path of the utility line.\n\n**5. Utility Poles Visible**\n*   **Yes**, utility poles are visible.\n*   **Locations**: They are represented by small circles containing an 'x' positioned directly on the **\"-OHE-\"** line along the southern (bottom) property boundary. \n*   There is one pole symbol near the southwest corner (bottom left), another roughly in the middle of the southern boundary, and a third near the southeast corner (bottom right).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1496,"outputTokens":753,"totalTokens":4287,"reasoningTokens":2038},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"This is Sheet 31, a landscape plan for Valley View Townhomes. Please examine this sheet and identify:\n\n1. Are there overhead electric (OHE) lines shown? If yes, describe their exact locations on the site (north, south, east, west areas, along which roads/property lines).\n\n2. What utility symbols are shown on this sheet? Look for legend items or symbols indicating overhead electric lines, utility poles, transformers, or other electrical infrastructure.\n\n3. Where are trees shown on this plan? What tree species and approximate mature heights are labeled?\n\n4. Identify the relationship between proposed trees and any overhead electric lines - specifically note which trees are near OHE lines and estimate their proximity.\n\n5. Are utility poles visible? If so, what are their locations on the site?\n\nPlease provide a detailed spatial description of the utility infrastructure and landscaping layout shown on this sheet."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-QCTbaYJLfLsVIMWFd9FEhggZ","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:46:12 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-ver