{"level":30,"time":1776368775156,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Are there any overhead electric utility lines, poles, conductors, or electric easements shown on this site plan? What utilities and infrastructure are depicted relative to the proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, and other site features?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the details regarding overhead electric utility lines, electric easements, and other utilities:\n\n### Overhead Electric Utility Lines, Poles, and Electric Easements\n\n**Yes**, there are overhead electric utility lines and electric easements explicitly shown on this site plan. \n\n*   **Overhead Lines (OHE):** \n    *   A utility line clearly labeled **\"--- OHE ---\"** (indicating Overhead Electric) runs along the entire southern boundary of the site plan, parallel to the main road (Valley View Road). \n    *   Another line labeled **\"--- OHE ---\"** runs vertically along the eastern property boundary (right side of the page).\n*   **Electric Easements:**\n    *   Along the eastern property line, there is a callout pointing to an easement that reads exactly: **\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   Near the southeast corner of the property, another callout points to an easement reading exactly: **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n*   **Associated Infrastructure:**\n    *   A **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** is labeled on the western side of the site, adjacent to the \"Construct Type II Driveway\" entrance and parking area near Building 1.\n\n### Other Utilities and Infrastructure Depicted\n\nThe site plan shows extensive underground utility infrastructure routed primarily through the proposed driveways and parking areas to service the buildings.\n\n*   **Wastewater (WW):** \n    *   Underground lines labeled **\"--- WW ---\"** are routed extensively throughout the internal drive aisles and parking areas, running between the proposed buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) to provide service.\n    *   A hatched area on the western property boundary is labeled **\"Wastewater Easement\"**.\n*   **Water (W):**\n    *   Underground lines labeled **\"--- W ---\"** run roughly parallel to the wastewater lines through the central driveways and branch off to individual buildings. \n    *   A **\"Combined Water and Wastewater Vault Easement\"** is noted near Bldg. 8 on the southern side of the interior drive aisle.\n    *   Fire hydrants, marked by **\"FH\"** symbols, are located along these water lines (e.g., one is visible near Bldg. 8 and another near the transformer pad by Bldg. 1).\n*   **Storm Drainage (SD):**\n    *   Lines labeled **\"--- SD ---\"** run through the main driveways, collecting runoff and directing it northward.\n    *   A **\"Detention Pond\"** with a **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** and **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** is located at the northernmost portion of the site to manage this drainage.\n*   **Gas (G):**\n    *   An underground line labeled **\"--- G ---\"** is shown running parallel to the street along the southern boundary, outside the main property line.\n*   **Other Easements:**\n    *   A **\"5' P.U.E.\"** (Public Utility Easement) is noted along the northern property line.\n    *   A **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** and a **\"15' Easement\"** are noted along the northeastern/eastern boundary.\n\n**Summary of Relationship to Site Features:** \nThe proposed buildings (Bldg 1 - 8) are arranged around a central, looping drive aisle. Almost all major new underground infrastructure (Water, Wastewater, Storm Drain) is buried directly beneath these paved driveways and parking spaces, branching off to connect to each building. The overhead electric lines are restricted to the southern street frontage and the eastern perimeter boundary, avoiding the interior building footprint.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1355,"outputTokens":851,"totalTokens":4322,"reasoningTokens":2116},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Are there any overhead electric utility lines, poles, conductors, or electric easements shown on this site plan? What utilities and infrastructure are depicted relative to the proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, and other site features?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-nVy7fUNULW