und lines labeled **\"--- W ---\"** run roughly parallel to the wastewater lines through the central driveways and branch off to individual buildings. \n    *   A **\"Combined Water and Wastewater Vault Easement\"** is noted near Bldg. 8 on the southern side of the interior drive aisle.\n    *   Fire hydrants, marked by **\"FH\"** symbols, are located along these water lines (e.g., one is visible near Bldg. 8 and another near the transformer pad by Bldg. 1).\n*   **Storm Drainage (SD):**\n    *   Lines labeled **\"--- SD ---\"** run through the main driveways, collecting runoff and directing it northward.\n    *   A **\"Detention Pond\"** with a **\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"** and **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** is located at the northernmost portion of the site to manage this drainage.\n*   **Gas (G):**\n    *   An underground line labeled **\"--- G ---\"** is shown running parallel to the street along the southern boundary, outside the main property line.\n*   **Other Easements:**\n    *   A **\"5' P.U.E.\"** (Public Utility Easement) is noted along the northern property line.\n    *   A **\"25' Drainage Easement\"** and a **\"15' Easement\"** are noted along the northeastern/eastern boundary.\n\n**Summary of Relationship to Site Features:** \nThe proposed buildings (Bldg 1 - 8) are arranged around a central, looping drive aisle. Almost all major new underground infrastructure (Water, Wastewater, Storm Drain) is buried directly beneath these paved driveways and parking spaces, branching off to connect to each building. The overhead electric lines are restricted to the southern street frontage and the eastern perimeter boundary, avoiding the interior building footprint.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex",