{"level":30,"time":1776368778136,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the southern boundary of this sheet where the overhead electric (-OHE-) line runs. I need precise information about:\n\n1. The exact clearance distance between tree canopies and the OHE line. Where trees are shown with circles (representing canopy spread), measure the relationship:\n   - Are any tree canopies directly overlapping the OHE line?\n   - Which specific trees (by label or location) have canopies that violate typical utility clearance zones?\n   - What is the approximate distance from tree trunks to the nearest utility pole?\n\n2. For each tree near the OHE line (particularly in southwest and southeast corners), provide:\n   - Its label designation (M, SY-M, PL, etc.)\n   - The estimated trunk location relative to the OHE line\n   - The estimated canopy spread\n   - Approximate distances\n\n3. Are there any notation marks, measurement dimensions, or clearance annotations on this plan that indicate the designer was aware of utility clearance requirements?\n\nThis is for compliance checking with Austin Energy clearance distances (15-50 feet depending on line type, and 10 feet from poles).","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
