{"level":30,"time":1776369021279,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012q8D15VKekVFVRdeXUs2GX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have a clear picture. The site plan shows:\n\n1. **Existing overhead electric lines** running along and across the property:\n   - Western boundary (along Valley View Road ROW): OHE line with utility poles and guy wires\n   - Southern boundary: OHE line extending eastward with poles\n   - Eastern side: OHE line running north\n   - Multiple utility poles on and adjacent to the site\n\nThis is CRITICAL because the entire EL grouping about clearances applies to this site since there ARE existing overhead electric facilities.\n\nNow I need to systematically evaluate each of the 47 checklist items. Let me organize my approach:\n\n1. First, I need to understand what the applicant has shown on the plans regarding clearance verification\n2. Check for issues with:\n   - Building clearances (7.5-foot and 15-foot requirements)\n   - Driveways/parking clearances (16-18 feet vertical)\n   - Fences, walls, and other site features\n   - Documentation (profile plans, surveyed elevations, etc.)\n   - Notification requirements\n   - Trees/landscaping\n   - Other site features\n\nLet me check the site plan sheets more carefully to see what clearance documentation and notes are provided.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2030,"cache_read_input_tokens":49786,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2030},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4842cd33-4ac7-488e-aa08-33032c2696e2","uuid":"d9c0762a-0282-423c-8203-