dg 4 (4,144 sf):** Located in the center of the site, south of Bldg 3. Oriented East-West.\n*   **Bldg 5 (3,290 sf):** Located in the Northeast corner, along the eastern boundary. Oriented North-South.\n*   **Bldg 6 (3,290 sf):** Located in the East-Central area, south of Bldg 5, along the eastern boundary. Oriented North-South.\n*   **Bldg 7 (4,144 sf):** Located in the Southeast corner, bounded by the eastern and southern property lines. Oriented North-South.\n*   **Bldg 8 (4,997 sf):** Located in the Southwest corner, bounded by the western and southern property lines. Oriented East-West.\n\n### 2) Overhead Utility Lines, Poles, or Transmission Structures\n*   **Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines:** Lines labeled `- OHE -` run along the exterior perimeter of the site. They are clearly visible running parallel to the Southern boundary, the Eastern boundary, and the Western boundary.\n*   **Utility Poles:** Symbols for utility poles (small circles intersecting the OHE lines) are visible along these OHE routes, particularly noted along the southern and eastern boundary lines. Guy wires are indicated near the pole at the southwest corner.\n\n### 3) Location of the Detention/Biofiltration Pond\n*   The **\"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\"** is located in the Northeast section of the site. It is situated directly north of Bldg 3 and Bldg 5, bordered to the north and east by a \"Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n\n### 4) Location of Driveways and Parking Areas\n*   **Driveways:** The primary access is on the West side, labeled \"Construct Type III Driveway\", which leads into a central internal roadway looping around Buildings 2 and 4. A secondary access point is located on the Southwest side, also labeled \"Construct Type III Driveway\".\n*   **Parking Areas:** Parking is integrated along the internal driveways. Surface parking spaces are arranged perpendicularly along the north side of the main East-West driveway (facing Bldgs 1 & 3), along the west side of the North-South driveway (facing Bldgs 5, 6, & 7), and in the southwest area between Bldgs 2 and 8. The \"Parking Data\" table indicates 76 of the provided spaces are garages (attached to the units).\n\n### 5) Utility Easement Markings or Boundaries\nSeveral utility easements are explicitly marked with dashed boundaries and text annotations:\n*   **South:** \"15' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"\n*   **East:** \"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14...\", \"15' Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\", and \"25' Drainage Easement\".\n*   **West:** \"Wastewater Easement\", \"Water & Wastewater Easement\", and \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n\n### 6) Clearance Dimension Annotations Near Utilities\n*   There are no specific radial clearance dimension annotations (e.g., \"10' OSHA Clearance Arc\") explicitly drawn or labeled around the overhead lines or poles. Standard dimensional setbacks are shown from buildings to property/easement lines (e.g., `21.3'` from Bldg 8 to the southern boundary).\n\n### Visible Electrical Infrastructure Summary\n*   **Overhead:** Continuous `- OHE -` lines and associated poles along the South, East, and West boundaries.\n*   **Underground/Pad-mounted:** A pad labeled **\"Transformer Pad (Typ.)\"** is located just west of Bldg 2, adjacent to the driveway. Electrical easements (5' and 15' widths) are marked on the East and South edges of the property.\n\n***\n\n### Document Table Transcriptions\nAs requested, here are exact, character-by-character transcriptions of the tables found at the bottom of the document.\n\n**Building Data Table**\n| Building # | Building Type | Gross Floor Area (sf) | Building Coverage (sf) | Bedroom Type | Units |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | Two Bedroom | 15 |\n| 2 | 6 Plex | 13,004 | 4,997 | Three Bedroom | 23 |\n| 3 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | Total Units | 39 |\n| 4 | 5 Plex | 10,776 | 4,144 | | |\n| 5 | 4 Plex | 8,550 | 3,290 | Maximum Number of Building Stories = 3 | |\n| 6