{"level":30,"time":1776369132604,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GVrXhzcv9LBHVGA2K1Z1jr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! So I now have confirmation that:\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Lines (OHE):**\n   - Southern boundary: runs horizontally along entire southern property line\n   - Northern boundary: runs horizontally along entire northern property line\n\n2. **Electrical Equipment:**\n   - Transformer Pad (Typ.) on western side near Bldg. 2\n   - 5' Electric Easements on eastern and southeastern areas\n   - Underground electric lines (typically, but not detailed on the site plan)\n\n3. **Utility Poles:**\n   - Present along the OHE lines but not explicitly labeled\n\nSo now I need to check the actual locations of the proposed trees against these overhead electric lines and equipment. The vision analysis of the Landscape Plan showed trees along the southern boundary that overlap with the OHE line.\n\nNow I need to measure the actual distances from trees to the overhead electric conductors. But first, I need to know which specific trees are in that southern row and get their species and utility compatibility info.\n\nLet me check if the plant schedule on Sheet 35 shows specific locations or symbols that I can cross-reference. Actually, from Sheet 35 blocks.md, I can see that the plant list uses symbols:\n\n**Shade Trees:**\n- 2 Live Oak (circle with cross)\n- 10 Cedar Elm (circle with hash)\n\n**Ornamental Trees:**\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (circle with wavy edge)\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (circle with jagged edge)\n\nNow I need to verify the utility compatibility and mature heights of these species. According to the grouping file's regulatory overview:\n- Utility-compatible trees are marked with \"UC\" in ECM Appendix F\n- Large trees have mature height ≥ 40 feet per ECM Appendix F\n\nI need to research these specific species. Let me check if there's any reference material in the project or if I need to use the measure-distance tool to actually measure clearances.\n\n\nBefore I can determine clearance distances, I should review the Electrical Design Plan on Sheet 21 to understand the scale and see exactly where the underground electrical equipment is positioned relative to the tree locations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1219,"cache_read_input_tokens":60141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1219},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f35260c3-5e1a-4786-b2cb-3f3a59e76a22","uuid":"a510fcfc-08b9-41e7-a1d2-21b00d65a8e4"}
