m the pole center\n3. The tree symbols show crown circles, and I'm measuring from the canopy edge rather than the trunk\n\nI need to determine whether the \"OHE\" marking represents just the utility corridor or the precise conductor position. Without being able to see the exact drawing details or cross-arm specifications, I can't definitively confirm whether this constitutes a violation.\n\nThe vision tool identified trees within 5-10 feet of the OHE line, and the distance measurement showed essentially 0 feet between them. This suggests potential clearance issues, but I should verify the Site Plan to see the actual pole and conductor locations relative to the proposed trees before concluding there's a deficiency.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1628,"cache_read_input_tokens":61623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1628},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ea8d5c-5e13-4865-9c33-dfa30e84d15a","uuid":"b9950c94-5080-4c6c-a662-d628dd6516e8"}
