{"level":30,"time":1776369377825,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and identify:\n1. Where are trees and shrubs shown on the plan?\n2. Are there any trees or vegetation shown near the transformer pad locations (near Building 8 or other areas)?\n3. What tree species or mitigation trees are identified?\n4. Are there any root barrier details or tree protection areas shown?\n5. What is the distance from trees to buildings and other features?\n6. Are there specific planting notes related to utility proximity?\n7. Where are parking lot islands and landscaped areas?\n\nPlease provide specific observations about vegetation placement relative to transformer pads, especially near the labeled transformer pad near Building 8.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776369377827,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical design plan and identify: 1) Location and type of underground electric lines, transformers, meters, and pull boxes; 2) Routing of electrical lines relative to buildings and driveways; 3) Any clearance dimensions annotated from electric facilities to buildings, driveways, parking areas, or other structures; 4) Location of service connections and whether they have clearance annotations; 5) Any overhead electric lines shown or referenced; 6) Any utility poles, guy wires, or other overhead infrastructure shown. Report the specific locations and whether clearance requirements are addressed with dimensions or notes.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the Valley View Townhomes project, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1) Location and type of underground electric lines, transformers, meters, and pull boxes:**\n*   **Underground Electric Lines:** Indicated by solid blue lines with periodic \"E\" markings.\n*   **Transformers:** There are two large square/rectangular pads explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. \n    *   One is located on the west side of the property, between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8.\n    *   The second is located on the east side of the property, between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 6.\n*   **Meters:** Banks of meters are indicated by rectangular boxes labeled **\"Electrical Meters\"**. These are located attached or immediately adjacent to the buildings at the following locations:\n    *   West side of Bldg. 1\n    *   West side of Bldg. 2\n    *   North side of Bldg. 3\n    *   East side of Bldg. 4\n    *   East side of Bldg. 5\n    *   East side of Bldg. 6\n    *   South side of Bldg. 7\n    *   West side of Bldg. 8\n*   **Pull Boxes:** Small blue circles/squares labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** are distributed along the underground lines. They are found near almost all meter locations (Bldg 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8), near the western property entrance, and near the southeast driveway entrance. \n\n**2) Routing of electrical lines relative to buildings and driveways:**\n*   The primary **\"Underground Electric Line\"** enters the site from the west (from Valley View Road), connecting first to a pull box and then to the western \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   From the transformers, the lines route parallel to the exterior walls of the buildings to reach the various \"Electrical Meters\".\n*   To connect the north buildings (1, 3, 4, 5) and south buildings (8, 7, 6), the electrical lines cross directly under the central east-west driveway/parking area. Lines also cross under the western and eastern north-south drive aisles.\n\n**3) Clearance dimensions annotated from electric facilities:**\n*   **None.** There are absolutely no clearance dimensions (e.g., specific distance measurements in feet/inches indicating required separation) annotated from any of the underground electric lines, transformer pads, pull boxes, or meters to the buildings, driveways, parking areas, or property lines on this plan.\n\n**4) Location of service connections and clearance annotations:**\n*   Service connections to the buildings terminate at the clustered **\"Electrical Meters\"** noted in Item 1 (located on the exterior walls of the buildings). \n*   **None.** As with the broader facilities, there are no clearance annotations or dimension lines provided for these service connection points.\n\n**5) Overhead electric lines shown or referenced:**\n*   Overhead lines are denoted by dashed lines labeled **\"OHE\"**.\n*   An \"OHE\" line runs north-south along the western property boundary (parallel to Valley View Road).\n*   Another \"OHE\" line runs west-east along the southern property boundary.\n\n**6) Utility poles, guy wires, or other overhead infrastructure:**\n*   Utility poles (represented by small circles on the OHE lines) are visible along both the western and southern \"OHE\" routes.\n*   A **\"Guy Wire\"** is explicitly labeled on the western edge near the southwest corner of the property, attached to one of the utility poles.\n*   **Clearance Requirements:** Neither dimensions nor notes addressing clearance requirements for these overhead facilities, poles, or guy wires are present on this document.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1432,"outputTokens":813,"totalTokens":4675,"reasoningTokens":2430},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the electrical design plan and identify: 1) Location and type of underground electric lines, transformers, meters, and pull boxes; 2) Routing of electrical lines relative to buildings and driveways; 3) Any clearance dimensions annotated from electric facilities to buildings, driveways, parking areas, or other structures; 4) Location of service connections and whether they have clearance annotations; 5) Any overhead electric lines shown or referenced; 6) Any utility poles, guy wires, or other overhead infrastructure shown. Report the specific locations and whether clearance requirements are addressed with dimensions or notes."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-FdezL4f5DqkrXWnHTLT4KGGw","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:52:40 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::v4h22-1776369133238-762194f7d57d"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" for the Valley View Townhomes project, here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1) Location and type of underground electric lines, transformers, meters, and pull boxes:**\n*   **Underground Electric Lines:** Indicated by solid blue lines with periodic \"E\" markings.\n*   **Transformers:** There are two large square/rectangular pads explicitly labeled **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**. \n    *   One is located on the west side of the property, between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8.\n    *   The second is located on the east side of the property, between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 6.\n*   **Meters:** Banks of meters are indicated by rectangular boxes labeled **\"Electrical Meters\"**. These are located attached or immediately adjacent to the buildings at the following locations:\n    *   West side of Bldg. 1\n    *   West side of Bldg. 2\n    *   North side of Bldg. 3\n    *   East side of Bldg. 4\n    *   East side of Bldg. 5\n    *   East side of Bldg. 6\n    *   South side of Bldg. 7\n    *   West side of Bldg. 8\n*   **Pull Boxes:** Small blue circles/squares labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** are distributed along the underground lines. They are found near almost all meter locations (Bldg 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8), near the western property entrance, and near the southeast driveway entrance. \n\n**2) Routing of electrical lines relative to buildings and driveways:**\n*   The primary **\"Underground Electric Line\"** enters the site from the west (from Valley View Road), connecting first to a pull box and then to the western \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   From the transformers, the lines route parallel to the exterior walls of the buildings to reach the various \"Electrical Meters\".\n*   To connect the north buildings (1, 3, 4, 5) and south buildings (8, 7, 6), the electrical lines cross directly under the central east-west driveway/parking area. Lines also cross under the western and eastern north-south drive aisles.\n\n**3) Clearance dimensions annotated from electric facilities:**\n*   **None.** There are absolutely no clearance dimensions (e.g., specific distance measurements in feet/inches indicating required separation) annotated from any of the underground electric lines, transformer pads, pull boxes, or meters to the buildings, driveways, parking areas, or property lines on this plan.\n\n**4) Location of service connections and clearance annotations:**\n*   Service connections to the buildings terminate at the clustered **\"Electrical Meters\"** noted in Item 1 (located on the exterior walls of the buildings). \n*   **None.** As with the broader facilities, there are no clearance annotations or dimension lines provided for these service connection points.\n\n**5) Overhead electric lines shown or referenced:**\n*   Overhead lines are denoted by dashed lines labeled **\"OHE\"**.\n*   An \"OHE\" line runs north-south along the western property boundary (parallel to Valley View Road).\n*   Another \"OHE\" line runs west-east along the southern property boundary.\n\n**6) Utility poles, guy wires, or other overhead infrastructure:**\n*   Utility poles (represented by small circles on the OHE lines) are visible along both the western and southern \"OHE\" routes.\n*   A **\"Guy Wire\"** is explicitly labeled on the western edge near the southwest corner of the property, attached to one of the utility poles.\n*   **Clearance Requirements:** Neither dimensions nor notes addressing clearance requirements for these overhead facilities, poles, or guy wires are present on this document.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1432,"outputTokens":813,"totalTokens":4675,"reasoningTokens":2430},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-