 of Bldg. 5\n    *   East side of Bldg. 6\n    *   South side of Bldg. 7\n    *   West side of Bldg. 8\n*   **Pull Boxes:** Small blue circles/squares labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** are distributed along the underground lines. They are found near almost all meter locations (Bldg 1, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8), near the western property entrance, and near the southeast driveway entrance. \n\n**2) Routing of electrical lines relative to buildings and driveways:**\n*   The primary **\"Underground Electric Line\"** enters the site from the west (from Valley View Road), connecting first to a pull box and then to the western \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   From the transformers, the lines route parallel to the exterior walls of the buildings to reach the various \"Electrical Meters\".\n*   To connect the north buildings (1, 3, 4, 5) and south buildings (8, 7, 6), the electrical lines cross directly under the central east-west driveway/parking area. Lines also cross under the western and eastern north-south drive aisles.\n\n**3) Clearance dimensions annotated from electric facilities:**\n*   **None.** There are absolutely no clearance dimensions (e.g., specific distance measurements in feet/inches indicating required separation) annotated from any of the underground electric lines, transformer pads, pull boxes, or meters to the buildings, driveways, parking areas, or property lines on this plan.\n\n**4) Location of service connections and clearance annotations:**\n*   Service connections to the buildings terminate at the clustered **\"Electrical Meters\"** noted in Item 1 (located on the exterior walls of the buildings). \n*   **None.** As with the broader facilities, there are no clearance annotations or dimension lines provided for these service connection points.\n\n**5) Overhead electric lines shown or referenced:**\n*   Overhead lines are denoted by dashed lines labeled **\"OHE\"**.\n*   An \"OHE\" line runs north-south along the western property boundary (parallel to Valley View Road).\n*   Another \"OHE\" line runs west-east along the southern property boundary.\n\n**6) Utility poles, guy wires, or other overhead infrastructure:**\n*   Utility poles (represented by small circles on the OHE lines) are visible along both the western and southern \"OHE\" routes.\n*   A **\"Guy Wire\"** is explicitly labeled on the western edge near the southwest corner of the property, attached to one of the utility poles.\n*   **Clearance Requirements:** Neither dimensions nor notes addressing clearance requirements for these overhead facilities, poles, or guy wires are present on this document.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":1322575.439858,"endTime":1349358.954696,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"7T3haZPuO_6Bh-cP0I-EuQI"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.04178","marketCost":"0.04178","inferenceCost":"0.04178","inputInferenceCost":"0.002864","outputInferenceCost":"0.038916","generationId":"gen_01KPBXKSX407CCJYGQAZ5B6ZEY"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
{"level":30,"time":1776369377827,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014LBo5Ka3vp7rEkuVsRFdcV","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided document, here is the requested information:\n\n**1. Sheet Identification**\nThis is the **Cover** sheet. This is indicated in the bottom right corner of the document (\"Sheet: 1 of 39\") and within the \"Sheet List Table\" which lists Sheet Number 1 as \"Cover\".\n\n**2. Table of Contents / Index (Sheet List Table)**\nBelow is the exact reproduction of the \"Sheet List Table\" found in the upper right quadrant of the document:\n\n| Sheet Number | Sheet Title |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| 1 | Cover |\n| 2 | Survey |\n| 3 | General Notes |\n| 4 | Existing Conditions Survey |\n| 5 | Erosion and Sedimentation Control Plan |\n| 6 | Erosion Control Notes |\n| 7 | Erosion Control Details |\n| 8 | Tree Removal & Demolition Plan |\n| 9 | Site Plan |\n| 10 | Fire Protection Plan |\n| 11 | Grading Plan |\n| 12 | Storm Sewer Plan |\n| 13 | Drainage Area Map |\n| 14 | Inlet Drainage Area Map |\n| 15 | Biofiltration-Detention Pond Plan & Calculations |\n| 16 | Biofiltration-Detention Pond Profiles |\n| 17 | Conveyance Cross Sections |\n| 18 | Austin Water General Information & Construction Notes |\n| 19 | Utility Tap Plan |\n| 20 | Utility Tap Public Plan & Profile |\n| 21 | Preliminary Electrical Design Plan |\n| 22 | Construction Details 1 |\n| 23 | Construction Details 2 |\n| 24 | Construction Details 3 |\n| 25 | Construction Details 4 |\n| 26 | Construction Details 5 |\n| 27 | Construction Details 6 |\n| 28 | Construction Details 7 |\n| 29 | Addressing Plan |\n| 30 | Existing Tree Plan |\n| 31 | Landscape Plan |\n| 32 | Tree List |\n| 33 | Canopy Impact Exhibit |\n| 34 | Root Zone Impact Exhibit |\n| 35 | Landscape Calculations |\n| 36 | Biofiltration Pond Plans & Calculations |\n| 37 | Landscape Details |\n| 38 | Wall Plan |\n| 39 | Wall Plan Notes and Details |\n\n**3. Landscape Plan Sheet Number**\nAccording to the Sheet List Table, the **\"Landscape Plan\"** is located on **Sheet Number 31**."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015NsDFTMFyqMDpfKEpSkiAS","session_id":"df64853a-4f90-499d-b38e-749986aed001","uuid":"56f9215d-a85c-4fc8-b13e-937deb082495"}
{"level":30,"time":1776369377827,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJGD6VyBDuEA75tqAMu18k","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a close visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), there are **no specific tree species** (e.g., Oak, Elm, Crape Myrtle) labeled on the plan, nor is there a plant schedule or legend on this page that identifies proposed tree species. \n\nInstead, trees are labeled strictly by their functional category using abbreviations. The legend on the right side of the page defines these abbreviations exactly as follows:\n\n*   `SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE`\n*   `M - MITIGATION TREE`\n\n**Regarding the southern property boundary (near the overhead electric lines):**\nThe overhead electric lines are indicated by a line style labeled \"- OHE -\" along the bottom (southern) edge of the site plan. There are three proposed trees shown directly adjacent to this boundary. \n*   All three of these trees are labeled exclusively with the letter **\"M\"**, indicating they are designated as **Mitigation Trees**. \n*   No specific plant species is listed for these trees on this sheet. \n\nOther trees throughout the plan are similarly labeled with these category tags, such as \"M\" (along the northern boundary), \"SY/M\" (in the western shaded street yard area), and \"PL/M\" (near the northern parking area), but none include species names."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1e954d11-1eb9-4d3c-b419-4ac7a7240f6a","uuid":"d3da5c2d-6309-4723-99c3-6cd20af92dc8","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a close visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), there are **no specific tree species** (e.g., Oak, Elm, Crape Myrtle) labeled on the plan, nor is there a plant schedule or legend on this page that identifies proposed tree species. \n\nInstead, trees are labeled strictly by their functional category using abbreviations. The legend on the right side of the page defines these abbreviations exactly as follows:\n\n*   `SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)`\n*   `P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE`\n*   `M - MITIGATION TREE`\n\n**Regarding the southern property boundary (near the overhead electric lines):**\nThe overhead electric lines are indicated by a line style labeled \"- OHE -\" along the bottom (southern) edge of the site plan. There are three proposed trees shown directly adjacent to this boundary. \n*   All three of these trees are labeled exclusively with the letter **\"M\"**, indicating they are designated as **Mitigation Trees**. \n*   No specific plant species is listed for these trees on this sheet. \n\nOther trees throughout the plan are similarly labeled with these category tags, such as \"M\" (along the northern boundary), \"SY/M\" (in the western shaded street yard area), and \"PL/M\" (near the northern parking area), but none include species names."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776369377827,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"Review the entire sheet and identify any notes, sections, or content blocks that specifically address electric transmission lines, clearance requirements, or Austin Energy requirements. Look for sections titled \"Electric Transmission Notes,\" \"Electric Notes,\" or similar. Report the exact text of these requirements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the exact transcriptions of the sections addressing electric transmission lines, clearance requirements, and Austin Energy requirements. \n\n### **Electric Notes**\n*(Located in the middle-left column)*\n\n\"1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n### **Electric Transmission Notes**\n*(Located in the top-center column)*\n\n\"1. **No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement.** No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n2. **Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.** Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512.505.7133 to schedule a meeting.\n3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512.505.7133 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (alt 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n7. No hazards, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20' feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n8. 24 Hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be roll/down curbing.\n12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\n16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n    - any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, or\n    - any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n\n*(Note: There is an additional unnumbered block of text in the middle column beneath the Electric Transmission Notes and adjacent to the Fire Department notes that contains the exact duplicate text of the 5 points listed under the \"Electric Notes\" section).*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1364,"outputTokens":1211,"totalTokens":6154,"reasoningTokens":3579},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Review the entire sheet and identify any notes, sections, or content blocks that specifically address electric transmission lines, clearance requirements, or Austin Energy requirements. Look for sections titled \"Electric Transmission Notes,\" \"Electric Notes,\" or similar. Report the exact text of these requirements."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-jJMPIeQDxKCx7crTHLMYNT0m","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:53:02 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::c2kkv-1776369124333-884b38c36881"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the exact transcriptions of the sections addressing electric transmission lines, clearance requirements, and Austin Energy requirements. \n\n### **Electric Notes**\n*(Located in the middle-left column)*\n\n\"1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n### **Electric Transmission Notes**\n*(Located in the top-center column)*\n\n\"1. **No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement.** No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\n2. **Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.** Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512.505.7133 to schedule a meeting.\n3. A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512.505.7133 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (alt 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\n4. Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\n5. Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n6. Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\n7. No hazards, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 20' feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\n8. 24 Hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\n9. Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\n10. Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\n11. Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structures/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be roll/down curbing.\n12. Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\n13. Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\n14. Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\n15. Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.\n16. Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    - any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices,\n    - any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, or\n    - any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n\n*(Note: There is an additional unnumbered block of text in the middle column beneath the Electric Transmission Notes and adjacent to the Fire Department notes that contains the exact duplicate text of the 5 points listed under the \"Electric Notes\" section).*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1364,"outputTokens":1211,"totalTokens":6154,"reasoningTokens":3579},"warnings":[],"providerMetadat