t 19 - Utility Tap Plan"}],"comment":"Wastewater service lines (labeled 'WW' with 6-inch PVC at 2.0% minimum slope) are shown on utility plan near transformer locations, but no clearance dimensions are documented. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["Storm drain routing in proximity to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 19 - Utility Tap Plan"}],"comment":"Storm drain lines (labeled 'SD') are shown on utility plan near transformer pads, particularly near Buildings 4 and 7, but no clearance dimensions are provided. Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["Underground utility coordination zones near transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","label":"Sheet 19 - Utility Tap Plan"}],"comment":"Multiple underground utilities are shown routing near transformer pads (water, wastewater, storm drain, electric), but no spacing dimensions are provided between these utilities and transformer equipment. Minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead structures and parking garages near transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in the electrical plan set. If overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas exist a