{"level":30,"time":1776369506310,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":38,"prompt":"Examine the retaining wall plan and identify: 1) All retaining wall locations on the site; 2) Relationship of retaining walls to the overhead electric (OHE) lines visible on prior sheets along the south, east, and west boundaries; 3) Any clearance dimensions shown from the retaining wall faces/tops to overhead electric lines; 4) Wall heights and wall face angles; 5) Any sections or profiles showing vertical clearances from walls to overhead infrastructure. Report specifically what clearance dimensions (if any) are shown between walls and overhead utilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided engineering drawing (titled \"3759 VALLEY VIEW\" and labeled \"WALL PLAN\"), here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**1) All retaining wall locations on the site:**\n*   The \"PLAN VIEW\" section on the left side of the document shows the layout of the retaining walls.\n*   A \"NEW RETAINING WALL\" is indicated by a thick dashed black line.\n*   This new wall runs roughly parallel to an \"EXISTING WALL\" (indicated by a thin solid line) and intersects with sections labeled \"POND WALL REF PG 2\" (indicated by thick solid black lines).\n*   A note in the plan view states: \"NEW WALL TO BE IN PLACE PRIOR TO DEMO FOR POND WALLS.\"\n\n**2) Relationship of retaining walls to the overhead electric (OHE) lines visible on prior sheets along the south, east, and west boundaries:**\n*   There are **no** overhead electric (OHE) lines, poles, or overhead utility easements depicted or referenced anywhere on this specific sheet. Therefore, the relationship between the retaining walls and OHE lines cannot be determined from this document alone.\n\n**3) Any clearance dimensions shown from the retaining wall faces/tops to overhead electric lines:**\n*   Because overhead electric lines are not shown on this sheet, there are **no clearance dimensions** provided from the retaining walls to any overhead electric lines.\n\n**4) Wall heights and wall face angles:**\n*   **Wall Heights:** The primary cross-section detail is titled **\"14'-0\\\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\"**. The diagram shows a vertical dimension line spanning from the top of the wall footing to the top of the wall itself, explicitly labeled **\"14'-0\\\" MAX\"**.\n*   **Wall Face Angles:** The cross-section drawing of the 14-foot retaining wall depicts a perfectly vertical wall face (90 degrees). It is shown with a uniform thickness of **\"1'-0\\\"\"** from top to bottom, with no batter (slope) indicated on either the front or back face. A note at the top indicates to \"CHAMFER EXPOSED EDGES (TYPICAL)\", but the primary face is vertical.\n\n**5) Any sections or profiles showing vertical clearances from walls to overhead infrastructure:**\n*   There are **no** sections or profiles on this sheet that show overhead infrastructure. The details provided (\"14'-0\\\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\", \"TYPICAL STEP IN FOOTING\", and \"DOWEL DETAIL\") only show the wall structure, footing, rebar, gravel backfill, and surrounding soil/slabs.\n\n**Summary of Clearance Dimensions to Overhead Utilities:**\n*   **None.** There are absolutely no clearance dimensions shown between the retaining walls and overhead utilities on this document. General note #2 states \"OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION\", but this specifies \"depth\", typically implying underground utilities rather than overhead.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1423,"outputTokens":623,"totalTokens":3582,"reasoningTokens":1536},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINAR