{"level":30,"time":1776369506312,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) and identify:\n1. Does this sheet show utility poles or overhead electric lines?\n2. Are there any utility easements marked along the property boundaries?\n3. Specifically look at the southern boundary along Valley View Road - are there any utility poles or overhead lines shown?\n4. Are there any notes or symbols indicating the presence or absence of overhead utilities?\n5. What utilities are shown on this plan - water, sewer, electric, or others?\n\nThe goal is to understand whether overhead electric infrastructure crosses or borders the property, and if so, where it's located relative to the proposed buildings and landscaping.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of the provided Site Plan (Sheet 9), here are the precise findings regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Does this sheet show utility poles or overhead electric lines?**\nYes, the sheet clearly shows both overhead electric lines and utility poles. \n*   Overhead electric lines are denoted by dashed lines interspersed with the text \"**--- OHE ---**\". \n*   An explicit utility pole is labeled in the top left (northwest) corner near the driveway entrance, reading \"**AT&T Pole**\". \n*   Circle symbols that typically denote poles are located along the lines labeled \"--- OHE ---\".\n\n**2. Are there any utility easements marked along the property boundaries?**\nYes, numerous utility easements are marked exactly along the property boundaries. I can identify the following exact text callouts:\n*   **Northern Boundary (Top right):** \"**5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n*   **Eastern Boundary (Right side):** \"**25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\", \"**5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\", and \"**10' Water Line Easement...**\" (text partially cut off).\n*   **Southern Boundary (Bottom edge):** \"**5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.**\" and further to the right, \"**5' Elec & Tele Easement Vol. 5968, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.**\"\n*   **Northwest Area (Near entrance):** \"**Wastewater Easement Doc# 2010...**\" (text partially obscured).\n\n**3. Specifically look at the southern boundary along Valley View Road - are there any utility poles or overhead lines shown?**\nYes. Running continuously along the very bottom property boundary (the southern edge), there is a dashed utility line explicitly labeled with the repeating text \"**--- OHE ---**\" signifying Overhead Electric lines. Associated with this line on the southern boundary are exact text notes indicating a \"**5' Elec. Easement**\" and a \"**5' Elec & Tele Easement**\". \n\n**4. Are there any notes or symbols indicating the presence or absence of overhead utilities?**\nYes, the presence of overhead utilities is indicated by a specific linetype symbol used throughout the drawing.\n*   The primary symbol is the dashed line containing the text \"**--- OHE ---**\" which traces the southern boundary. \n*   Specific callouts point to infrastructure, such as the \"**AT&T Pole**\" in the northwest corner.\n\n**5. What utilities are shown on this plan - water, sewer, electric, or others?**\nThe plan shows a comprehensive layout of multiple utility types, indicated by linetypes, equipment pads, and specific notes:\n*   **Electric:** Overhead lines marked \"**--- OHE ---**\", multiple rectangular features labeled \"**Transformer Pad (Typ.)**\" located near the proposed buildings, and \"**5' Electric Easement**\" boundaries. \n*   **Water:** Underground lines marked \"**--- W ---**\", an \"**Existing Water Manhole**\" (top left), and a \"**Water Meter**\" vault.\n*   **Wastewater/Sewer:** Underground lines marked \"**--- S ---**\", a \"**Wastewater Service Connection**\" (top left), and cleanouts labeled \"**CO**\". \n*   **Storm Drainage:** Underground lines marked \"**--- SD ---**\", a large \"**Detention Pond**\" at the northeast corner, and a \"**25' Drainage Easement**\".\n*   **Telecommunications:** An \"**AT&T Pole**\" (top left) and a boundary marked \"**5' Elec & Tele Easement**\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1447,"outputTokens":896,"totalTokens":4853,"reasoningTokens":2510},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Site Plan (Sheet 9) and identify:\n1. Does this sheet show utility poles or overhead