 4, near Units 404/405)*\n1. **Contours and Spot Elevations:** Building 4 has an FFE of \"685.50\". Immediately east of the building, spot elevations drop steeply to \"683.75\" and \"683.25\". Further east is an \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\" with Top of Wall (\"TW\") elevations near \"681.64\" and Existing Grade (\"EG\") dropping down to \"669.97\".\n2. **Direction of Surface Drainage/Slope Flow:** A flow arrow points directly **East**. The slope drops rapidly and aggressively from the building (685.50) towards the eastern retaining wall (~681.64).\n3. **Runoff Flow Relative to Pad Location:** Surface runoff flows strongly **away** from the building across this area toward the eastern drop-off/retaining wall.\n4. **High/Low Point:** This area is situated on a **steep downward slope**. It is a low point relative to the building slab, but a severe high point relative to the deep grade drop beyond the retaining wall to the east.\n\n### **Location 4: South-central south of Bldg. 7**\n*(Area immediately south of Building 7, near Units 701-705)*\n1. **Contours and Spot Elevations:** Building 7 has an FFE of \"685.0\". Spot elevations immediately south of the building wall are \"681.50\", \"681.69\", and \"681.56\". Further south is an established drainage channel/swale with spot elevations dropping from \"680.99\" to \"680.50\" to \"679.94\" as it moves west. Contour lines \"681\" and \"680\" run parallel to the southern edge of the building.\n2. **Direction of Surface Drainage/Slope Flow:** Flow arrows immediately south of the building point **South**, directing water down the slope from the 681.50 range into the swale (680.99 range). Once in the swale, flow arrows point **West**.\n3. **Runoff Flow Relative to Pad Location:** Runoff flows **away** from the building southward. If the pad is immediately south of the building, water will shed past it and into the lower drainage swale.\n4. **High/Low Point:** The area immediately next to the building is on a **slope**. It is substantially lower than the building itself (685.0 -> 681.50) but remains a relative high point compared to the dedicated drainage swale (~680.50) located directly to its south."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776369506313,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":3,"prompt":"What notes or requirements are listed on this sheet regarding electric utilities, overhead electric lines, electric transmission, electrical clearances, or the 48-hour notification requirement before work near high-voltage lines? Please list all electric-related notes or requirements found on this sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan sheet, here are the exact notes and requirements regarding electric utilities, overhead electric lines, electric transmission, electrical clearances, and notifications. \n\nThese are found in two dedicated sections, **\"Electric Notes\"** and **\"Electric Transmission Notes\"**, as well as an unnumbered block of text that duplicates the Electric Notes. \n\n### **Electric Notes**\n*Found in the middle-left column of the document:*\n\n1. \"Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n2. \"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\"\n3. \"The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\"\n4. \"The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless required clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\"\n5. \"Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\"\n\n*(Note: Immediately below the \"Fire Department\" section, there is an unnumbered block of text that repeats the exact same five paragraphs listed above word-for-word.)*\n\n---\n\n### **Electric Transmission Notes**\n*Found in the upper-middle section of the document. Bolding is replicated exactly as it appears:*\n\n1. \"**No trees shall be planted within the transmission easement.** No trees shall be planted within 25 feet of the base of the transmission structure. Vehicular access for Austin Energy trucks and equipment is always to be maintained within the easement. Austin Energy will not be responsible for damage and/or removal of vegetation within the easement.\"\n2. \"**Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures, including down guy anchors.** Grading near electric transmission facilities must be coordinated with Austin Energy prior to commencement of grading. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a meeting.\"\n3. \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting. Include Chuck Hendry (at 505-7151) in the meeting, if cranes are being used during construction. OSHA requires a 20' clearance from energized transmission lines during construction.\"\n4. \"Barricades must be erected 10 feet from electric transmission structures during construction.\"\n5. \"Any relocation of electric transmission facilities or outages caused by this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n6. \"Warning signs must be placed under the overhead electric transmission facilities as notification of the electrical hazard.\"\n7. \"No spoils, materials, aerial equipment, dumpsters, staging or spoils areas are not permitted within 25 feet of the transmission wire and/or structures and must be located outside the easement.\"\n8. \"24 hour access to electric facilities shall be maintained.\"\n9. \"Any temporary or permanent fence preventing access to the transmission facilities and/or easement shall be coordinated with Austin Energy staff. AE staff will install a lock on the gate for access.\"\n10. \"Property owner and contractor are responsible for dust controls to minimize contamination of wire and insulators caused by dust from this project. Any subsequent cleaning or electrical outages caused by dust from this project will be charged to the property owner and contractor.\"\n11. \"Property owner is responsible for any damages to curbing, landscaping, walls, paving placed around the electric transmission structure/poles/lines caused by Austin Energy during maintenance and repairs. All curbing within the electric transmission easement must be non-load bearing.\"\n12. \"Roads/driveways/pavement/parking within the easement should be built to support a 46,000 lb tandem axle (5 foot spacing) to ensure safety.\"\n13. \"Fire hydrants must be located out of the transmission easement and a minimum of 20 feet from any transmission structure.\"\n14. \"Sprinklers are prohibited within 25 feet of transmission poles and structures.\"\n15. \"Do not dig or grade within 25 feet of the transmission structures (including down guy anchors).\"\n16. \"Owner may not place, erect, construct or maintain the following within electric transmission easement:\n    * any permanent structures, including, but not limited to habitable structures such as homes, mobile homes, garages, or offices.\n    * any structure of any kind in such proximity to the electric transmission or distribution lines, poles, structures, towers, or appurtenant facilities as would constitute a violation of the National Electric Safety Code in effect at the time the structure is erected, nor\n    * any structures, including but not limited to, fences, storage sheds, drainage, filtration or detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to the transmission easements or its lines, poles, structures, towers or appurtenant facilities in the easements.\"\n\n---\n\n### **Legend Items Related to Electrical**\n*Found in the Legend in the top-right:*\n*   **-OHE-** Existing Overhead Electric Line\n*   **Symbol (Circle with cross)** Existing Power Pole & Down Guy\n*   **Symbol (Square box)** Existing Electric Meter\n*   **Symbol (Square with 'T')** Existing Transformer Pad","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1365,"outputTokens":1354,"totalTokens":6634,"reasoningTokens":3915},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 3237656]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"What notes or requirements are listed on this sheet regarding electric utilities, overhead electric lines, electric transmission, electrical clearances, or the 48-hour notification requirement before work near high-voltage lines? Please list all electric-related notes or requirements found on this sheet."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-999aCdP3lyqUMj5qtlgKrLqm","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 16 Apr 2026 19:57:15 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encodi