{"level":30,"time":1776369506314,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017SES4cPkeDoQJ5rZnsa8rS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided landscape plan document, here is the comprehensive breakdown of the utility infrastructure and tree planting locations as requested:\n\n**6. SITE CONTEXT (Addressing Document Identification First)**\n*   *Correction to Prompt:* You stated this is \"Sheet 31\". However, the title block in the bottom right corner explicitly states this is **Sheet 28 of 35**.\n*   *Sheet Title:* LANDSCAPE PLAN\n*   *Project Name:* VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\n*   *Buildings/Structures:* The plan shows two large, central building footprints that are long and rectangular with articulated edges. On the east side of the site, there are two distinct, hatched rectangular structures labeled **SEDIMENTATION BASIN** and **FILTRATION BASIN**.\n*   *Boundaries:* The site is bounded by property lines marked heavily with **-LOC-** (Limits of Construction). To the west (left side of the drawing), a street is faintly labeled **Valley View Road**.\n\n**1. OVERHEAD ELECTRIC LINES**\n*   **Presence and Location:** Yes, overhead electric lines are shown. They run along the entire southern property line (the bottom edge of the drawing based on the North arrow pointing up).\n*   **Line Style/Symbols:** The line is represented by a solid black line that is periodically broken by the text label **-OHE-**.\n*   **Other Utility Text Labels Visible:** While OHE is present on the south edge, other utility lines visible on the plan include **-SD-** (running horizontally through the center courtyard area between the buildings) and **-W-** (running vertically along the western edge near the street yard).\n\n**2. UTILITY POLES**\n*   **Presence:** Utility pole locations are **not explicitly marked** or clearly discernible along the -OHE- line on this specific landscape plan sheet.\n*   **Representation:** There are no distinct utility pole symbols (such as circles with crosses, solid squares, or specific \"pole\" callouts) visible along the path of the overhead electric line.\n*   **Spacing:** Because utility poles are not marked on this drawing, it is impossible to determine the spacing between them.\n\n**3. UTILITY LEGEND**\n*   **Utility Symbols:** There are **no utility symbols shown in a legend** on this page. The \"KEY NOTES\" section in the top right corner is exclusively dedicated to landscaping, paving, and fencing elements (e.g., H-1 Proposed Paving, H-7 Sod).\n*   **Abbreviations:** Because there is no utility legend, abbreviations present on the drawing itself (such as **OHE**, **SD**, **W**, **LOC**) are not explicitly defined anywhere on this specific sheet.\n\n**4. TREE LOCATIONS AND SPECIES**\n*   **Locations:** Trees are located primarily along the perimeters:\n    *   *North:* A row of trees runs along the upper property boundary.\n    *   *South:* A row of trees runs along the lower property boundary.\n    *   *West (Street Yard):* A dense cluster of trees is located within the shaded area bordering Valley View Road.\n    *   *Interior/East:* Scattered trees are placed in parking lot islands, between the buildings, and near the drainage basins on the east side.\n*   **Tree Species and Heights:** There are **no tree species names or mature heights** labeled anywhere on this plan. This sheet only shows locations and designation codes.\n*   **Tree Designation Codes:** The following codes are used in the drawing and are explicitly defined in the text below the \"KEY NOTES\":\n    *   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    *   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n    *   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    *   **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n    *   *(Note: On the plan, these codes are often combined next to a tree symbol, such as \"SY M\" or \"PL M\").*\n\n**5. TREES NEAR OVERHEAD LINES**\n*   **Conflict Area:** Multiple trees along the southern property line (bottom edge of the drawing) are located directly adjacent to or directly underneath the Overhead Electric (**-OHE-**) line.\n*   **Specific Trees and Overlap:** Tracing the southern boundary from west to east (left to right), there is a continuous row of proposed tree canopy circles. The solid **-OHE-** line is drawn passing directly *through* the center points (the crosshairs representing the trunk) of at least three trees on the southwestern edge, and passes completely through the drawn canopy circles of the remaining trees along that southern border.\n*   **Labels and Species:** The tree symbols along this southern -OHE- line feature a distinct **M** (Mitigation Tree) label beside one of the canopies towards the eastern end. As noted above, specific species and mature heights are not provided on this sheet.\n*   **Distance:** Based on the 2D drawing, the distance from the utility line to the trees is zero; the tree planting locations (trunks/canopies) are drawn directly overlapping the -OHE- line."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015NsDFTMFyqMDpfKEpSkiAS","session_id":"df64853a-4f90-499d-b38e-749986aed001","uuid":"b2bef311-acb1-4f69-9f93-27f3ec2770fb"}
