{"level":30,"time":1776369511234,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_013Pr4jkBQ3fvaDCHL667gjm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CRITICAL FINDING! I can see the Electric Transmission Notes mention:\n\"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction.\"\n\nThis is related to transmission facilities, but I need to check if there's a standard 48-hour notification requirement for distribution lines as well, as mentioned in the grouping file.\n\nThe grouping file states that plans must include: \"48-hour notification plan note: Plans must include note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003)\"\n\nFrom what I can see, there's a pre-construction safety meeting requirement for TRANSMISSION facilities (item 3 in Electric Transmission Notes), but I don't see a specific 48-hour notification note for distribution line work in the general notes.\n\nLet me now look at what overhead facilities are actually shown on the plans and whether proper clearance dimensions are provided. I should also check if there are profile/section views showing vertical clearances.\n\nLet me examine Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan) more carefully to see if it shows clearances from overhead lines to buildings and driveways.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1692,"cache_read_input_tokens":66561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1692},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"