{"level":30,"time":1776369747666,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RrEcmKgSXbk4cLcwg3z9Mt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete\n\nI've completed the comprehensive site plan review for **Grouping 2: Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**. \n\n**Summary of Findings:**\n\nThe site plan for Valley View Townhomes includes overhead electric distribution infrastructure along the southern property boundary. The Landscape Plan proposes trees—including large species like Live Oak and Cedar Elm—positioned immediately adjacent to the overhead electric line (approximately 0 feet from the conductor). \n\n**Six deficiencies were identified:**\n\n1. **EL-2.1 (FAIL):** Non-utility-compatible trees (Live Oak) within 15 feet of the distribution conductor\n2. **EL-2.3 (FAIL):** Large trees (40+ feet mature height) within 25 feet of the distribution conductor  \n3. **EL-2.10 (FAIL):** Two trees in the southern row cannot be identified to species—plant legend is incomplete\n4. **EL-2.11 (FAIL):** Large trees are not differentiated in the plant schedule, preventing verification of clearance compliance\n5. **EL-2.14 (FAIL):** Trees are not clearly shown in relation to the overhead electric facilities with measurements or callouts\n6. **EL-2.15 (FAIL):** Trees are proposed within prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval\n\n**Items not flagged (pass, n/a, or not-verifiable):** EL-2.2, EL-2.4 (transmission lines not present), EL-2.5 (non-transmission easements), EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9 (insufficient information), EL-2.12, EL-2.13 (no dimensions shown on plans to evaluate).\n\nThe applicant must revise the landscape plan to either relocate trees outside restricted clearance zones or obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy 