{"level":30,"time":1776369955864,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017qoABMsWanvMZrLMyQgjvc","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md:18:* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/06-fire-for-site-plan-review.md:19:* U0: Fire Department access roads must be a minimum of 25 ft wide with a minimum of 14 ft vertical clearance. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:149:* U0: Service commitment from a commercial trash service must be provided indicating they can provide service. The letter should address the minimum clearance requirement for the service vehicles.\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 50, offset: 0]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea9f585d-bb2f-49f8-82db-171aaa3ded31","uuid":"2a42099d-d98f-4107-8d0b-f9624027a687","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md:18:* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/06-fire-for-site-plan-review.md:19:* U0: Fire Department access roads must be a minimum of 25 ft wide with a minimum of 14 ft vertical clearance. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/03-transportation-public-works-tpw-tds-review.md:149:* U0: Service commitment from a commercial trash service must be provided indicating they can provide service. The letter should address the minimum clearance requirement for the service vehicles.","numLines":3,"appliedLimit":50}}
{"level":30,"time":1776369955864,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KmkLAu7bwzafrZJ5SiiyDp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The search results show that UCM § 1.10.4 has been referenced by Austin Energy but I haven't found specific comments about transformer pads. Let me now compile my findings and determine the status of each checklist item.\n\nBased on my comprehensive research:\n\n**FINDINGS FROM DOCUMENT REVIEW:**\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Locations**: Sheet 21 shows 4 transformer pads, but they are NOT DIMENSIONED relative to buildings, structures, or other features.\n\n2. **Critical Missing Documentation**:\n   - No Austin Energy Design written approval documents\n   - No transformer pad detail sheets (required by UCM § 1.5.2.6)\n   - No clearance dimensions or annotations on any plan sheets\n   - No cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances\n   - No transformer easements shown\n   - No specifications identifying transformer type (single-phase vs. three-phase, oil-filled vs. dry-type)\n   - No evidence of 100% private property electrical routing\n   - No documentation of fire escape clearances\n   - No root barrier details for trees near transformers\n\n3. **Overhead Distribution Lines**: Shown on western and southern site boundaries (outside property)\n\n4. **Fire Hydrant**: 1 private hydrant shown in SW corner\n\n5. **Parking**: 10 surface spaces shown, pads located near parking areas\n\n6. **Buildings**: 8 buildings with various heights and setbacks\n\n7. **Sidewalks**: 5' concrete sidewalk on western edge near transformer pad\n\n8. **Retaining Walls**: Shown around site perimeter\n\n9. **Trees/Vegetation**: Proposed on landscape plan, but no utility-compatible species verification visible\n\n10. **Utility Lines**: Underground water, wastewater, storm drain shown\n\n11. **Grading/Drainage**: Cannot determine if drainage slopes away from transformer pads (critical for oil-filled equipment)\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:\n\n\n- **EL-13.1**: Cannot verify the 5-foot building clearance since no dimensions are provided on the plans.\n- **EL-13.2**: Retaining walls exist on site, but without measurements I cannot confirm whether they maintain adequate separation from the transformer pads.\n- **EL-13.3**: Need to assess fire escape clearance requirements, but this information is not documented on the submitted sheets.\n- **EL-13.4**: No evidence of reduced clearances or corresponding architect approval is shown.\n- **EL-13.5**: No balconies or overhangs are depicted near the equipment locations, so this requirement doesn't apply.\n- **EL-13.6**: The transformer type isn't specified, so I cannot determine if the 12-foot window/door setback for oil-filled units is required.\n- **EL-13.7**: Sheet 9 shows the transformer pads appear to be less than 2 feet from the back of sidewalk, which represents a potential non-compliance issue.\n- **EL-13.8**: No stairwells are shown adjacent to the transformer locations.\n- **EL-13.9**: Without transformer specifications or identified fire escapes, the 20-foot clearance requirement cannot be verified.\n- **EL-13.10**: The access door location and orientation aren't indicated, so the 10-foot hot-stick clearance cannot be assessed.\n- **EL-13.11**: No confined space is identified near the transformer pads that would trigger the 15-foot clearance requirement.\n- **EL-13.12**: The fire hydrant location relative to the transformer pads is not shown on the plans.\n- **EL-13.13**: Tree species aren't identified in relation to the transformer locations.\n- **EL-13.14**: Shrub placement relative to transformers lacks dimensional information.\n- **EL-13.15**: No trees are documented as being within the 20-foot zone requiring root barriers.\n- **EL-13.16**: Dumpsters aren't shown; trash collection uses individual bins per unit instead.\n- **EL-13.17**: Bike rack locations aren't specified relative to the transformer pads.\n- **EL-13.18**: Light pole placement relative to transformers is not clearly documented.\n- **EL-13.19**: Fire lanes aren't explicitly marked on the fire protection plan, making clearance verification impossible.\n- **EL-13.20**: While four pads are shown, no dimensions exist between them.\n- **EL-13.21**: Water lines are visible but lack dimensional callouts from the pads.\n- **EL-13.22**: Wastewater lines are shown without clearance dimensions.\n- **EL-13.23**: Storm drain lines are present but lack dimensional information.\n- **EL-13.24**: No gas service is indicated on the site plan.\n\nUtilities are depicted on the plans but lack the specific measurements needed to confirm proper spacing. Overhead lines are shown, though the pad-mounted configuration may affect applicability of certain clearance requirements. Other facilities could still be impacted by these installations.\n\nNiche-mounted transformers aren't indicated on the drawings, so those standards don't apply. Cross-section details are missing entirely, which prevents verification of vertical clearances around the pad locations. The transformer type can't be determined from available documentation, making it impossible to assess drainage and grading conditions. All four pads do fall within the property boundary as shown on Sheet 21. Easement conflicts require further examination.\n\nTransformer easements aren't depicted anywhere on the plans, and electrical routing clarity is questionable regarding private property boundaries. The AE Design specifications for pad dimensions lack supporting detail sheets, leaving dimensions unverified on the construction documents. Equipment positioned near parking areas needs bollard protection, but the necessary dimensional and detail information isn't provided to confirm compliance.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":68117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":721},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea9f585d-bb2f-49f8-82db-171aaa3ded31","uuid":"1ef872e1-c922-4851-b301-c4a605ec1b7f"}
