{"level":30,"time":1776369955864,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019qdbg4ne6CcGSBR464HL89","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 10: text_block — List of 10 site plan release notes outlining requirements and conditions for the approved site plan, including building codes, relocation costs, demolition permits, and utility service providers.\n     4→\n     5→Site Plan Release Notes\n     6→1. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require a site plan amendment and approval from the Development Services Department.\n     7→2. Approval of this site plan does not include Building Code and Fire Code approval; or building, demolition, or relocation permits approval. A City demolition or relocation permit can only be issued once the historic review process is completed.\n     8→3. All signs must comply with the requirements of the Land Development Code.(Chapter 25-10)\n     9→4. The owner is responsible for all costs of relocation of, or damage to, utilities.\n    10→5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\n    11→6. A Site Development Permit must be issued prior to an application for building permit for non-consolidated or Land Use Commission approved site plans.\n    12→8. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n    13→9. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n    14→10. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\n    15→\n    16→## Block 11: text_block — Locations and elevations for two benchmarks used in the project.\n    17→\n    18→Benchmarks\n    19→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    20→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    21→\n    22→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    23→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    24→\n    25→## Block 12: text_block — Notice stating the applicant's responsibility for determining ADA compliance.\n    26→\n    27→Americans with Disabilities Act\n    28→The City of Austin has reviewed this plans for compliance with City development regulations only. The applicant, property owner, and occupant of the premises are responsible for determining whether the plan complies with all other laws, regulations , and restrictions which may be applicable to the property and its use.\n    29→\n    30→## Block 13: text_block — List of 7 requirements from the Austin Fire Department regarding pavement, hydrants, installation timing, paving standards, dumpster placement, fire lanes, and vertical clearances.\n    31→\n    32→Fire Department\n    33→1. The Austin Fire Department requires asphalt or concrete pavement prior to construction as an \"all-weather driving surface.\"\n    34→2. Hydrants must be installed with the center of the four-inch opening at least 18 inches above finished grade. The four-inch opening must face the driveway or street with three- to six-foot setbacks from the curbline(s). No obstruction is allowed within three feet of any hydrant and the four-inch opening must be totally unobstructed from the street.\n    35→3. TIMING OF INSTALLATION: When fire protection facilities are installed by the developer, such facilities shall include all surface access roads which shall be installed and made serviceable prior to and during the time of construction. Where alternative methods of protection, as approved by the Fire Chief, are provided, the above may be modified or waived.\n    36→4. All pervious/decorative paving shall be engineered and installed for 80,000 lb. live-vehicle loads. Any pervious/decorative paving within 100 feet of any building must be approved by the Fire Department.\n    37→5. Commercial dumpsters and containers with an individual capacity of 1.5 cubic yards or greater shall not be stored or placed within ten feet of openings, combustible walls, or combustible eave lines.\n    38→6. Fire lanes designated on site plan shall be registered with City of Austin Fire Marshal's office and inspected for final approval.\n    39→7. Vertical clearance required for fire apparatus is 14 feet for full width of access drive.\n    40→\n    41→## Block 17: text_block — Legal description of the property for the site plan.\n    42→\n    43→Legal Description\n    44→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    45→\n    46→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea9f585d-bb2f-49f8-82db-171aaa3ded31","uuid":"8ed7af90-b496-431a-9229-9af02da2cb08","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 10: text_block — List of 10 site plan release notes outlining requirements and conditions for the approved site plan, including building codes, relocation costs, demolition permits, and utility service providers.\n\nSite Plan Release Notes\n1. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require a site plan amendment and approval from the Development Services Department.\n2. Approval of this site plan does not include Building Code and Fire Code approval; or building, demolition, or relocation permits approval. A City demolition or relocation permit can only be issued once the historic review process is completed.\n3. All signs must comply with the requirements of the Land Development Code.(Chapter 25-10)\n4. The owner is responsible for all costs of relocation of, or damage to, utilities.\n5. Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\n6. A Site Development Permit must be issued prior to an application for building permit for non-consolidated or Land Use Commission approved site plans.\n8. All existing structures shown to be removed will require a demolition permit from the City of Austin Development Services Department.\n9. For construction within the right-of-way, a ROW excavation permit is required.\n10. Water and wastewater service will be provided by the City of Austin (or identify the service provider if other than the City of Austin).\n\n## Block 11: text_block — Locations and elevations for two benchmarks used in the project.\n\nBenchmarks\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 12: text_block — Notice stating the applicant's responsibility for determining ADA compliance.\n\nAmericans with Disabilities Act\nThe City of Austin has reviewed this plans for compliance with City development regulations only. The applicant, property owner, and occupant of the premises are responsible for determining whether the plan complies with all other laws, regulations , and restrictions which may be applicable to the property and its use.\n\n## Block 13: text_block — List of 7 requirements from the Austin Fire Department regarding pavement, hydrants, installation timing, paving standards, dumpster placement, fire lanes, and vertical clearances.\n\nFire Department\n1. The Austin Fire Department requires asphalt or concrete pavement prior to construction as an \"all-weather driving surface.\"\n2. Hydrants must be installed with the center of the four-inch opening at least 18 inches above finished grade. The four-inch opening must face the driveway or street with three- to six-foot setbacks from the curbline(s). No obstruction is allowed within three feet of any hydrant and the four-inch opening must be totally unobstructed from the street.\n3. TIMING OF INSTALLATION: When fire protection facilities are installed by the developer, such facilities shall include all surface access roads which shall be installed and made serviceable prior to and during the time of construction. Where alternative methods of protection, as approved by the Fire Chief, are provided, the above may be modified or waived.\n4. All pervious/decorative paving shall be engineered and installed for 80,000 lb. live-vehicle loads. Any pervious/decorative paving within 100 feet of any building must be approved by the Fire Department.\n5. Commercial dumpsters and containers with an individual capacity of 1.5 cubic yards or greater shall not be stored or placed within ten feet of openings, combustible walls, or combustible eave lines.\n6. Fire lanes designated on site plan shall be registered with City of Austin Fire Marshal's office and inspected for final approval.\n7. Vertical clearance required for fire apparatus is 14 feet for full width of access drive.\n\n## Block 17: text_block — Legal description of the property for the site plan.\n\nLegal Description\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776369955864,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VvhEaCAtxcozVDWQAe7Jsi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good - I found important information. The release notes (Block 10, item 5) state: \"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\" This confirms that no electric easements are currently shown on the plans, which is a deficiency.\n\nNow let me compile my findings. Based on my comprehensive research, here are the items I will flag as FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE:\n\n**FAIL items:**\n1. EL-13.7 - Pad immediately adjacent to sidewalk (not 2 feet away) based on Sheet 9 vision analysis\n2. EL-13.31 - No cross-section drawings provided\n3. EL-13.35 - Transformer easements not shown\n4. EL-13.37 - No AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE items:**\n1. EL-13.1 - No dimension callouts for building clearances\n2. EL-13.2 - Retaining walls present but no distances to transformer pads shown\n3. EL-13.3 - Fences may be adjacent but no clearances dimensioned\n4. EL-13.4 - No documentation of reduced clearances or AE approval\n5. EL-13.6 - No transformer equipment type specified (oil-filled vs. dry)\n6. EL-13.9 - No transformer type specified, no fire escapes identified\n7. EL-13.10 - No access door orientation or clearances shown\n8. EL-13.12 - Fire hydrant shown but no distance dimensions from pads\n9. EL-13.13 - No tree species identification relative to transformer pads\n10. EL-13.14 - No shrub clearances documented\n11. EL-13.15 - No trees identified within 20 feet with root barrier details\n12. EL-13.17 - Bike racks not specifically located\n\n\n13. EL-13.18 - Light poles lack specific positioning\n14. EL-13.19 - Fire lanes unmarked on plans\n15. EL-13.20 - Spacing between the four transformer pads not dimensioned\n16. EL-13.21 through EL-13.26 - Water, wastewater, and storm drain lines are depicted but without clearance dimensions, making utility stacking indeterminate\n17. EL-13.27 - Overhead lines present yet pad clearances cannot be verified given the pad-mounted configuration\n18. EL-13.32 - Transformer specifications unclear regarding oil-filled status and drainage provisions\n19. EL-13.34 - No transformer easements documented, preventing conflict verification\n20. EL-13.36 - Electrical routing path not confirmed as entirely within private property boundaries\n21. EL-13.38 - Pads positioned near parking areas without bollard protection details\n22. EL-13.39 - Overhead line routing relative to structures remains unresolved\n\nThe most pressing deficiencies center on dimensional clarity and utility coordination. Reconsidering the pad placement near the sidewalk and tree well from the site analysis suggests potential conflicts that warrant closer examination of the actual positioning constraints.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3640,"cache_read_input_tokens":68838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3640},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea9f585d-bb2f-49f8-82db-171aaa3ded31","uuid":"a03591e4-b6a2-45cf-ba98-70326722946b"}
{"level":30,"time":1776369955864,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VvhEaCAtxcozVDWQAe7Jsi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research of the site plan documents, I can now evaluate the transformer pad clearance and location requirements. Let me compile my findings.\n\n## Summary of Research Findings\n\n**Documents Reviewed:**\n- Sheet 21: Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (4 transformer pads shown)\n- Sheet 9: Site Plan (1 transformer pad labeled near Building 8)\n- Sheet 10: Fire Protection Plan (1 private fire hydrant shown)\n- Sheet 31: Landscape Plan (vegetation shown)\n- Sheet 11: Grading Plan (topography and drainage)\n- Sheet 19: Utility Tap Plan (water, wastewater, storm drain)\n- Sheets 22-28: Construction Details (no transformer pad details found)\n- Master Comment Report and Austin Energy Review (generic requirements, no project-specific approvals)\n\n**Critical Missing Documentation:**\n- No Austin Energy Design written approval documents\n- No AE Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets\n- No clearance dimensions or annotations from transformer pads to buildings/structures\n- No transformer specifications (single-phase vs. three-phase, oil-filled vs. dry-type)\n- No transformer easements shown on any plan\n- No cross-section drawings showing vertical clearances\n- No root barrier details for vegetation near pads\n- No evidence of 100% private property electrical routing from transformers to meters\n- No documentation of fire escape clearances\n- No bollard details or specifications\n\n**Key Observations:**\n- 4 transformer pads shown on electrical plan (Sheet 21) but with no dimension callouts\n- All pads appear to be within property boundary\n- Overhead distribution lines shown on western and southern edges (outside property)\n- Fire hydrant shown in southwest corner\n- Parking areas present, with surface spaces near transformer pads\n- Sidewalks, retaining walls, and vegetation shown on plans but without clearance dimensions to transformer pads\n\nNow I will generate my findings for items that are FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3640,"cache_read_input_tokens":68838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3640},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea9f585d-bb2f-49f8-82db-171aaa3ded31","uuid":"6590f3b3-c428-43cc-bb1d-466d82466209"}
{"level":30,"time":1776369955864,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VvhEaCAtxcozVDWQAe7Jsi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CdZh1qZnbbaknHphSpUaQk","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4","UCM § 1.10.5.B"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations shown on electrical plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown on the electrical plan but no dimension callouts or clearance annotations indicate distances from the pads to adjacent buildings (Buildings 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8). Minimum 5-foot clearance from buildings cannot be verified from the submitted documents."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls present around site perimeter and detention pond area"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls are shown on the grading and site plans, but no dimensions indicate clearance distances from transformer pads to these walls. Minimum 5-foot clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations on electrical plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No fence locations or clearance dimensions from transformer pads are shown on the site plans. Compliance with required 5-foot clearance (for sides with operators/controls) or 3-foot clearance (for sides without operators/controls) cannot be verified without access door orientation and fence location details."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.4","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 2"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations if clearances less than 5 feet to buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No evidence of reduced (3-foot) clearances or Austin Energy Design written approval is provided. If reduced clearances are proposed, documentation of AE Design approval, fire rating verification, confined space confirmation, and vertical clearance to windows/doors/ducts cannot be verified from submitted plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.5","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations if balconies or overhangs are present"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevations or architectural details showing balconies or overhangs above or adjacent to transformer pads are provided. Clearance from balconies/overhangs and absence of coverings directly above pads cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer equipment specifications are provided indicating whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. For oil-filled equipment, minimum 12-foot horizontal clearance from windows, doors, or ventilating ducts (when less than 12 feet from grade or less than 5 feet lateral separation) cannot be verified without equipment type specification and building elevation details."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad on west side of site near Building 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The transformer pad shown near Building 8 on the site plan is positioned adjacent to a 5-foot concrete sidewalk on the western property line. No dimension callout indicates the exact distance from the pad to the back of the sidewalk, preventing verification of the required 2-foot minimum clearance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer equipment specifications indicate whether equipment is oil-filled. No fire escape locations are identified on the site or building elevation plans. For oil-filled equipment, minimum 20-foot horizontal/radial clearance from fire escapes cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No dimensions or annotations indicate access door orientation or clearance distances from the hot-stick use area (access door side) to open areas or adjacent buildings/structures. The required 10-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified without this information."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations relative to private fire hydrant"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"One private fire hydrant is shown in the southwest corner of the site. Dimension callouts showing distances from each transformer pad to the fire hydrant are not provided. Compliance with the 5-foot minimum clearance requirement cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.13","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4","ECM Appendix F"],"applicableAreas":["Tree locations on landscape plan relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":32}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan shows trees marked with designations (SY, PL, M, P) but does not provide species names or identify which trees meet ECM Appendix F utility-compatible requirements. Trees within 10 lateral feet of pad-mounted equipment or 15 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors cannot be verified as utility-compatible species per ECM Appendix F."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas adjacent to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Shrub and low-lying vegetation locations are shown on the landscape plan, but clearance distances (10 lateral feet from access door side, 5 lateral feet from other sides) from transformer pads are not dimensioned. Compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.15","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No root barrier details or specifications are shown on the landscape or detail sheets. Trees within 20 lateral feet of underground electric equipment cannot be verified as having required root barriers (minimum 4 feet deep, installed 5 feet from equipment)."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Bike rack locations relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Bike rack locations are not explicitly dimensioned relative to transformer pad locations on the site plan. Compliance with required 5-foot minimum clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Light pole locations relative to transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Light pole locations are not specifically shown or dimensioned on the site plan or electrical plan. Compliance with required 5-foot minimum clearance from light poles cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Fire lanes on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Fire lanes are not explicitly marked, dimensioned, or labeled on the fire protection plan. Therefore, 15-foot clearance between transformer pads and designated fire lanes cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"F