{"level":30,"time":1776369958659,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01P7Bvvbz1t1nRZ5tF5Yxpt5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed the evaluation of grouping **EL-MD-EXP 13** (Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan.\n\n### Summary of Findings\n\n**Total Checklist Items Evaluated:** 39  \n**Fail Items:** 3  \n**Not-Verifiable Items:** 26  \n**Pass Items:** 1 (EL-13.33 - all pads are within property boundary)  \n**N/A Items:** 9 (items requiring specific features not present on site)\n\n### Critical Deficiencies Identified\n\n**Immediate Failures:**\n\n1. **EL-13.31** - No cross-section drawings provided showing vertical clearances around transformer locations\n2. **EL-13.35** - Transformer easements are not shown on any plan sheets\n3. **EL-13.37** - No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets provided; pad dimensions not specified\n\n### Primary Gaps Preventing Verification\n\nThe site plan shows four transformer pads on the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) but lacks critical documentation:\n\n- **No clearance dimensions** from transformer pads to buildings, structures, utilities, vegetation, sidewalks, or other site features\n- **No transformer specifications** indicating equipment type (single-phase vs. three-phase, oil-filled vs. dry-type)\n- **No access door orientation** preventing verification of hot-stick clearance requirements (10-foot or 15-foot depending on confined space)\n- **No tree species identification** relative to utility-compatibility requirements\n- **No root barrier or bollard details** provided\n- **No evidence of Austin Energy Design coordination or approval documents**\n- **Electrical routing not verified** as 100% on private property\n\nAll of these missing elements prevent verification of compliance with UCM § 1.10.4 and related standards governing transformer pad placement and clearances. The applicant must coordinate directly with Austin Energy to obtain approved transformer pad details, provide clearance dimensions on all relevant plan sheets, and document all required easements and design approvals."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7135,"cache_read_input_tokens":72478,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7135},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea9f585d-bb2f-49f8-82db-171aaa3ded31","uuid":"ba06d628-5f87-4060-8f70-16e9b6810aab"}
