n drawings are provided showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas. Cross-sections are required to demonstrate compliance with vertical clearance requirements for transformer access and any overhead obstructions."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations and grading"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer equipment specifications indicate whether equipment is oil-filled. Grading plan shows contours but does not explicitly annotate drainage direction from transformer pad locations. For oil-filled equipment, compliance with requirement that liquid flow be directed away from buildings cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pad locations and easement areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer easements are shown on any plan sheet. Plat depicts drainage easement (NE corner), public utility easement, and wastewater easement, but transformer pad locations relative to these easements cannot be verified. Confirmation that pads are not located in drainage easements, water easements, sewer easements, or electrical easements under overhead lines (without AE Design written approval) cannot be provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer easements are depicted on the plat, site plan, electrical plan, or easement exhibit sheets. Transformer easements around pads (required for Austin Energy accessibility) are not shown, and their widths are not specified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from transformers to meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The electrical plan shows routing of underground electric lines from transformer pads to meters, but does not clearly indicate whether 100% of the routing is on private property. Property boundary and easement locations relative to electrical routing cannot be definitively verified from the submitted plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["All four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided in the site plan. Pad dimensions, foundation specifications, equipment specifications, and construction details do not match AE Design-approved specifications for the service type (single-phase or three-phase). Specific pad dimensions are not shown on the submitted plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads located near parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pads are shown adjacent to parking areas, but no dimension callouts indicate distances from pads to parking edges. Bollard details (4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal posts) per AE Design equipment pad details are not shown. Compliance with bollard requirements when pads are within 4 feet of parking areas or vehicle routes cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed customer facilities relative to overhead distribution lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines are shown on the western and southern site boundaries. Building and structure locations relative to these overhead lines cannot be definitively verified as not being installed under or over the conductors due to lack of dimension callouts and utility clearance annotations."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7b8aae6b-d1a8-417b-b2bd-8dc0380f0bdd"}
