overlapping the \"- - OHE - -\" lines in this bottom right corner.\n*   **Left Edge (West):** While not labeled \"OHE\", there is a line running vertically along the left property boundary labeled \"- - E - -\" which typically denotes an electric line. There are existing trees located near this line.\n\n**3. Any notation about tree removal or retention near utility lines**\n*   **Regarding OHE lines:** There are no specific text notations regarding tree removal or retention in relation to the \"- - OHE - -\" lines. Based purely on the legend symbols overlapping the lines in the bottom right corner, the trees directly over the OHE lines are designated as \"EXISTING TREE - TO REMAIN\" (circle with a dot). Other trees in that cluster are marked \"EXISTING TREE - TO BE REMOVED\" (circle with an 'X').\n*   **Regarding the '- - E - -' line:** Along the left edge of the plan near the \"- - E - -\" line, there are two specific notations pointing to trees designated to remain (circle with a dot):\n    *   \"4939 TO REMAIN - BUT WILL BE MITIGATED AS IF REMOVED\"\n    *   \"4924 TO REMAIN - BUT WILL BE MITIGATED AS IF REMOVED\"\n\n**4. Species of trees that remain near overhead lines**\nThe species of the trees are **not provided** on this specific drawing sheet.\n*   There is a note below the \"KEY NOTES\" legend that states exactly: **\"NOTE: REFER SHEET 28 FOR TREE LIST.\"**\n*   Because Sheet 28 is not included in this single image, the species cannot be determined from the provided document.\n\n**5. Any clearance dimensions or utility-related notes**\n*   There are **no clearance dimensions** indicated between the overhead electric lines and the existing trees on this plan.\n*   There are **no specific utility-related text notes** regarding construction, safety, or clearance requirements in the text blocks titled \"SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\" or \"REMEDIAL TREE CARE NOTES.\" The only utility indicators are the line labels \"- - OHE - -\" and \"- - E - -\".","provide