{"level":30,"time":1776370082941,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":11,"prompt":"Examine the grading plan and identify: 1) Location of all proposed and existing contours and final grades; 2) Location and identification of retaining walls; 3) Any overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the plan; 4) Location of driveways and parking areas with their finished grades; 5) Any clearance dimensions from the finished grades or structures to overhead electric lines; 6) Any utility poles or overhead infrastructure depicted. Report specifically whether overhead electric lines are shown and whether any vertical or horizontal clearances are dimensioned for driveway/parking grades or structures in relation to overhead utilities.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided Grading Plan for \"Valley View Townhomes\", here are the findings corresponding to your requests:\n\n**1) Location of all proposed and existing contours and final grades:**\n*   **Existing contours** are depicted as dashed lines traversing the entire site (e.g., marked with elevations like 680, 681, 682). \n*   **Proposed contours** are depicted as solid lines, primarily shaping the grades around the proposed buildings (Bldg. 1 through Bldg. 8) and the central parking areas.\n*   **Final grades (spot elevations)** are marked extensively throughout the site using a cross symbol (+) with the numerical elevation adjacent to it. They are heavily concentrated at building corners, along the proposed storm drain lines, sidewalks, and throughout the driveways and parking areas (e.g., +685.29 near Bldg. 1, +683.48 near Bldg. 4, +681.50 near Bldg. 7). Finished Floor Elevations (FFE) are also provided for each building (e.g., Bldg. 1 \"FFE = 688.50\").\n\n**2) Location and identification of retaining walls:**\nRetaining walls are located primarily along the perimeter of the property and are identified with specific labels and Top of Wall (TW) / Bottom of Wall (BW) elevations:\n*   **Northeast Corner / East Boundary:** Labeled explicitly as \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\". Spot elevations are provided, such as \"TW 677.25\", \"BW 671.53\", and \"TW 681.00\". Further south along the east boundary, there is a label for an \"Existing Stone Retaining Wall\" and another \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\" with a callout \"TW 680.26\".\n*   **South Boundary:** Several segments are labeled \"Existing Retaining Wall\". Near the southwest corner, a note states \"Tie into existing Retaining Wall Match existing Wall Elevations\" and \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" with callouts like \"TW 682.23\" and \"TW 684.39\".\n\n**3) Any overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on the plan:**\n*   There are **no visible overhead electric (OHE) lines** explicitly drawn or labeled on this grading plan. \n*   The plan does identify electrical easements, such as a \"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14\" along the south and east property boundaries, and a \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 885\" at the southeast corner, but the actual overhead wires are not depicted.\n\n**4) Location of driveways and parking areas with their finished grades:**\n*   The **driveway entrance** is located on the west side of the property, connecting to Valley View Road. Spot elevations at the entrance show finished grades of +686.20, +685.60, and +685.10.\n*   The **central parking area** runs horizontally through the middle of the site between the northern buildings (Bldg. 1-4) and southern buildings (Bldg. 7-8). Finished grades are marked throughout this paved area, showing the slope (e.g., +685.20, +684.86, +683.91, +683.18, and sloping down to +681.29 in the south-central parking area).\n\n**5) Any clearance dimensions from the finished grades or structures to overhead electric lines:**\n*   There are **no vertical or horizontal clearance dimensions** provided anywhere on this plan regarding overhead electric lines, structures, or finished grades.\n\n**6) Any utility poles or overhead infrastructure depicted:**\n*   There is a \"Guy\" wire indicated near the southwest corner (often associated with stabilizing utility poles), but distinct overhead utility poles and wire infrastructure traversing the site are not illustrated on this specific grading sheet.\n\n***\n\n**Final Summary / Specific Report:**\nOverhead electric (OHE) lines are **not shown** on this grading plan. Consequently, **no vertical or horizontal clearances are dimensioned** for driveway/parking grades or structures in relation to overhead utilities on this document.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1433,"outputTokens":943,"totalTokens":4484,"reasoningTokens":2108},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2337396]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on wha