{"level":30,"time":1776370094172,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AW16qttD8x6bp4ZEUSCxut","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have gathered sufficient research. Let me synthesize the findings and evaluate each checklist item. Based on my research:\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY - WHAT WAS FOUND:**\n\n**Overhead Electric Facilities Present:**\n- Overhead electric lines shown on existing survey (Sheet 4) crossing from Valley View Road poles into the property\n- Overhead lines labeled on site plans (Sheet 9) along southern (Valley View Road) and eastern boundaries\n- Power poles noted at property edges\n- Electric easements (5') dedicated on eastern boundary\n\n**Proposed Infrastructure:**\n- Underground electric service proposed with transformer pads\n- No overhead electric facilities proposed on-site (converting to underground)\n- Proposed buildings (8 townhome complexes) positioned centrally on site, apparently away from overhead line routing\n\n**Tree Species Proposed:**\n- Live Oak (2) - NOT utility-compatible, mature height 40-80 ft\n- Cedar Elm (10) - NOT utility-compatible, mature height 40-50 ft  \n- Mexican Redbud (6) - Smaller species, status unknown\n- Texas Mountain Laurel (2) - Smaller species, status unknown\n- Mitigation trees (\"M\" category) shown near southern boundary/overhead lines but species not specified\n\n**Documentation Gaps Found:**\n- NO building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor locations and clearance dimensions\n- NO section/profile views showing vertical clearances from overhead lines to buildings, driveways, or parking\n- NO clearance dimensions marked from outdoor conductors to proposed buildings/structures on site plans\n- NO specific notation that proposed tree species are utility-compatible\n- NO 48-hour notification requirement note in