{"level":30,"time":1776370101027,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01WLZU7dBBzcq2ASXvE9gZro","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The file doesn't exist - that's fine. Let me just look at the blocks.md file again to see if there are any notes or details about clearances. Actually, I already read the blocks.md for sheet 31, and it showed that the drawing contains trees and OHE lines but no clearance zones or distance callouts.\n\nLet me now document my findings. I have solid evidence of:\n\n1. **EL-2.1 - FAIL**: Non-utility-compatible trees (or unverified compatibility) within 15 feet of OHE\n   - Trees at southern boundary: 0 feet distance\n   - Trees at northern boundary: 0.5 feet distance\n\n2. **EL-2.3 - FAIL/NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Large trees (need to verify mature height) within 25 feet of OHE\n   - Trees at southern boundary appear large based on symbol size\n\n3. **EL-2.6 - FAIL**: Trees within 10 feet of poles\n   - Northern boundary trees: 0.5 feet from OHE line (which indicates proximity to poles)\n\n4. **EL-2.10 - Need to verify**: Plant legend/schedule completeness\n   - Sheet 35 shows complete plant list with scientific names\n\n5. **EL-2.11 - FAIL**: Large trees not differentiated on landscape plan\n   - Vision analysis showed trees are marked by category (SY, PL, P, M) but not by size (>40 ft)\n\n6. **EL-2.12 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: No dimension lines showing clearances from conductors\n   - Sheet 31 has no dimension callouts for clearances\n\n7. **EL-2.13 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: No dimension lines showing clearances from tree trunks\n   - Same as above\n\n8. **EL-2.14 - FAIL**: Trees not properly shown relative to OHE facilities\n   - While trees and OHE are shown, no clearance verification is possible without measurements\n   - No legend or notes indicating how clearances comply with requirements\n\n9. **EL-2.15 - FAIL**: No documented Austin Energy written approval for trees in prohibited zones\n   - Master comment report references Austin Energy review link, but no approval documentation visible\n\nI need to verify the utility compatibility and mature height of the proposed species to complete this analysis. Based on standard horticultural knowledge, Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) is a large native tree reaching 40-80 feet at maturity and is not utility-compatible, Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) is medium-large at 35-50 feet and likely not utility-compatible, and Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) and Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) are smaller species at 20-30 feet that may be utility-compatible. However, the plans don't document utility compatibility status at all, which represents another deficiency regardless of what Appendix F specifies. I should compile my findings now and determine the status for each checklist item.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":779,"cache_read_input_tokens":71729,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":779},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f35260c3-5e1a-4786-b2cb-3f3a59e76a22","uuid":"309c4a82-243c-4c40-a162-5301012cbf2c"}
