{"level":30,"time":1776370123576,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Review the site plan drawing carefully and look for:\n1. Any dimension callouts or annotations showing clearances between buildings and the overhead electric lines (marked OHE)\n2. Any clearance dimensions between driveways/parking and overhead lines\n3. Any profile or section views embedded in the plan view showing vertical clearances\n4. Any specific notations about electric line clearances near buildings or parking\n5. Whether dimensions are shown measured from the outside conductor or from the utility pole\n\nReport what clearance dimensions are visible, if any, and how they are measured (from conductor vs. pole).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a thorough visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here are the findings regarding your specific questions about overhead electric line (OHE) clearances:\n\n1. **Dimension callouts or annotations showing clearances between buildings and the overhead electric lines:**\n   There are no visible dimension lines, callouts, or annotations indicating clearances between the proposed buildings and the overhead electric lines. While an \"-OHE-\" line is visible running along the bottom (street side), left, and right boundaries of the property, the only dimensions provided in relation to the buildings are standard property line setbacks (e.g., 20.0' or 25.0' from the property boundary). \n\n2. **Clearance dimensions between driveways/parking and overhead lines:**\n   There are no vertical or horizontal clearance dimensions provided between the driveways/parking areas and the overhead electric lines. The \"-OHE-\" line is clearly depicted crossing over both proposed driveway entrances at the bottom of the plan, but no clearance heights or distances are annotated at these intersections.\n\n3. **Profile or section views embedded in the plan view showing vertical clearances:**\n   There are no profile views, cross-sections, or elevation diagrams embedded on this page that show vertical clearances to overhead electric lines. The plan is strictly a top-down, 2D site layout (with some embedded tables and a lighting fixture detail).\n\n4. **Specific notations about electric line clearances near buildings or parking:**\n   There are no specific notations regarding required clearances for electric lines near buildings or parking. The only note mentioning electric utilities is found in the **Site Plan Release Notes** (Note 4), which states exactly: \n   *\"Additional electric easements may be required at a later date.\"*\n   There is no mention of safety clearances, setbacks from conductors, or height restrictions.\n\n5. **Whether dimensions are shown measured from the outside conductor or from the utility pole:**\n   Because there are no clearance dimensions provided on this drawing, it is not possible to determine the measurement methodology (conductor vs. pole) from this page.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1428,"outputTokens":426,"totalTokens":3499,"reasoningTokens":1645},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain conten