andscape planting locations relative to the overhead electric lines:**\n*   There are several proposed trees placed in very close proximity to, or directly underneath, the **\"- OHE -\"** routing along the southern boundary of the site. Specifically, there are at least four prominent tree canopy circles drawn directly over or immediately adjacent to the OHE line.\n\n**4) Tree species identified (check if any are non-utility-compatible species placed near overhead lines):**\n*   The trees placed near the overhead electric lines are tagged with the letter **\"M\"**.\n*   According to the legend located below the \"KEY NOTES,\" the symbol **\"M\"** corresponds to **\"MITIGATION TREE\"**.\n*   **Specific botanical or common species names (e.g., Oak, Elm, Crepe Myrtle) are NOT provided** on this sheet. Because the actual plant species are not identified in a plant schedule on this page, it is impossible to determine from this document alone whether these proposed \"Mitigation Trees\" are non-utility-compatible species.\n\n**5) Any clearance dimensions from trees, landscaping, or structures to the overhead electric lines:**\n*   **No clearance dimensions are annotated.** There are no visible dimension lines or callouts indicating the required or proposed horizontal or vertical clearance distances between the proposed trees and the overhead electric lines.\n\n**6) Whether tree species comply with utility-compatible requirements for placement within clearance zones:**\n*   Compliance cannot be verified from this sheet. As noted above, the specific tree species are not identified (only categorized generically as \"MITIGATION TREE\"), and clearance dimensions are absent. Therefore, a determination of utility compatibility cannot be made based solely on this page of the submission.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1438,"outputTokens":546,"totalTokens":4235,"reasoningTokens":2251},"warnings":[],"providerMetada