{"level":30,"time":1776370144641,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"This is the landscape plan. Please read and transcribe ALL text notes, annotations, and legend items visible on this sheet, specifically:\n\n1. What does the entire \"KEY NOTES\" section say? List every single item (H-1, H-2, H-3, etc.) and their full definitions.\n\n2. What text appears under the tree designation codes (M, SY, PL, P, etc.)? Provide the complete text for each code definition.\n\n3. Are there any NOTES sections that discuss utility clearances, tree spacing, utility conflicts, or coordination with utility companies? If so, provide the exact text.\n\n4. What does the IRRIGATION NOTES section say?\n\n5. Look at the title block area - what information is shown there (project name, sheet title, scale, date, etc.)?\n\n6. Are there any asterisks, footnotes, or special symbols that might indicate required clearances or modifications?\n\nPlease transcribe the exact text for all of these items so I have accurate information about what the designer specified regarding utilities and trees.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan sheet, here is the exact transcription of the requested elements:\n\n### 1. \"KEY NOTES\" Section\nLocated in the top right corner, below the title \"KEY NOTES:\":\n\n*   **H-1:** PROPOSED PAVING\n*   **H-2:** STREET YARD\n*   **H-3:** STREET YARD LANDSCAPING\n*   **H-4:** PARKING LOT LANDSCAPING\n*   **H-5:** PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE\n*   **H-6:** WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE *(Note: Symbol shown is a line with an \"X\")*\n*   **H-7:** SOD\n\n### 2. Tree Designation Codes\nLocated immediately below the Key Notes section:\n\n*   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n*   **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n\n### 3. Utilities, Tree Spacing, and Conflicts Notes\nThere are **no notes** in the provided text blocks (IRRIGATION NOTES, NOTE, or KEY NOTES) that explicitly discuss utility clearances, tree spacing requirements, utility conflicts, or coordination with utility companies.\n\n*(Note: While utility lines such as \"OHE\" (Overhead Electric) and \"SD\" (Storm Drain) are drawn and labeled on the plan itself, there is no accompanying text outlining clearance rules or coordination on this specific sheet).*\n\n### 4. \"IRRIGATION NOTES\" Section\nLocated in the top left corner, under the heading \"IRRIGATION NOTES:\":\n\n\"AUTOMATIC IRRIGATION SYSTEMS SHALL COMPLY WITH TCEQ CHAPTER 344, AS WELL AS THE FOLLOWING REQUIREMENTS:\n\n1. THESE REQUIREMENTS SHALL BE NOTED ON THE SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT AND SHALL BE IMPLEMENTED AS PART OF THE LANDSCAPE INSPECTION:\na. THE SYSTEM MUST PROVIDE A MOISTURE LEVEL ADEQUATE TO SUSTAIN GROWTH OF THE PLANT MATERIALS;\nb. THE SYSTEM DOES NOT INCLUDE SPRAY IRRIGATION ON AREAS LESS THAN TEN (10) FEET WIDE (SUCH AS MEDIANS, BUFFER STRIPS, AND PARKING LOT ISLANDS);\nc. CIRCUIT REMOTE CONTROL VALVES HAVE ADJUSTABLE FLOW CONTROLS;\nd. SERVICEABLE IN-HEAD CHECK VALVES ARE ADJACENT TO PAVED AREAS WHERE ELEVATION DIFFERENCES MAY CAUSE LOW HEAD DRAINAGE;\ne. A MASTER VALVE INSTALLED ON THE DISCHARGE SIDE OF THE BACKFLOW PREVENTER;\nf. ABOVE-GROUND IRRIGATION EMISSION DEVICES ARE SET BACK AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES FROM IMPERVIOUS SURFACES;\ng. AN AUTOMATIC RAIN SHUT-OFF DEVICE SHUTS OFF THE IRRIGATION SYSTEM AUTOMATICALLY AFTER MORE THAN A ONE-HALF INCH (1/2\") RAINFALL; AND\nh. NEWLY PLANTED TREES SHALL HAVE PERMANENT IRRIGATION CONSISTING OF DRIP OR BUBBLERS.\n\n2. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL DEVELOP AND PROVIDE AN AS-BUILT DESIGN PLAN TO THE CITY AT THE TIME THE FINAL IRRIGATION INSPECTION IS PERFORMED.\na. UNLESS FISCAL SECURITY IS PROVIDED TO THE CITY FOR THE INSTALLATION OF THE SYSTEM, IT MUST BE OPERATIONAL AT THE TIME OF THE FINAL LANDSCAPE INSPECTION.\n\n3. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL ALSO PROVIDE EXHIBITS TO BE PERMANENTLY INSTALLED INSIDE OR ATTACHED TO THE IRRIGATION CONTROLLER, INCLUDING:\na. A LAMINATED COPY OF THE WATER BUDGET CONTAINING ZONE NUMBERS, PRECIPITATION RATE, GALLONS PER MINUTE AND THE LOCATION OF THE ISOLATION VALVE; AND AN AS-BUILT PLAN.\n\n4. THE IRRIGATION INSTALLER SHALL PROVIDE A REPORT TO THE CITY ON A FORM PROVIDED BY AUSTIN WATER CERTIFYING COMPLIANCE WITH SUBSECTION 1. WHEN THE FINAL PLUMBING INSPECTION IS PERFORMED BY THE CITY.\"\n\n### 5. Title Block Information\nLocated in the rightmost column, reading from top to bottom:\n\n*   **Company Logo:** BLU FISH COLLABORATIVE Landscape Architecture\n*   **Address/Contact:** 107 Leland Street, Suite 2, Austin, TX 78704 / P.O. BOX 40792, Austin, TX 78704 / Phone: (512) 380-4115\n*   **Professional Seal:** Seal of Stephen H. Spears, Landscape Architect, State of Texas.\n*   **DATE SEALED:** 02/13/2020\n*   **PROJECT NAME:** VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\n*   **OWNER:** WM 41 AUSTIN RE, LLC\n*   **PROJECT LOCATION:** 3759 VALLEY VIEW ROAD, AUSTIN, TEXAS 78704\n*   **REVISIONS:** *(The table is blank)*\n*   **PROJECT #:** 019-25-01\n*   **ORIGINAL ISSUE:** 02/13/2020\n*   **DRAWING TITLE:** LANDSCAPE PLAN\n*   **NORTH:** *(Upward pointing arrow)*\n*   **SCALE IN FEET:** (1\"=20'-0\") *(Includes graphic bar scale showing 0, 10, 20, 50)*\n*   **SHEET NO.:** 28 of 35\n\n### 6. Asterisks, Footnotes, or Special Symbols\nThere are **no asterisks or footnotes** on this sheet that indicate required utility clearances.\n\nHowever, there is an additional general **\"NOTE:\"** section located in the top middle of the page detailing elevation and soil modifications. While not related to utilities, it is transcribed here for completeness:\n\n\"NOTE:\nFINISHED ELEVATION FOR PARKING LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED PARKING LOT ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL. [LDC 25-2-1007(F)(4)]\n\nIF ESTABLISHING VEGETATION DURING ANY STAGE OF A DROUGHT, SECTION 6-4-30 MAY REQUIRE A VARIANCE, CONTACT AUSTIN WATER STAFF AT WATERUSECOMPLIANCE@AUSTINTEXAS.GOV OR CALL (512) 974-2199.\n\nSUPPLEMENTAL IRRIGATION IS REQUIRED FOR NEWLY PLANTED, REQUIRED LANDSCAPE PLANTS PER LDC 25-2-1008, ECM 2.4.6, AND ECM APPENDIX B.\n\nFOR PARKING LOT ISLANDS, MEDIANS, PENINSULAS, AND SIMILAR LANDSCAPE AREAS THAT ARE TO RECEIVE PARKING LOT STORMWATER RUNOFF, FINISHED ELEVATION MUST BE AT LEAST SIX (6) INCHES BELOW THE FINISHED CURB ELEVATION TO ALLOW FOR PLACEMENT OF SIX (6) INCHES OF TOPSOIL [ECM 1.6.7]\"","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1529,"outputTokens":1474,"totalTokens":5658,"reasoningTokens":2655},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisel