inimal mature height) for areas near OHE\n   - Install physical barriers or management plans if relocation is not feasible\n\n5. **Check for Amendments:** Determine if revisions or amendments to this landscape plan have been issued since the February 2020 seal date to address utility clearance conflicts\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table: Southern Boundary Trees vs. OHE Line\n\n| Location | Tree Label | Trunk Distance from OHE | Canopy Diameter | Overlap Status | Compliance Risk |\n|----------|-----------|------------------------|-----------------|----------------|-----------------|\n| Southeast 1 | M | 2-5 feet | 20-25 ft | YES | HIGH |\n| Southeast 2 | M | 0-2 feet | 20-25 ft | YES | CRITICAL |\n| Central/SW areas | H.4, H.7, other | Variable | 15-25 ft | LIKELY | HIGH |\n\n---\n\nThis analysis reveals significant potential compliance gaps with Austin Energy tree clearance standards along the southern OHE line. Further detailed review of Sheet 32 (Tree List) and Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan) is necessary to complete a full compliance assessment."}],"totalDurationMs":1453804,"totalTokens":26348,"totalToolUseCount":7,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2145,"cache_read_input_tokens":22096,"output_tokens":2103,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2145},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
