{"level":30,"time":1776370178301,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan drawing and identify:\n1. Any proposed fences near the property boundaries where overhead electric lines (OHE) exist\n2. Retaining walls and their proximity to overhead lines\n3. Water meter locations shown on the plan (usually near building service connections)\n4. Driveway and parking locations relative to overhead electric lines\n5. Trash/dumpster enclosures near overhead lines\n6. Any temporary or permanent poles, signs, or light fixtures\n\nBe specific about locations (north, south, east, west edges) and describe what you see.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan for Valley View Townhomes, here are the observations regarding the requested items:\n\n**1. Proposed fences near property boundaries where overhead electric lines (OHE) exist:**\n*   **Overhead Electric Lines (OHE):** Lines labeled `--OHE--` run along or near all four main property boundaries (North, South, East, and West).\n*   **Fences near OHE:**\n    *   **East Boundary:** A line labeled \"Wood Fence\" runs along the eastern property boundary, directly parallel and in close proximity to the eastern `--OHE--` line.\n    *   **North Boundary:** A \"Pond Perimeter Fence\" is located around the Detention Pond in the north/northeast section of the site, situated somewhat near the northern `--OHE--` line.\n    *   **Southeast Corner:** The \"Wood Fence\" label appears again near the southeast corner, adjacent to both the eastern and southern `--OHE--` lines.\n\n**2. Retaining walls and their proximity to overhead lines:**\n*   **East Boundary:** There are multiple retaining walls running along the eastern property line, very close to and directly under the path of the eastern `--OHE--` line. Specific labels include \"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\" (multiple instances) and \"Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n*   **South Boundary:** A retaining wall runs parallel to the southern property line, in close proximity to the southern `--OHE--` line. It is marked with labels indicating \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\" and \"End Concrete Retaining Wall / Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n*   **North Boundary:** There is a \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" forming part of the Detention Pond structure in the north, relatively close to the northern `--OHE--` line.\n\n**3. Water meter locations shown on the plan:**\n*   **Northwest Corner:** A specific callout for \"Water Meter\" is located in the extreme northwest corner of the drawing area (top left), near the intersection/street edge. It points to a small circular symbol near other utility markers like \"Gas Meter\" and \"Wastewater Service Connection\".\n\n**4. Driveway and parking locations relative to overhead electric lines:**\n*   **West Driveway:** The primary entrance on the west side, labeled \"Construct Type III Driveway\", is crossed directly by the `--OHE--` line running roughly parallel to the western boundary.\n*   **Southwest Driveway:** There is a secondary entrance at the southwest corner, also labeled \"Construct Type III Driveway\". The `--OHE--` line running along the southern boundary crosses directly over this driveway entrance.\n*   **Parking:** Surface parking spaces located near the western entrance (near Building 1 and the driveway) are situated closely to the western `--OHE--` line, which appears to pass directly over or immediately adjacent to that parking area.\n\n**5. Trash/dumpster enclosures near overhead lines:**\n*   There are no dedicated, large communal dumpster or trash enclosures visually identified on the site plan drawing itself near the property boundaries or overhead lines.\n*   A \"Trash Collection Notes\" section is present in the lower center, which states: \"Trash containers shall not be left at curb side unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside...\" This suggests the use of individual rollout carts rather than a permanent enclosure.\n\n**6. Any temporary or permanent poles, signs, or light fixtures:**\n*   **Poles:** Small circular symbols at the vertices and along the paths of the `--OHE--` lines indicate the presence of permanent utility poles supporting these lines along the north, south, east, and west perimeters.\n*   **Signs:**\n    *   A \"Road End Sign\" is labeled in the far northwest corner, outside the main property line.\n    *   A \"Stop Sign\" is labeled pointing to a location near the exit lane of the main western driveway.\n*   **Light Fixtures:** While there is a \"Lighting Note\" and \"Figure 34\" illustrating \"Examples of Fully-Shielded Light Fixtures\" in the bottom left, specific proposed light pole locations are not clearly marked with standard distinct lighting symbols across the main site plan drawing.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1427,"outputTokens":913,"totalTokens":4296,"reasoningTokens":1956},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, l