ng or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside...\" This suggests the use of individual rollout carts rather than a permanent enclosure.\n\n**6. Any temporary or permanent poles, signs, or light fixtures:**\n*   **Poles:** Small circular symbols at the vertices and along the paths of the `--OHE--` lines indicate the presence of permanent utility poles supporting these lines along the north, south, east, and west perimeters.\n*   **Signs:**\n    *   A \"Road End Sign\" is labeled in the far northwest corner, outside the main property line.\n    *   A \"Stop Sign\" is labeled pointing to a location near the exit lane of the main western driveway.\n*   **Light Fixtures:** While there is a \"Lighting Note\" and \"Figure 34\" illustrating \"Examples of Fully-Shielded Light Fixtures\" in the bottom left, specific proposed light pole locations are not clearly marked with standard distinct lighting symbols across the main site plan drawing."}]}
