77","sheetNumber":38}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining walls' maintenance of minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outermost electric line cannot be verified. Sheet 38 shows wall plan and locations, but dimension annotations from conductors to wall faces are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Retaining walls around site perimeter and detention pond"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":38},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":39}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Retaining wall section exhibits lack dimension annotations from outer electric conductor to outermost edge of walls for clearance verification. Sheets 38 and 39 show wall details and sections, but no dimensions showing clearances from surveyed overhead conductor locations to wall faces are provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed driveways, parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways do not show documented minimum 16-foot vertical clearance (parking without truck traffic) or 18-foot vertical clearance (areas with truck traffic) from lowest point of overhead electric facilities. No surveyed mid-span clearance data or registered surveyor documentation is provided showing conductor heights above proposed driveway grades."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Vehicle parking areas on concrete pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Vertical clearance from vehicles parked or displayed on concrete pads to lowest overhead electric lines cannot be verified, and no requirement note is shown on site plans. Parking areas are shown on site plan, but no section views document minimum vertical clearance (12 feet for residential pedestrian areas, 16 feet for parking without trucks, 18 feet with truck traffic) from overhead lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site plan, areas with overhead electric line routing"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Clearance dimensions are not provided on plans with sufficient clarity to verify whether they are measured from utility pole centerline or from the outside conductor. While overhead electric lines are shown on sheets, no dimension lines with annotations are visible indicating the measurement origin point (conductor vs. pole centerline). Without dimensioned clearances from identified outside conductors, compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings and site features in electric easement areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Customer facilities within electric easement boundaries lack documented clearances to ensure they maintain minimum 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductors. Site plan shows 5' Electric Easements on eastern boundary, but no section views or dimension annotations demonstrate that site features (buildings, utilities, structures) within or adjacent to these easements maintain required clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meters' maintenance of minimum 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor of existing overhead electric service drops cannot be verified. Water meter locations are not clearly identified on utility plans with dimension annotations from overhead service-drop conductor locations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Buildings 1-8, driveways, overhead electric facility locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":4},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Survey by registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span clearances is not provided. The existing survey shows overhead electric lines at the property edges, but proposed building finished floor elevations and driveway grades must be verified against mid-span overhead conductor elevations. Without registered surveyor documentation of conductor heights and mid-span clearance data, vertical clearances from buildings and driveways to overhead lines cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape areas near overhead electric lines on southern and eastern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed trees are not verified to be from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list per ECM Appendix F. The landscape plan proposes 10 Cedar Elm (mature height 40-50 ft) and 2 Live Oak (mature height 40-80 ft) as primary shade trees—both are large-canopy species that are NOT utility-compatible. Large mitigation trees (marked 'M') are shown adjacent to the southern property boundary where overhead electric lines are located; their species are not identified on the plan. There is no notation verifying that proposed trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution lines are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformers' maintenance of minimum 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance from overhead electric lines cannot be verified. Sheet 21 shows transformer pad locations, but no section views document vertical clearance dimensions from overhead line conductors to top of transformer equipment."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet or general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines as required by Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. While a pre-construction safety meeting requirement for transmission facilities is noted, no 48-hour notification requirement note for work near distribution line facilities is present on cover sheet or general notes."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"5622c455-f8b9-47e2-881f-2325439bed62"}
{"level":30,"time":1776370305405,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01RoSFZe2z5FZmy3oU9VPSEp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I have very specific information about site features near overhead lines:\n\n**Site Features Near Overhead Electric Lines:**\n1. **Fences:**\n   - Wood fence along eastern boundary near OHE line\n   - Pond perimeter fence near northern OHE line\n   - Wood fence at southeast corner near OHE lines\n\n2. **Retaining Walls:**\n   - Multiple retaining walls along eastern boundary directly under OHE line\n   - Retaining wall along southern boundary near OHE line\n   - Concrete retaining wall forming detention pond structure\n\n3. **Driveways:**\n   - Primary (west) driveway crosses OHE line\n   - Secondary (southwest) driveway crosses OHE line\n\n4. **Parking:**\n   - Surface parking spaces near western entrance, close to OHE line\n\n5. **Water Meter:**\n   - Located in northwest corner near other utilities\n\n6. **Utilities:**\n   - Gas meter shown\n   - Wastewater service connection shown\n\n7. **Poles:**\n   - Utility poles along all four boundaries supporting OHE lines\n\n8. **Signs:**\n   - Road End Sign (outside property)\n   - Stop Sign near western driveway exit\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n\nNow let me go through the checklist systematically:\n\n1. **EL-1.1** - Buildings and clearance from overhead conductors:\n   - Multiple buildings shown near overhead lines\n   - No 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance dimensions shown\n   - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (no dimensions shown)\n\n2. **EL-1.2** - Customer facilities and 15-foot radial clearance:\n   - Buildings are customer facilities\n   - No 15-foot radial clearance shown\n   - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (no dimensions shown)\n\n3. **EL-1.3** - Building projections clearances:\n   - Elevation views would be needed to assess overhangs, awnings, or balconies, but none are provided\n   - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (no elevation sheets provided)\n\n4. **EL-1.4** - Gas pump canopies:\n   - No gas pumps shown on site plan\n   - **Status: N/A** (not applicable to this project)\n\n5. **EL-1.5** - Elevated walkways/platforms:\n   - No elevated structures identified on the plans\n   - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (architectural plans would clarify, but site plan shows none)\n\n6. **EL-1.6** - Buildings in ROW adjacent to site:\n   - Buildings are positioned near right-of-way with overhead lines present\n   - Clearance distances from ROW facilities cannot be confirmed\n   - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (dimensions from ROW overhead lines to buildings are missing)\n\n7. **EL-1.7** - Surveyed elevations/locations of overhead conductors on building elevations:\n   - Building elevation sheets are absent from the submission\n   - **Status: FAIL** (required element missing - no building elevations with surveyed conductor data)\n\n8. **EL-1.8** - Section and plan exhibits with dimensions from conductor:\n   - These exhibits are not included\n   - **Status: FAIL** (required element missing)\n\n9. **EL-1.9** - Fences and 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance:\n   - Wood fences run along the east boundary near the OHE line, and a pond perimeter fence is shown at the north boundary near the OHE line\n   - Clearance verification is incomplete because specific dimensions are not annotated, making it impossible to confirm the required 7.5-foot clearances. Items 10-13 address additional fence-related requirements: fence posts must maintain 10-foot clearance from utility poles, fencing near transmission lines requires material specifications and grounding details, and vehicle barriers need proper design documentation—all of which lack the necessary dimensional or specification data on the current plans. plan, with sections detailed on Sheet 38 (Wall Plan Details), but these sections lack overhead electric conductor elevations or clearance data needed for verification. The retaining walls shown on the east and south boundaries don't include the conductor elevation information required to confirm compliance.\n\nFor the driveways crossing overhead lines on the west and southwest, no vertical clearance dimensions are provided from ground level to the lines. Similarly, parking areas positioned near the western overhead line lack any clearance notes or dimensions to verify the required heights. Roads beneath transmission lines also lack the necessary clearance documentation.\n\nElectric poles positioned along and potentially crossing driveway areas have no relocation notes visible on the plans, making it unclear whether conflicts exist or if any relocation has been documented. Additionally, since no clearance dimensions appear anywhere on the plans, I cannot determine whether measurements are taken from poles or conductors, or verify compliance with any clearance standards.\n\nProposed light pole locations aren't clearly marked on the site plan, so I'm unable to assess whether streetlights would be positioned under overhead lines. Sidewalks are shown adjacent to utility poles at property edges, but without specific dimensions between them, I cannot verify adequate clearance. The plan indicates individual rollout carts rather than a permanent trash enclosure structure, so this item doesn't apply to the project.\n\nA key distinction emerges with the facilities prohibition—parking and driveways are depicted crossing overhead distribution lines, and I need to determine whether these fall within the transmission easement where such facilities are explicitly prohibited. Water infrastructure presents similar verification gaps: the meter location in the northwest corner is shown near overhead lines without documented clearance measurements, and water line routing relative to distribution lines lacks the necessary dimensional data to confirm compliance.\n\nThe survey requirements reveal a critical deficiency—while benchmark data exists on the plans, the specific pole location coordinates and mid-span clearance measurements that a registered surveyor should provide are absent entirely. Overhead line crossings at driveways cannot be verified as perpendicular without dimensional notation or clear angle marking on the plans. Foundation setbacks from property lines would require detailed analysis against the boundary, which the current documentation doesn't support.\n\nFor secondary versus primary line designation, there's no voltage labeling to differentiate line types. Marquee signage and new poles for underground conversion don't apply to this project. Decorative lighting fixtures are referenced in notes but their exact positions and clearances beneath overhead conductors aren't clearly delineated. Trees present a notable gap—while existing vegetation and proposed plantings appear on the landscape plan near the OHE line, there are no clearance dimensions from tree canopies to conductors, and no confirmation that species selections meet utility compatibility standards for the 10-foot distribution and 50-foot transmission setback requirements.\n\nThe water meter in the northwest corner shows no apparent obstructions in plan view, though specific access clearance dimensions aren't documented. Streetlight locations aren't clearly identified on the site plan, making it impossible to verify development clearances from existing fixtures. Guy wire symbols appear near poles with transmission notes referencing guy wire structures, but their spatial relationship to accessible paths and driveways requires further clarification.\n\n41. **EL-1.41** - Guy easements for angled guy anchors:\n    - Transmission lines exist (per notes on Sheet 3)\n    - No separate guy easement diagram shown (beyond transmission easement noted)\n    - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (specific guy easement boundaries not documented)\n\n42. **EL-1.42** - Down guy anchor easements:\n    - Down guy anchors may exist with transmission poles\n    - No dedicated easement diagram for down guys\n    - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (down guy anchor easements not documented)\n\n43. **EL-1.43** - Transformers vertical clearance from overhead lines:\n    - Proposed pad\n\n-mounted transformers shown on electrical design plan (Sheet 21)\n    - No section views showing vertical clearance to overhead lines\n    - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (no vertical clearance dimension)\n\n44. **EL-1.44** - Transformers in niche configurations:\n    - No niche service configurations shown\n    - **Status: N/A** (not applicable)\n\n45. **EL-1.45** - Construction staging clearances from overhead lines:\n    - No construction logistics plan provided\n    - Cannot verify 10-foot radial clearance from overhead lines during construction\n    - **Status: NOT VERIFIABLE** (construction logistics plan not provided)\n\n46. **EL-1.46** - 48-hour notification note requirement:\n    - Plan notes reference Austin Energy and transmission requirements\n    - The Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3 state: \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction\". The requirement exists in the transmission notes but lacks sufficient visibility on the cover sheet or general notes for contractor awareness. **Status: NEED TO VERIFY**\n\n47. **EL-1.47** - Service mast through-roof installations:\n    - No roof-mounted service masts identified on the landscape/site plan\n    - Building elevation sheets are absent, making verification impossible\n    - **Status: N/A or NOT VERIFIABLE** (building elevations not provided)\n\nNow determining which items constitute FAIL versus NOT VERIFIABLE:\n\n**FAIL items (missing required elements):**\n- EL-1.7: Building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor locations absent\n- EL-1.8: Section and plan exhibits with clearance dimensions from conductor missing\n\n**NOT VERIFIABLE items (clearances may exist but cannot be confirmed from available plans):**\n- EL-1.17: Retaining wall sections lack overhead conductor elevation data needed for clearance verification\n- EL-1.31: Surveyor mid-span clearance data not provided\n- EL-1.37: Trees positioned near overhead lines missing clearance verification and species identification\n- EL-1.1 through EL-1.20: Various clearance dimensions (building radial, fence sky-to-ground, fence post-to-pole, retaining wall, driveway, parking, transmission vertical) not dimensioned on plans\n- EL-1.12: Transmission fence material and grounding specifications absent\n- EL-1.23: Clearance measurement methodology cannot be assessed from submitted documents\n- EL-1.25, EL-1.28, EL-1.29: Sidewalk/pole, water meter, and water line clearances not dimensioned\n- EL-1.40: Down guy conflicts not documented\n- EL-1.43: Transformer vertical clearances not dimensioned\n- EL-1.45: Construction staging clearances not addressed\n- EL-1.46: 48-hour notification requirement needs verification for contractor clarity\n\n**N/A items:**\nNo building projections, gas pump canopies, elevated walkways, substations, vehicle barrier fences, emergency access structures, or highway/freeway conditions identified in the project scope.\n\nThe remaining items—no permanent trash enclosure, marquee signs, new power poles for underground conversion, niche transformer configuration, or roof service masts—don't apply to this site. For EL-1.38, visual obstruction doesn't appear to be a concern given the site conditions.\n\nRegarding EL-1.46, the grouping file specifies this notification is required when overhead electric lines exist on or adjacent to the site and construction activities are proposed. Both conditions are met here—overhead lines are present and construction is planned. The transmission notes reference this requirement, but I need to confirm whether it's stated clearly enough in the general notes or cover sheet for the contractor to understand their obligation.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3809,"cache_read_input_tokens":73367,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3809},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4842cd33-4ac7-488e-aa08-33032c2696e2","uuid":"3be5920a-f227-4135-a038-98afbd6b6974"}
