{"level":30,"time":1776370305407,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":32,"prompt":"Examine the tree list and identify: 1) All tree species listed with their ID numbers or callouts; 2) Any designation or flag indicating whether trees are \"UC\" (utility-compatible) or standard species; 3) Specifically, identify any mitigation trees (labeled \"M\") and their species, particularly those in the southern landscape area near the overhead electric line; 4) Tree sizes/caliper sizes noted; 5) Any notes indicating utility compatibility or placement restrictions. Report the complete tree species list with their utility compatibility status.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a close visual analysis of the provided \"SURVEYED TREES\" table (Sheet 29 of 35, titled \"TREE LIST\"), here are the precise findings corresponding to your requests. \n\n*Note: This document appears to be an inventory of **existing** surveyed trees on the site, rather than a proposed planting plan. Consequently, several of the designations you asked to identify (which are typically found on proposed planting lists) are not present on this specific page.*\n\n### 1) & 4) Tree Species Listed with ID Numbers and Sizes\nBelow is the exact transcription of the \"TREE NO.\", \"TREE INCHES\", and \"TREE SPECIES\" columns for every tree listed in the table:\n\n| TREE NO. | TREE INCHES | TREE SPECIES |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| 143 | 12 | Live Oak |\n| 144 | 14 | Live Oak |\n| 145 | 20 | China Berry |\n| 4001 | 15 | Live Oak |\n| 4002 | 9, 14 | China Berry |\n| 4003 | 12 | China Berry |\n| 4004 | 12 | China Berry |\n| 4008 | 11 | Hackberry |\n| 4009 | 18 | Hackberry |\n| 4010 | 17 | Cedar Elm |\n| 4011 | 9 | Hackberry |\n| 4012 | 13 | Unknown |\n| 4013 | 9 | Poplar |\n| 4014 | 30 | China Berry |\n| 4015 | 24 | Pecan |\n| 4016 | 15 | China Berry |\n| 4017 | 10 | China Berry |\n| 4018 | 32 | Live Oak |\n| 4019 | 42 | Live Oak |\n| 4020 | 10 | Hackberry |\n| 4021 | 13 | Hackberry |\n| 4022 | 27 | American Elm |\n| 4023 | 11 | Poplar |\n| 4024 | 8 | Hackberry |\n| 4025 | 14 | Cedar Elm |\n| 4026 | 36 | Live Oak |\n| 4027 | 27 | Live Oak |\n| 4028 | 20 | Live Oak |\n| 4029 | 16 | Hackberry |\n| 4030a | 15 | Live Oak |\n| 4030b | 18 | Live Oak |\n| 4031 | 14 | Hackberry |\n| 4032 | 19.5 | Cedar Elm |\n| 4033 | 11 | Arizona Ash |\n| 4034 | 18 | Live Oak |\n| 4035 | 24 | China Berry |\n| 4036 | 15 | Arizona Ash |\n| 4037 | 10 | Pecan |\n| 4038 | 24 | Live Oak |\n| 4039 | 20 | Live Oak |\n| 4040 | 14 | Bradford Pear |\n| 4041 | 13 | Arizona Ash |\n| 4042 | 11 | Arizona Ash |\n| 4043 | 16 | Live Oak |\n| 4044 | 19 | Live Oak |\n| 4045 | 20.5 | Live Oak |\n| 4046 | 14 | Live Oak |\n| 4047 | 16 | Pine |\n\n### 2) Designation or Flag Indicating \"UC\" (Utility-Compatible)\n**Not Present.** There are no columns, flags, notes, or designations anywhere on this page indicating whether the surveyed trees are \"UC\" (utility-compatible) or standard species. \n\n### 3) Mitigation Trees Labeled \"M\" and their Locations\n**Not Present.** There are no trees labeled with an \"M\" in the \"TREE NO.\" column or species list. Furthermore, this table contains no location data (such as \"southern landscape area\" or references to an \"overhead electric line\"). \n\n*Contextual Note:* The table does contain a column titled \"**PROPOSED MITIGATION**\" (with numerical values like `0.00`, `0.50`, `1.00`, `1.5`, `3.00`) and a large section titled \"**REQUIRED TREE MITIGATION**\" containing calculations based on inches removed. However, it does not list proposed replacement/mitigation planting trees, which is typically where an \"M\" identifier would be used.\n\n### 5) Notes Indicating Utility Compatibility or Placement Restrictions\n**Not Present.** There are no notes on this document discussing utility compatibility or placement restrictions. \n\nThe only note provided on this page is located at the bottom left, which reads exactly:\n`* TREE SURVEY PROVIDED BY`\n`SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC.`\n`SURVEY DATE: 03/28/2023`","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1423,"outputTokens":1203,"totalTokens":5213,"reasoningTokens":2587},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1495484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the tree list and identify: 1) All tree species listed with their ID numbers or callouts; 2) Any designation or flag indicating whether trees are \"UC\" (utility-compatible) or standard species; 3) Specifically, identify any mitigation trees (labe