{"level":30,"time":1776370329462,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QdRMtiEmJHsNYhG9pTjizD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive analysis of the site plans, I have gathered sufficient evidence to evaluate the checklist items. Let me compile the findings:\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY:**\n\n**Infrastructure Present:**\n- Overhead Electric (OHE) lines shown on Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) running along entire southern property boundary\n- Distribution voltage (no transmission easement identified; facts.md shows 5-foot electric easements)\n- No transmission lines or transmission easement documented\n- Underground electric infrastructure shown on Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) - transformers, pull boxes\n\n**Tree Documentation:**\n- Proposed trees per Plant Schedule (Sheet 35):\n  - 10 Cedar Elm (ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA) - 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' height at installation\n  - 2 Live Oak (QUERCUS VIRGINIANA) - 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' height at installation\n  - 6 Mexican Redbud - 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL., 10' height at installation\n  - 2 Texas Mountain Laurel - 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL., 8' height at installation\n- Mature heights NOT provided on plant schedule (these are installation heights, not mature heights)\n- Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) shows tree locations with symbols (M, SY, PL, P) but NO SPECIES LABELS\n- Agent analysis revealed mitigation trees (\"M\") in southeastern corner located 0-5 feet from OHE line\n\n**Critical Findings:**\n- Trees are proposed within 0-5 feet of overhead electric line (violation of 15-foot minimum for distribution)\n- Plant schedule does NOT indicate which trees are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F\n- Mature heights NOT documented on plans (cannot verify large tree requirement 40+ feet)\n- No clearance dimensions shown on landscape plan\n- No