{"level":30,"time":1776370337176,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QdRMtiEmJHsNYhG9pTjizD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cmte8ZoPJ5nUN6PsquA6Gh","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along overhead electric line (southeastern corner)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees are located 0-5 feet north of the overhead electric line along the southern property boundary. Plant schedule proposes Cedar Elm and Live Oak; neither species is designated as utility-compatible (UC) per ECM Appendix F. Minimum 15-foot clearance from non-utility-compatible tree trunks to distribution conductors is required; proposed trees fall short by 10-15 feet."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along overhead electric line (southeastern corner)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed Cedar Elm (10 trees) and Live Oak (2 trees) have typical mature heights of 40-50 feet, meeting the definition of large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F). Two such trees are located 0-5 feet from the overhead electric line on the southern boundary. Minimum 25-foot clearance for large trees from distribution conductors is required; proposed placement violates this requirement by 20-25 feet."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"not-veri