{"level":30,"time":1776370346360,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BwragQKU5oxmqPDtzAr4My","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the 48-hour notification requirement is NOT on the cover sheet. It's only mentioned in the Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3, but that's not the same as a clear general note on the cover sheet that all contractors would see. The requirement should be on the cover sheet per the checklist item EL-1.46.\n\nNow let me also check EL-1.22 more carefully - whether existing electric poles need to be relocated from driveway conflicts. Let me also make sure I understand which items truly don't apply vs. which are just not documented.\n\nLet me also reconsider EL-1.46 more carefully. The grouping description says the requirement note should include \"note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003)\". This is indeed on Sheet 3 in the Electric Transmission Notes, which IS part of the site plan, but it may not be prominent enough or specifically stated as a general note visible to contractors.\n\nActually, looking back at what I captured from the Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3, item #3 states:\n\"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512.505.7133 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.\"\n\nThis DOES address the 48-hour notification requirement, though it's in the transmission-specific notes rather than as a prominent general note. However, it does exist on the plans.\n\nI need to reconsider my evaluation. Let me think about whether this satisfies EL-1.46 or not:\n- The checklist item says \"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins\"\n- The Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3 DO include a note requiring a \"pre-construction safety meeting\" 48 hours before construction\n- This is technically a note on the plans, though not on the cover sheet\n\n\n- The requirement IS documented on Sheet 3, so marking this as a fail might be too harsh. I should consider NOT VERIFIABLE since the note exists but may not meet the prominence or placement standards Austin expects. This could be borderline depending on whether the requirement specifically mandates cover sheet placement.\n\nNow I'll compile my final findings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5960,"cache_read_input_tokens":77176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5960},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4842cd33-4ac7-488e-aa08-33032c2696e2","uuid":"a3514dde-dac7-44d9-8d79-2a4fc33b98ed"}
