es (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F). Landscape plan (Sheet 31) uses symbols (M, SY, PL, P) but does not differentiate or label which proposed trees will reach 40+ feet at maturity. Mature height information must be added to allow verification of large tree clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary within 15 feet of overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"e1c5768d-263b-4500-98ff-f6723ae5876c","label":"Project Review Form"},{"documentId":"ca29fbe6-6361-4580-848e-7807ae462499","label":"Master Comment Report"}],"comment":"Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees are proposed 0-5 feet from the overhead electric line, within the prohibited clearance zone. No documented written approval from Austin Energy is provided in the application materials (Project Review Form, Master Comment Report, or supplementary documents) authorizing placement of trees in these prohibited zones. Obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy or relocate trees to comply with minimum clearance distances."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3248,"cache_read_input_tokens":69326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3248},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df64853a-4f90-499d-b38e-749986aed001","uuid":"4b123da1-c35d-4494-addc-e5d7dee01426"}
