{"level":30,"time":1776370372342,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_018zXwCm3H5WNEEUxh88TeYo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have completed the comprehensive review of Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI identified **six deficiencies** across the 15 checklist items in this grouping:\n\n### **FAILURES (requiring correction):**\n\n1. **EL-2.1** - Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) proposed 0-5 feet from overhead distribution line, violating 15-foot minimum clearance\n2. **EL-2.3** - Large trees (40+ ft mature height) proposed 0-5 feet from distribution line, violating 25-foot minimum clearance  \n3. **EL-2.15** - Trees proposed in prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval\n\n### **NOT-VERIFIABLE (requiring clarification):**\n\n4. **EL-2.6** - Utility poles not clearly marked on landscape plan; cannot verify 10-foot pole clearances\n5. **EL-2.10** - Tree species not identified on landscape plan near utilities; cross-reference required to plant schedule\n6. **EL-2.11** - Mature heights not provided on plant schedule; cannot verify which trees are \"large\" (40+ feet)\n\n### **Items Determined Not Applicable:**\n- EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5 (transmission-only requirements; no transmission infrastructure present)\n- EL-2.7 (pad-mounted equipment not shown)\n- EL-2.12, EL-2.13 (no clearance dimensions present on plans)\n\n### **Compliant:**\n- **EL-2.14** (Trees ARE shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities)\n\nThe most critical issue is that mitigation trees on the southern property boundary are positioned only 0-5 feet from the overhead electric line, creating significant clearance violations with large tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak). These violations must be resolved either by relocating the trees or obtaining documented Austin Energy approval before plan approval can be issued."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3282,"cache_read_input_tokens":72574,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3282},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df64853a-4f90-499d-b38e-749986aed001","uuid":"b40d6f1a-eda7-4de3-825d-f50b7996d234"}
{"level":30,"time":1776370372348,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1730871,"duration_api_ms":235941,"num_turns":26,"result":"Perfect! I have completed the comprehensive review of Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI identified **six deficiencies** across the 15 checklist items in this grouping:\n\n### **FAILURES (requiring correction):**\n\n1. **EL-2.1** - Non-utility-compatible trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) proposed 0-5 feet from overhead distribution line, violating 15-foot minimum clearance\n2. **EL-2.3** - Large trees (40+ ft mature height) proposed 0-5 feet from distribution line, violating 25-foot minimum clearance  \n3. **EL-2.15** - Trees proposed in prohibited clearance zones without documented Austin Energy written approval\n\n### **NOT-VERIFIABLE (requiring clarification):**\n\n4. **EL-2.6** - Utility poles not clearly marked on landscape plan; cannot verify 10-foot pole clearances\n5. **EL-2.10** - Tree species not identified on landscape plan near utilities; cross-reference required to plant schedule\n6. **EL-2.11** - Mature heights not provided on plant schedule; cannot verify which trees are \"large\" (40+ feet)\n\n### **Items Determined Not Applicable:**\n- EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5 (transmission-only requirements; no transmission infrastructure present)\n- EL-2.7 (pad-mounted equipment not shown)\n- EL-2.12, EL-2.13 (no clearance dimensions present on plans)\n\n### **Compliant:**\n- **EL-2.14** (Trees ARE shown on landscape plan in relation to overhead electric facilities)\n\nThe most critical issue is that mitigation trees on the southern property boundary are positioned only 0-5 feet from the overhead electric line, creating significant clearance violations with large tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak). These violations must be resolved either by relocating the trees or obtaining documented Austin Energy approval before plan approval can be issued.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"df64853a-4f90-499d-b38e-749986aed001","total_cost_usd":0.41037309999999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78687,"cache_read_input_tokens":1219342,"output_tokens":15805,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78687,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":220,"outputTokens":20634,"cacheReadInputTokens":1313831,"cacheCreationInputTokens":140480,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.41037309999999994,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along overhead electric line (southeastern corner)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Mitigation trees are located 0-5 feet north of the overhead electric line along the southern property boundary. Plant schedule proposes Cedar Elm and Live Oak; neither species is designated as utility-compatible (UC) per ECM Appendix F. Minimum 15-foot clearance from non-utility-compatible tree trunks to distribution conductors is required; proposed trees fall short by 10-15 feet."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary along overhead electric line (southeastern corner)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed Cedar Elm (10 trees) and Live Oak (2 trees) have typical mature heights of 40-50 feet, meeting the definition of large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F). Two such trees are located 0-5 feet from the overhead electric line on the southern boundary. Minimum 25-foot clearance for large trees from distribution conductors is required; proposed placement violates this requirement by 20-25 feet."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Overhead electric infrastructure area (poles not clearly marked)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows overhead electric (OHE) line along southern property boundary but utility poles are not clearly marked or designated on the sheet. Without pole locations, compliance with the 10-foot clearance requirement from tree trunks to poles cannot be verified. Indicate utility pole locations on the landscape plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan identifying trees near overhead electric facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows tree symbols (circles with designations M, SY, PL, P for mitigation, street yard, parking lot, and buffer trees) but does not label specific species on the landscape plan drawing. Mitigation trees (M) near the overhead electric line cannot be confirmed to specific species from the landscape plan alone; species identification requires cross-reference to plant schedule. A legend or label on the landscape plan identifying the species of trees near utilities would improve verifiability."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Proposed shade trees and ornamental trees on landscape and grading plans"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plant schedule (Sheet 35) lists proposed trees with installation sizes (e.g., 4-inch caliper, 16-foot height at planting) but does NOT provide mature height specifications required to identify large trees (40+ feet per ECM Appendix F). Landscape plan (Sheet 31) uses symbols (M, SY, PL, P) but does not differentiate or label which proposed trees will reach 40+ feet at maturity. Mature height information must be added to allow verification of large tree clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary within 15 feet of overhead electric distribution line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[{"documentId":"e1c5768d-263b-4500-98ff-f6723ae5876c","label":"Project Review Form"},{"documentId":"ca29fbe6-6361-4580-848e-7807ae462499","label":"Master Comment Report"}],"comment":"Cedar Elm and Live Oak trees are proposed 0-5 feet from the overhead electric line, within the prohibited clearance zone. No documented written approval from Austin Energy is provided in the application materials (Project Review Form, Master Comment Report, or supplementary documents) authorizing placement of trees in these prohibited zones. Obtain explicit written approval from Austin Energy or relocate trees to comply with minimum clearance distances."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"cff60415-a524-48f2-b0b6-b9b8de8fd9fa"}
