le","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and site features in areas crossed by transmission lines (based on transmission easement references on Sheet 3)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission lines noted on Sheet 3 and referenced in transmission easement notes, but no grading plan sections or elevation data show vertical clearance from finished grade to lowest transmission conductor. Required 30-foot minimum vertical clearance for roads/driveways beneath transmission lines cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["All site features near overhead lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No clearance dimensions are provided on the site plan from any features to overhead electric lines. Therefore, measurement methodology (whether from outside conductor vs. pole centerline) cannot be assessed. Per UCM § 1.10.3 and measurement methodology requirements, dimensions must originate from the outside conductor location, not pole center."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Sidewalk alignment along Valley View Road right-of-way where utility poles exist at property corners"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":22}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sidewalks shown on site plan and detail sheets, and utility poles are depicted at property boundaries along right-of-way, but dimension callouts showing clear spacing between sidewalk construction and existing power poles are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.28","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3","UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["Water meter location shown in northwest corner near utility cluster"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water meter location identified on utility plans but clearance dimension from the outside conductor of overhead electric service lines is not annotated. Required 7.5-foot minimum horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified from available documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.29","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Water utility lines routing across site near overhead electric distribution facilities"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":19},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Water lines shown on utility plans routing across site where overhead electric facilities exist, but clearance dimensions from water lines to overhead conductors are not provided. Minimum clearance separation cannot be verified from plan documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["Driveways and accessible paths in areas with transmission structures and down guy anchors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transmission lines and transmission easement noted on Sheet 3; overhead line poles depicted on site plan. Electric Transmission Notes (Sheet 3, Item 2) reference 'down guy anchors' in restriction zone but specific down guy anchor locations and conflicts with proposed driveways are not documented. Whether down guy wires conflict with accessible paths or need relocation/conversion to self-supporting poles cannot be determined from available plans."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Pad-mounted transformers shown on electrical design plan near proposed buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed pad-mounted electrical transformers shown on preliminary electrical design plan, but no section view providing vertical clearance dimension from top of transformer equipment to lowest overhead electric line is provided. Compliance with 7.5-foot minimum sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.45","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Construction staging area; equipment operation zones; crane swing radius during construction"],"sheetReferences":[],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No construction logistics plan, staging area diagram, or crane swing plan provided on site plan set. Required 10-foot radial clearance from energized overhead lines during construction and material staging cannot be verified. OSHA working clearance compliance cannot be documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site; all construction activities near overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3 include a requirement for 'pre-construction safety meeting...48 hours before commencement of construction' with Austin Energy; however, this requirement appears only in transmission-specific notes, not as a prominent general note visible to all contractors on the cover sheet or general notes section. Clear