{"level":30,"time":1776370398252,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011YgfTQ6pmuguy9V8S8MCCY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I've completed the comprehensive review of grouping EL-1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\nLet me summarize what I found:\n\n**TOTAL CHECKLIST ITEMS: 47**\n\n**FAIL (5 items):**\n1. EL-1.7 - No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor locations\n2. EL-1.8 - No section/plan exhibits with clearance dimensions from conductor\n3. EL-1.17 - Retaining wall sections lack overhead conductor elevation data\n4. EL-1.31 - No surveyor mid-span clearance data provided\n5. EL-1.37 - Trees lack clearance verification and species identification\n\n**NOT VERIFIABLE (17 items):**\n1. EL-1.1 - Building clearances not dimensioned\n2. EL-1.2 - Facility radial clearances not dimensioned\n3. EL-1.9 - Fence sky-to-ground clearances not dimensioned\n4. EL-1.10 - Fence post clearances from poles not dimensioned\n5. EL-1.12 - Transmission fence material and grounding not specified\n6. EL-1.14 - Retaining wall clearances not dimensioned\n7. EL-1.18 - Driveway vertical clearances not dimensioned\n8. EL-1.19 - Parking vertical clearances not dimensioned\n9. EL-1.20 - Transmission vertical clearance not dimensioned\n10. EL-1.23 - Clearance measurement methodology cannot be assessed\n11. EL-1.25 - Sidewalk/pole clearances not dimensioned\n12. EL-1.28 - Water meter clearances not dimensioned\n13. EL-1.29 - Water line clearances not dimensioned\n\n\n14. EL-1.40 - Down guy conflicts not documented\n15. EL-1.43 - Transformer vertical clearances not dimensioned\n16. EL-1.45 - Construction staging clearances not addressed\n17. EL-1.46 - 48-hour notification note not prominently placed\n\n**N/A or PASS ITEMS (25 items):** The remaining items either don't apply to this project—such as building projections, gas pump canopies, elevated walkways, and adequate ROW setbacks—or have been adequately addressed in the submitted documentation. ee signs proposed. Several additional items lack clarity: decorative light fixture positions aren't marked, streetlight locations are missing, guy easement boundaries and down guy anchor easements remain undocumented, and no roof service masts are shown. The fundamental problem is that while the site plan identifies the overhead lines and general facility positions, it's missing the detailed clearance documentation—dimensions, surveyed elevations, cross-sections, and vegetation details—necessary to confirm compliance with Austin's requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5684,"cache_read_input_tokens":83136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5684},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4842cd33-4ac7-488e-aa08-33032c2696e2","uuid":"3ff2da79-c2fa-4fbd-a7bd-028a237f36f4"}
{"level":30,"time":1776370401048,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011YgfTQ6pmuguy9V8S8MCCY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive review of Grouping EL-1 (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) and returned the findings via structured output.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Grouping Context:** This grouping covers clearance requirements between existing overhead electric distribution and transmission facilities and all proposed site features (buildings, fences, driveways, utilities, landscaping, etc.).\n\n**Applicability:** ✓ **APPLICABLE** - The site plan clearly shows existing overhead electric lines (OHE) on and adjacent to the property, running along all four property boundaries and crossing over proposed driveways and parking areas. The site includes transmission easements and facilities as noted in the Electric Transmission Notes on Sheet 3.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n**5 FAIL Items** - Missing critical required documentation:\n- **EL-1.7:** No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor locations\n- **EL-1.8:** No section/plan exhibits with clearance dimensions from outside conductor  \n- **EL-1.17:** Retaining wall sections lack overhead conductor elevation data\n- **EL-1.31:** No surveyor's mid-span clearance survey data\n- **EL-1.37:** Existing and proposed trees near overhead lines lack species verification and clearance dimensions\n\n**17 NOT VERIFIABLE Items** - Clearances cannot be confirmed because required dimensions are not provided on plans despite site features being in proximity to overhead lines (buildings, driveways, parking, fences, walls, utilities, water lines, down guy conflicts, transformers, and construction staging areas).\n\n**Core Deficiency:** The site plan depicts overhead electric lines and identifies proposed site improvements near those lines, but provides **no dimension callouts, section views, or elevation data** showing clearances from the outside conductor to any site features. The 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground, 15-foot radial, and 16-18 foot vertical clearances required by UCM § 1.10.3 cannot be verified. Additionally, no registered surveyor's pole location and mid-span clearance data is provided as required by the code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5684,"cache_read_input_tokens":83136,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5684},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4842cd33-4ac7-488e-aa08-33032c2696e2","uuid":"f4babef1-09ff-466b-85d5-7c95b2df355b"}
