{"level":30,"time":1776370412489,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":1,"prompt":"Examine the cover sheet and identify: 1) Any project notes or general requirements listed; 2) Specifically look for any notes about notifying Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines; 3) Check for any references to safety requirements or utility coordination; 4) List all notes or disclaimers that relate to electric utilities or overhead lines. Report whether the required 48-hour notification note is present on this cover sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan cover sheet, here are the detailed findings regarding your requested items:\n\n**1) Project notes or general requirements listed:**\nThe cover sheet contains numerous project notes and general requirements organized primarily in lists on the left and right columns. \n\n*Notes on the Left Column (verbatim excerpts):*\n*   **Watershed:** \"This project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed (Urban). All storm flows from this site will be directed to the West Bouldin Creek Watershed...\"\n*   **Environmental Controls:** \"All temporary spoils and equipment storage areas shall have silt fence placed along the perimeter of the downslope side. Additional erosion/sedimentation controls may be required...\"\n*   **Water Quality:** \"All detention basins, water quality ponds and appurtenances which receive stormwater runoff from commercial or multi-family development shall be maintained by the record owner...\"\n*   **EPA Forms:** \"Contractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for all projects involving 5 acres or more of disturbed area...\"\n*   **Edwards Aquifer Note:** \"This project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer Contributing Zone.\"\n*   **Commercial Design Standards:** \"This site plan is subject to Subchapter E of the Land Development Code...\"\n*   **Potable Water:** \"All potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, shall be essentially 'lead free'...\"\n*   **City Approval Disclaimer:** \"Approval of these plans by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only...\"\n*   **Water and Wastewater Utility:** \"City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060. This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin Fire Code...\"\n*   **Recycling Ordinance:** \"Compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory...\"\n*   **Pest Management:** \"For Integrated Pest Management Plan, see agreement filed in document No. ____________, Official Public Records, Travis County, Texas.\"\n*   **Street Impact Fee:** \"Development of structures that require a building permit within this Site Plan, or revisions thereof, are required to comply with the City of Austin Street Impact Fee Ordinances...\"\n*   **DCM Waiver Note:** \"On 01/21/2026 this project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department of a waiver to Section 1.2.4.E.1.a.i of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\"\n\n*Notes on the Right Column (verbatim excerpts):*\n*   **Engineer Responsibility:** \"All responsibility for the adequacy of these plans remains with the Engineer who prepared them...\"\n*   **Survey Disclaimer:** \"Bleyl Engineering and its associates will not be held responsible for the accuracy of the survey or for design errors or omissions resulting from survey inaccuracies.\"\n*   **Application Release:** \"Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant...\"\n*   **Engineer Certification:** \"A civil engineer registered in Texas must certify a plan or plat as complete, accurate, and in compliance...\"\n*   **Parkland Dedication:** \"A fee-in-lieu of parkland dedication must be paid for 39 residential units prior to the issuance of the Certificate of Occupancy.\"\n*   **UST Discovery:** \"If at any time during construction of this project an underground storage tank (UST) is found, construction in that area must stop until a City of Austin UST Construction Permit is applied for and approved...\"\n*   **Traffic Control Plan Note:** \"This note is being placed on the plan set in the absence of a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) with the full understanding that an engineered TCP shall be reviewed and approved by the Right of Way Management Division...\"\n\n**2) Notes about notifying Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines:**\nAfter closely inspecting all text on the document, there are **no** notes present on this cover sheet that mention notifying Austin Energy before working near high-voltage lines.\n\n**3) References to safety requirements or utility coordination:**\n*   **Safety Requirements:** \n    *   There is a large \"Austin Fire Department\" table detailing safety codes including \"Fire Design Codes\" (2021 International Fire Code Edition), \"Fire Flow Demand\", \"Building Fire Area (s.f.)\", and \"Automatic Fire Sprinkler System Type\". \n    *   The \"Traffic Control Plan Note\" outlines safety requirements for blocking the right-of-way, noting that \"a TCP must be submitted... for review a minimum of 6 weeks prior to the start of construction.\"\n    *   The underground storage tank (UST) note details safety and environmental protocol if a tank is discovered: \"construction in that area must stop... Any UST removal work must be conducted by a UST Contractor that is registered with the Texas Commission on Environmental Quality (TCEQ).\"\n*   **Utility Coordination:** \n    *   Coordination regarding private hydrants is directed to the \"City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\". \n    *   *Note:* The Sheet List Table references a \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" on Sheet 21, indicating electric utility coordination exists within the plan set, but there are no specific electrical coordination instructions on this cover sheet.\n\n**4) Notes or disclaimers that relate to electric utilities or overhead lines:**\nThere are **no** notes, disclaimers, or references to electric utilities, Austin Energy, or overhead lines anywhere on this cover sheet.\n\n**5) Required 48-hour notification note:**\nThe required 48-hour notification note for Austin Energy (typically required for utility coordination or excavation near lines) is **NOT** present on this cover sheet.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1401,"outputTokens":1238,"totalTokens":4906,"reasoningTokens":2267},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2370268]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nRep