the issuance of the Certificate of Occupancy.\"\n*   **UST Discovery:** \"If at any time during construction of this project an underground storage tank (UST) is found, construction in that area must stop until a City of Austin UST Construction Permit is applied for and approved...\"\n*   **Traffic Control Plan Note:** \"This note is being placed on the plan set in the absence of a temporary traffic control plan (TCP) with the full understanding that an engineered TCP shall be reviewed and approved by the Right of Way Management Division...\"\n\n**2) Notes about notifying Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines:**\nAfter closely inspecting all text on the document, there are **no** notes present on this cover sheet that mention notifying Austin Energy before working near high-voltage lines.\n\n**3) References to safety requirements or utility coordination:**\n*   **Safety Requirements:** \n    *   There is a large \"Austin Fire Department\" table detailing safety codes including \"Fire Design Codes\" (2021 International Fire Code Edition), \"Fire Flow Demand\", \"Building Fire Area (s.f.)\", and \"Automatic Fire Sprinkler System Type\". \n    *   The \"Traffic Control Plan Note\" outlines safety requirements for blocking the right-of-way, noting that \"a TCP must be submitted... for review a minimum of 6 weeks prior to the start of construction.\"\n    *   The underground storage tank (UST) note details safety and environmental protocol if a tank is discovered: \"construction in that area must stop... Any UST removal work must be conducted by a UST Contractor that is registered with the Texas Commission on Environmental Quality (TCEQ).\"\n*   **Utility Coordination:** \n    *   Coordination regarding private hydrants is directed to the \"City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\". \n    *   *Note:* The Sheet List Table references a \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" on Sheet 21, indicating electric utility coordination exists within the plan set, but there are no specific electrical coordination instructions on this cover sheet.\n\n**4) Notes or disclaimers that relate to electric utilities or overhead lines:**\nThere are **no** notes, disclaimers, or references to electric utilities, Austin Energy, or overhead lines anywhere on this cover sheet.\n\n**5) Required 48-hour notification note:**\nThe required 48-hour notification note for Austin Energy (typically required for utility coordination or excavation near lines) is **NOT** present on this cover sheet."}]}
{"level":30,"time":1776370429434,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AtHWEV77eZMdaCLTzVakCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent. The vision analysis of Sheet 1 (Cover Sheet) confirms:\n- **NO notes about notifying Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines**\n- **NO references to electric utility safety or coordination**\n- **The required 48-hour notification note is NOT present**\n\nHowever, I recall from Sheet 3 Block 14 and Block 20 that there WERE notes about Austin Energy requirements and 48-hour notification. Let me verify whether those notes constitute the required notice on the cover sheet. Looking back at my earlier reading:\n\n**From Sheet 3 Block 14:**\n\"The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required... owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electrical facilities designed to provide electric service to this project...\"\n\n**From Sheet 3 Block 20 (Transmission Notes):**\nNote 3 states: \"A pre-construction safety meeting is required with Austin Energy 48 hours before commencement of construction. Call Andrew Perez at 512-505-7153 to schedule a tailgate safety meeting.\"\n\nSo the 48-hour notification requirement IS on Sheet 3, but the grouping item EL-1.46 specifies: \"Plans must include note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003)\"\n\nThe note needs to be about working near high-voltage overhead lines in general (for worker safety), not just transmission lines. The Sheet 3 Block 20 note is specific to transmission structures. Block 14 also mentions overhead electrical facilities.\n\nActually, wait. Let me re-read EL-1.46 more carefully:\n\n\"Plans do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines\"\n\n\nThe requirement calls for a general safety note covering all high-voltage overhead work per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. While Sheet 3 Block 20 addresses the 48-hour requirement for transmission line safety meetings specifically, and Block 14 references overhead electrical facilities, the plans lack a comprehensive note addressing notification for any work near high-voltage lines. Given that the site has both distribution and transmission overhead lines, a prominent general notification requirement should be included.\n\nNow I'm compiling my complete findings across all checklist items. The site has substantial electrical infrastructure—overhead lines border three sides (South, East, West) with utility poles and guy wires visible, plus electrical easements ranging from 5' to 15'. Underground electric lines also route through the site with transformers, meters, and pull boxes at multiple locations. There's a transformer pad west of Building 2, and while transmission lines aren't shown directly on-site, transmission easement references appear in Block 20. The underground lines cross under driveways without adequate clearance documentation.\n\nHowever, critical gaps emerge immediately: no clearance dimensions are annotated anywhere for buildings to overhead lines, driveway/parking grades to overhead lines, retaining walls to overhead lines, or underground utilities to driveways. The mitigation trees on Sheet 31 are positioned directly adjacent to the OHE line on the south boundary—species like Live Oak and Cedar Elm aren't utility-compatible and lack any clearance dimensions or utility compatibility notes. Building elevations showing vertical clearances from overhead lines are missing entirely, as are sections that would document clearances from overhead lines to driveways, parking areas, and other site features.\n\nAdditionally, the cover sheet is missing the required 48-hour Austin Energy notification note for work near high-voltage lines, though Sheet 3 Block 20 does contain a transmission line-specific note. A registered surveyor proximity survey showing pole locations and mid-span clearances hasn't been provided, and some dimension lines appear to measure to the property line rather than to the actual conductor.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2413,"cache_read_input_tokens":70805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2413},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbcfd4d1-5bca-4c8e-97ca-aab614fb6d42","uuid":"9f610d62-f86e-4e5a-96e4-7fa835599c2a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776370432460,"pid":59252,"hostname":"Williams-MacBook-Pro.local","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01AtHWEV77eZMdaCLTzVakCT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me now compile my research into a comprehensive evaluation. I have gathered extensive evidence about the overhead electric infrastructure and clearance deficiencies. Let me systematically evaluate each checklist item based on my findings:\n\n## RESEARCH PHASE SUMMARY\n\n**Evidence Found:**\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Confirmed:**\n- OHE lines along South, East, West property boundaries (Sheet 9, 21, 31)\n- Utility poles with guy wire at SW corner (Sheet 9, 21)\n- Electrical easements: 15' South, 5' East, others perimeter\n- Transmission easement with detailed restrictions (Sheet 3 Block 20)\n- Transformer Pad west of Bldg 2\n\n**Underground Electric Infrastructure:**\n- Underground lines routing through site under driveways (Sheet 21)\n- 2 Transformer Pads (west and east locations)\n- Meters at each building exterior\n- Pull boxes along routing\n- NO clearance dimensions from underground lines to driveways\n\n**Critical Gaps / NOT FOUND:**\n- Building elevation sheets showing vertical clearances\n- Section/profile views showing clearances from overhead lines to buildings, driveways, parking\n- Clearance dimension annotations on any sheet (site plan, electrical design, grading, wall plans)\n- Proximity survey by registered surveyor with pole locations and mid-span clearances\n- Utility compatibility verification for proposed trees near overhead lines\n- General 48-hour Austin Energy notification note on cover sheet\n- Tree species identification with UC compatibility status for mitigation trees placed near OHE lines\n\n**Trees Near Overhead Lines (Sheet 31):**\n- Mitigation trees (\"M\") directly adjacent to OHE line on southern boundary\n- Proposed species: Live Oak, Cedar Elm (both large-mature trees, NOT utility-compatible)\n- No clearance dimensions shown\n- No UC (utility-compatible) designation on any sheets\n\n---\n\nNow I'll evaluate each checklist item using PASS, FAIL, NOT-VERIFIABLE, or N/A logic, then output only the FAIL and NOT-VERIFIABLE items:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2413,"cache_read_input_tokens":70805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2413},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbcfd4d1-5bca-4c8e-97ca-aab614fb6d42","uuid":"6de2f2e4-c2b2-441c-b031-df5ec9b6a854"}
