 EL-1.15 - Retaining walls near substation - N/A (no substation mentioned)\n- EL-1.16 - Emergency access structures - N/A (none proposed)\n- EL-1.19 - Vehicles on concrete pads under overhead lines - N/A (no vehicle display pads shown)\n- EL-1.20 - Road grades under transmission - Possibly applicable due to transmission easement, need to check\n- EL-1.21 - Highway/freeway grades with distribution - N/A (not highways)\n- EL-1.22 - Existing electric poles in conflict with driveways - Possibly applicable if poles are shown as conflicting\n- EL-1.23 - Clearance dimensions from pole instead of conductor - Could be applicable since no clearance dimensions are shown at all\n- EL-1.24 - Streetlight poles under overhead lines - N/A (no streetlights proposed on site that I can see)\n- EL-1.25 - Sidewal ks not cleared from power poles - Possibly applicable\n- EL-1.26 - Trash enclosures under overhead lines - N/A (not shown in overhead line area)\n- EL-1.28 - Water meters under service drops - Possibly applicable\n- EL-1.29 - Water lines near overhead distribution - Possibly applicable if shown\n- EL-1.30 - Foundations within 5 feet of property line - May be applicable\n- EL-1.32 - Overhead line crossings not at 90 degrees - N/A (not new overhead lines being installed)\n- EL-1.33 - Secondary over primary - N/A (not applicable)\n- EL-1.34 - Marquee signs - N/A (none proposed)\n- EL-1.35 - New power poles spacing - N/A (no new poles for underground conversion shown)\n- EL-1.36 - Decorative lighting under overhead lines - Possibly applicable if shown\n- EL-1.38 - Meter obstructions - Possibly applicable\n- EL-1.39 - Development near streetlights - N/A\n- EL-1.40 - Down guy wires conflicting - Possibly applicable if guy wires are shown\n- EL-1.41 - Guy easements - Possibly applicable\n- EL-1.42 - Down guy anchor easements - Possibly applicable\n- EL-1.43 - Transformers vertical clearance - Possibly applicable\n- EL-1.44 - Transformers in niche - N/A (not in niche)\n- EL-1.45 - Construction staging clearance - May be applicable but hard to determine from static plan\n- EL-1.47 - Service mast through roof - N/A (not shown)\n\nI need to reconsider a few items more carefully. Looking at **EL-1.7** specifically - surveyed elevations and overhead conductor locations on building elevation sheets. There are no building elevation sheets provided at all. This creates ambiguity: the requirement could be N/A if interpreted as conditional on elevation sheets existing, or it could be a FAIL since the required sheets are missing. The checklist language suggests it's checking whether existing elevation sheets contain this information, not mandating that elevation sheets must exist.\n\nHowever, since buildings are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities, the applicability condition is met. The absence of elevation sheets showing surveyed elevations and conductor locations represents a deficiency - I should flag EL-1.7.\n\nFor **EL-1.23**, the requirement checks whether clearance dimensions are measured from the correct reference point (utility pole or conductor centerline). Since no clearances are shown in the drawings at all, this becomes conditional - the item only applies if clearance dimensions actually exist to evaluate. The few dimensions that do appear would need checking against this standard.\n\nRegarding **EL-1.40**, the vision reports reference a guy wire near the southwest corner. I need to determine if this conflicts with proposed accessible paths or driveways shown on the site plans.\n\nThe applicability criteria requires an actual conflict between the down guy and proposed features. The guy wire appears to be at the SW corner near Building 8, which is outside most developed areas, so a conflict seems unlikely but I should verify this more carefully.\n\nI'm confident I've identified the main deficiencies. Let me confirm my list of 11 items is complete: EL-1.1, EL-1.2, EL-1.3, EL-1.8, EL-1.14, and several others all marked as not-verifiable based on missing clearance dimensions and overhead electric facility information on the plans.\n\nI should also flag EL-1.7 regarding surveyed elevations and overhead conductor locations on building elevation sheets. Since buildings are proposed within potential clearance distance of overhead facilities, those sheets are required but completely absent from the submission. Without them, I can't verify compliance, so this is not-verifiable. I'll add this to my findings.\n\nEL-1.25 about sidewalk clearances from existing power poles also warrants examination, particularly along the property edges where poles are located. Checking the driveway layout against pole positions—the driveways appear to be interior to the site, so boundary poles shouldn't create conflicts. I'd need to confirm whether any poles are positioned within the driveway paths themselves, but based on what's visible, this seems not applicable.\n\nGiven the analysis so far, EL-1.7 stands out as the clearest deficiency since it requires a specific deliverable that's absent from the submission.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4647,"cache_read_input_tokens":73218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4647},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbcfd4d1-5bca-4c8e-97ca-aab614fb6d42","uuid":"d0ebcfba-f47e-4c0c-9d8f-5ab18005c559"}
