iveways and parking areas where overhead electric lines traverse or are adjacent"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading plan and electrical design plan show driveway and parking grades and overhead electric lines, but no vertical clearance dimensions are provided from lowest overhead electric facility (including any telecommunications attachments) to finished driveway/parking grades. Finished grades shown but no surveyor mid-span clearance verification provided. Cannot verify 16-foot (parking without trucks) or 18-foot (with truck traffic) minimum vertical clearance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Biofiltration/detention pond in NE portion of site and associated retaining walls within electric easement zones"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":15}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows biofiltration/detention pond in northeast corner of site where multiple easements exist, including electric easements. Sheet 3 Block 20 note 16 prohibits detention ponds which would impair Austin Energy's access to transmission easements. No clearance dimensions from pond or pond retaining walls to overhead electric facilities or easement boundaries are provided to verify 7.5-foot clearance from outside conductor to pond structures."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site where vertical clearance from overhead facilities to proposed site features (driveways, parking, buildings) appears potentially marginal"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa77